docs/vision-v3/r1-concepts/C3-swarm-codex.md:185:5. **Capability-gap recruitment:** unknown work creates tested skills and hybrid expertise on demand.
docs/vision-v3/r1-concepts/J2-judge-codex.md:3:**Carry C3 forward as the execution spine, with C2 providing strategic continuity and C4 governing experimental learning.** Graft C1’s economic comparisons and C5’s reusable assets and artifact review.
docs/vision-v3/r1-concepts/J2-judge-codex.md:14:| **C4 — Lab** | **9** — Venture and organisational experiments preserve ambition; long commitments fit less naturally. | **8** — Evidence improves decision altitude; numerous bets and appeals threaten attention. | **9** — Uncertainty maps find consequential questions and expose necessary judgment calls. | **7** — Cheap tests accelerate rejection; scarce traffic and delayed outcomes constrain validation. | **7** — Interference controls protect experiments; durable operations and outages need fuller design. | **9** — Preregistration, null results and controlled comparisons provide the strongest learning discipline. | **49** |
docs/vision-v3/r1-concepts/J2-judge-codex.md:33:**C4 — strongest: preregistered experiments settled against authoritative outcomes.** Fixed criteria, preserved null results and controlled organisational trials make learning falsifiable.
docs/vision-v3/r1-concepts/J2-judge-codex.md:35:**Dangerous flaw: an evidence timetable mistaken for business reality.** Delayed retention can kill sound theses prematurely. Distinguish disproved, underpowered and not-yet-observable bets. Expiry must preserve customer obligations.
docs/vision-v3/r1-concepts/J2-judge-codex.md:49:| **C4: learning** | Uncertainty map, preregistration, interference graph, null results, configuration trials | Test consequential unknowns without turning every operational task into an experiment. |
docs/vision-v3/r1-concepts/J2-judge-codex.md:62:6. **Cross-family review versus provider availability.** Both families remain equal. Require independent evidence and permissions. During outages, continue verifiable authorised work; queue effects missing required checks.
docs/vision-v3/r1-concepts/J2-judge-codex.md:72:2. **Missing-evidence audits.** Independently sample abandoned checkouts, silent customers and unreported failed missions. Record collection coverage beside outcomes. An authoritative database can still describe a biased slice of reality.
docs/vision-v3/r1-concepts/J2-judge-codex.md:73:3. **Complementary-investment funding.** Evaluate bundles whose parts have little standalone value: instrumentation, distribution and an offer, for example. Fund dependency milestones against the bundle’s outcome. Isolated contract and experiment rankings can reject every necessary prerequisite.
docs/vision-v3/r1-concepts/J2-judge-codex.md:75:5. **Transferable operating-company packages.** Export authority, assets, obligations, data permissions and operating evidence into a handover rehearsal with a different operator. Measure undocumented founder dependence. Make creating, acquiring and transferring businesses a tested capability.
docs/vision-v3/r1-concepts/J2-judge-codex.md:77:## 5. Evidence checks against Round 0
docs/vision-v3/r1-concepts/J2-judge-codex.md:81:- **C1: market authority exceeds the evidence.** R0-D §1 reports losses for all six Prediction Arena trading models. This does not disprove internal markets; it leaves their allocation quality unproven. Require calibration before market-driven freezes.
docs/vision-v3/r1-concepts/J2-judge-codex.md:86:- **All five: autonomy and improvement remain hypotheses.** R0-E §§2–3 supports bounded skill transfer and external feedback, not indefinite organisational improvement or simulated purchasing validity. C3/C4 preserve these distinctions most explicitly. R0-D does not establish durable profitability with negligible intervention; illustrative days and founder-minute totals remain design targets.
docs/vision-v3/r1-concepts/C5-studio.md:32:4. **The ladder replaces the plan.** Inside a tranche the **Director** (single-threaded lead) picks the method. The ladder fixes only the evidence ("footage") that buys the next tranche:
docs/vision-v3/r1-concepts/C5-studio.md:53:- **Hybrid crafts.** A craft registry holds fused roles (Pricing-Psychologist-Engineer, Regulatory-Copywriter, Support-Refund-Accountant). Each survives only while it beats the classic split crew on accepted outcome per dollar.
docs/vision-v3/r1-concepts/C5-studio.md:57:- **Call sheet.** The 1st AD agent writes one per production per day: who is called, which sets and paths each person holds, the scene, the done-evidence, and the wrap time.
docs/vision-v3/r1-concepts/C5-studio.md:65:- **Backlot.** Each reusable asset is a set record: `{kind, version, provenance, productions_used[], reuse_count, last_used, known_faults[]}`. Kinds: code starters, payment stacks, brand kits, outreach sequences, eval scenarios, audience segments. **Striking at wrap is mandatory**: improvements come back as diffs. A set unused for 90 days is archived, and a set with rising faults is condemned. Target: **≥40% backlot reuse in T1 footage by week 12.**
docs/vision-v3/r1-concepts/C5-studio.md:95:- **Unknown work:** the ladder fixes the evidence required, not the method.
