docs/vision-system/planning/specification/07-integrations-capacity.md:119:**DESIGN PROPOSAL.** The priced reference is OP-AWS-LINUX-1: A in eu-central-1, R/G in independent account eu-west-1, N and X ephemeral in eu-central-1. Four steady execution VM placements retain five logical boundaries; a disposable trusted R restore VM is additionally budgeted during recovery exercises. Software G co-locates with R; there is no AWS NAT Gateway, managed Kubernetes, Redis, hosted queue, RDS, managed identity or managed signing service. Pg hot standby and the separate writable witness cluster share R; load and correlated loss are explicit. Independent account/admin/billing/MFA/recovery custody remains an actual human prerequisite. AWS's common provider root is outside the independence claim. **ASSUMPTION:** Compute sizes are workload estimates, not benchmark results.
