field-level ownership half IS checked -- A POSITIVE CONTROL IS OWNED BY THE PARTY IT CONTROLS and A DECLARED CONTROL FIELD IS NOT READ BY THE GUARD THAT DECLARES IT in validate_contracts.py, over pinned-conjuncts.json#/producer_unauthorable_fields, with fixtures r35. What the review ASKED FOR is the rebinding of three guard BODIES to a record the producer cannot author, through IdentityBinding or `current_owner`; that needs a ref field and a phase no chapter fixes, and inventing them would be specification by side effect. A row moves to answered_elsewhere when the check answers the finding, not when it answers part of it. Residue and the two owed chapter sentences are in F2/07-repair-names-contract.md.","F6D-10":"No file-and-check pair is recorded here for it. Classified conservatively by F6R-01: the recheck measured that THREE of the committed 37 had no repair anywhere and did not establish that the other 34 did, so `answered_elsewhere` carries only the findings whose answering file and check this package can name. A finding moves out of this set by someone naming them, never by assertion.","G2-06":"No file-and-check pair is recorded here for it. Classified conservatively by F6R-01: the recheck measured that THREE of the committed 37 had no repair anywhere and did not establish that the other 34 did, so `answered_elsewhere` carries only the findings whose answering file and check this package can name. A finding moves out of this set by someone naming them, never by assertion.","F6R-01":"The structural half landed in the previous lane and the reclassification half is only partly done. This entry is what remains: the conservative `not_answered` rows this lane did not personally verify a file-and-check pair for. Moving one across is cheap and must be earned by reading the check, which is the whole discipline the split exists for.","F6R-02":"ANSWERED BY A NOTE, NOT BY A CHECK, and recorded here rather than in answered_elsewhere because that distinction is the finding's own subject. The measurement (classify.mjs -> tier=trivial, enforcement=shadow) is written into the RC5-01 comment block of validate_contracts.py. Nothing executes it. Claiming a `check` for it would commit the exact error F6R-02 is about: treating a convention as an enforced tier.","F6R-04":"ANSWERED BY A NOTE, NOT BY A CHECK. The F6D-07 block now records that a hand edit to either enum surfaces as derivation drift before it surfaces as the concrete rule, and names F6C-11's cure (place the concrete check above the oracle). Applying that cure to F6D-07 is a reordering of validate_contracts.py with no fixture behind it, which this lane refused. Owed, with the remedy named.","F6V-01":"Raised by the second recheck against the PROSE layer, not the contracts layer. Lane r7-prose-b reports repairing halves of F6V-01 and F6V-03 in chapters 05 and 07. This lane did not read those chapters against those findings and will not record a file-and-check pair it has not verified -- which is the rule that made the previous lane's 32 rows conservative, applied to itself. A prose-side recheck is what moves these.","F6V-02":"Raised by the second recheck against the PROSE layer, not the contracts layer. Lane r7-prose-b reports repairing halves of F6V-01 and F6V-03 in chapters 05 and 07. This lane did not read those chapters against those findings and will not record a file-and-check pair it has not verified -- which is the rule that made the previous lane's 32 rows conservative, applied to itself. A prose-side recheck is what moves these.","F6V-03":"Raised by the second recheck against the PROSE layer, not the contracts layer. Lane r7-prose-b reports repairing halves of F6V-01 and F6V-03 in chapters 05 and 07. This lane did not read those chapters against those findings and will not record a file-and-check pair it has not verified -- which is the rule that made the previous lane's 32 rows conservative, applied to itself. A prose-side recheck is what moves these.","F6V-04":"Raised by the second recheck against the PROSE layer, not the contracts layer. Lane r7-prose-b reports repairing halves of F6V-01 and F6V-03 in chapters 05 and 07. This lane did not read those chapters against those findings and will not record a file-and-check pair it has not verified -- which is the rule that made the previous lane's 32 rows conservative, applied to itself. A prose-side recheck is what moves these.","F6AA-01":"Raised in F2-06-recheck-05.md section 3 against chapter 05. This lane writes no chapter and cannot name the file and check that answer a prose finding; the owner recorded in registers/review-findings.json is the chapter-05 prose lane. MD-02's question is restated with one of its two subjects removed and the narrowed version declared fully answered.","F6AA-02":"Raised in F2-06-recheck-05.md section 3 against chapter 05. This lane writes no chapter and cannot name the file and check that answer a prose finding; the owner recorded in registers/review-findings.json is the chapter-05 prose lane. The disposition that closes AC-M4-02 escalates the middle two consequence classes to the party whose non-answer triggered it.","F6AA-03":"Raised in F2-06-recheck-05.md section 3 against chapter 05. This lane writes no chapter and cannot name the file and check that answer a prose finding; the owner recorded in registers/review-findings.json is the chapter-05 prose lane. The OWED clause the F6Z-04 repair added is false at its own subject commit.","F6AA-04":"Raised in F2-06-recheck-05.md section 3 against chapter 05. This lane writes no chapter and cannot name the file and check that answer a prose finding; the owner recorded in registers/review-findings.json is the chapter-05 prose lane. Two further MD-02 sites still state the packet in its pre-decision form.","F6AA-05":"Raised in F2-06-recheck-05.md section 3 against chapter 05. This lane writes no chapter and cannot name the file and check that answer a prose finding; the owner recorded in registers/review-findings.json is the chapter-05 prose lane. MD-03's third clause is characterised two ways in one section and the repair's UNKNOWN rests on the narrower one.","F6AA-06":"Raised in F2-06-recheck-05.md section 3 against chapter 05. This lane writes no chapter and cannot name the file and check that answer a prose finding; the owner recorded in registers/review-findings.json is the chapter-05 prose lane. The fourth bucket is defined as \"neither ... dissolve ...\" and its member CAP-16 is then declared dissolved.","F6AA-11":"Raised in F2-06-recheck-05.md section 3 against chapter 05. This lane writes no chapter and cannot name the file and check that answer a prose finding; the owner recorded in registers/review-findings.json is the chapter-05 prose lane. Two different 41s six lines apart, over provably different sets, with nothing distinguishing them.","F6AA-07":"Raised in F2-06-recheck-05.md section 3 against this package and REPAIRED here: the comments above UNANSWERED_CEILING, NOT_ANSWERED_CEILING, ANSWERED_ELSEWHERE_CEILING and FINDING_SOURCE_FLOOR now state the value each constant holds, the committed count, and the fixture that holds the odd slot open. It stays on the conservative side of the partition anyway, because the repair is a SENTENCE and no check in this package can carry the truth of a sentence. A row moves across when a check answers the finding, not when the finding has been attended to.","F6AA-10":"Raised in F2-06-recheck-05.md section 3 against this package and REPAIRED here: the `why` of negative/r36-step-6-finding-loses-its-source-row now states the mechanism as it is -- a re-narrowing makes the fixture fail for the WRONG REASON, which the runner fails the build for -- and names FINDING_SOURCE_FLOOR, which fired first until this lane moved that assertion after the sweep. Same reason as F6AA-07 for staying here: the repair is a sentence in a fixture, and no check reads a fixture's `why`."},"source":"planning/specification/contracts/pinned-conjuncts.json#/not_answered"},{"id":"census_keys","why":"RC4-07. `CENSUS_KEYS` was a literal in validate_contracts.py and nothing else, so the set of fields the demand walk's census must carry was declared exactly once, in the file that also decides whether it carries them. One edit dropped a field from the requirement and from the check simultaneously, and the verdict went on printing a census that looked complete. Every `demanded` in the contracts means whatever that walk decided, and the census is the only thing in the verdict that says how far the walk reached -- so a quietly narrowed census is a quietly narrowed coverage claim. Pinned HERE and compared there, which is the shape `admissible_ancestors` already uses: two declarations in two files, so narrowing the set takes two edits a reviewer sees and the diff says what was dropped.","value":["operators","predicate_positions","refused","slots_classified","under_disjunction","under_negation","under_quantifier","value_positions"],"source":"planning/specification/contracts/pinned-conjuncts.json#/census_keys"},{"id":"computed_projections","why":"F6D-08, and it is a REGISTRY-LEVEL pin rather than a conjunct one: `ArmedSet.registration.permitted_commands` is `[]`, it has zero transitions, and mutation m4 -- replacing that empty list with the three kernel record commands -- was exit 0, UNDETECTED. The one structural containment the record has was one JSON line from gone and nothing compared it to anything. Seven records declare `lifecycle.projection: true`; FIVE have no permitted command and TWO (DependencyClosure, IndexSnapshot) do, so a blanket rule over the flag would be false about the tree it is written against. The partition below is hand-written for that reason and is checked in both directions -- a new projection record belongs in exactly one list, and adding one without saying which is what the completeness half refuses. SECOND, and this is the other half of F6D-08: on a derived projection `owner_component` names the CUSTODIAN, not a writer. `ArmedSet.owner_component` is S1-C02, the admission authority its own invariant excludes from writing precondition-bearing kinds; those two statements only contradict if the field is read as write authority. The custodial reading is now written into `ArmedSet.owner_assignment` in record-registry.json as well, because a reader of the record does not come here first. THIRD: `evaluator_module` was a free string with no binding to anything -- W8, nothing creates an `ArmedSet` either. `evaluator_modules` below states the closed set, each member of which must be a `planned_module` actually registered on some record. FOURTH, and it is a correction this lane made after its own first draft was refused: the no-transition clause was written as `transitions == []` for all five and AccessGraph has edges, so the rule was false about the tree in front of it. `transition_count` states each record's current count and the check compares it -- an edge ADDED to a projection is a second write path and is what this refuses; an edge that already exists is recorded, not pretended away.","value":[{"record":"ArmedSet","evaluator_modules":["system/packages/work/armed-set"],"why":"`05` section 7: a computed projection with no lifecycle that nobody writes, and in particular the admission authority holds no write access to any precondition-bearing kind. m4 is the mutation this row refuses.","transition_count":0},{"record":"AccessGraph","evaluator_modules":[],"why":"The reachability closure over access grants is derived from the grants; a command that wrote it would let a component grant itself reach.","transition_count":8},{"record":"DomainEvent","evaluator_modules":[],"why":"Events are emitted by the kernel commit path, never registered through a record command; a permitted command here would let a party author its own history.","transition_count":0},{"record":"OperationStatus","evaluator_modules":[],"why":"Status is read off the operation's own lifecycle. A writable status is a report of success for work that stopped, which is W7's failure condition verbatim.","transition_count":6},{"record":"OperatorProjection","evaluator_modules":[],"why":"The operator's view is computed from the records it projects; writing it directly would make the view and the thing disagree with nothing noticing.","transition_count":12}],"source":"planning/specification/contracts/pinned-conjuncts.json#/computed_projections"},{"id":"computed_projections_with_writers","why":null,"value":[{"record":"DependencyClosure","permitted_commands":["kernel.record.register","kernel.record.revise","kernel.record.transition"],"why":"Declared `projection: true` AND carries the three kernel record commands. Recorded rather than hidden: this is either a projection that is written or a flag that is wrong, and F6D-08 is about exactly that kind of disagreement. Naming it here means the next edit to it is a two-place edit a reviewer sees."},{"record":"IndexSnapshot","permitted_commands":["kernel.record.register","kernel.record.revise","kernel.record.transition","knowledge.index.record"],"why":"The same shape, plus `knowledge.index.record`. Same reading: listed so the exception is declared rather than discovered by a later mutation that passes."}],"source":"planning/specification/contracts/pinned-conjuncts.json#/computed_projections_with_writers"},{"id":"producer_unauthorable_fields","why":"F6D-05: twenty-nine of thirty guards read only fields on their own subject record, and in twenty-six the guard's owning component is the component that writes that record. `05` section 1 requires the consequence class to be computed from records the ACTING PARTY CANNOT AUTHOR. Two of the thirty are load-bearing -- guard.skill.declared_grant_inert and guard.launcher.stripping_positive_control both take Ref<SkillVersion>, whose owner_component is S1-C03, THE PRODUCING EXECUTOR, so the positive control on grant removal was a field on the record whose grants are being removed. guard.interest.precondition_invokes_no_model has the same shape over StandingInterest (S1-C02). WHAT THIS TABLE IS AND IS NOT. It fixes the field-level OWNER of each control field to a component that is not the record's producer, and refuses the edit that hands it back. It does NOT make the guard read a record the producer cannot author -- that is the IdentityBinding rebinding the finding asks for, it needs a ref field and a phase the chapters have not fixed, and it is recorded OWED in F2/07-repair-names-contract.md rather than invented here. The finding classifies itself (b), 'recorded with its verification owed', and this is the half that is checkable offline. S1-C04 is chosen because it owns IdentityBinding, which is the binding the finding names. THE CITATION FOR THAT OWNERSHIP IS THE REGISTRY, `record-registry.json#/IdentityBinding/owner_component`, AND NOT `02` SECTION 4 (F6Y-05): that section, lines 67 to 113, contains no S1-C0* id at all and its one mention of IdentityBinding, in the mutual-TLS paragraph, assigns no owner. The old citation sent a reader to a passage that could not settle what it was cited for, which is worse than no citation, because the mechanism it points at is real. What remains a reading rather than a chapter statement is the CHOICE of S1-C04 for these five fields, and two of the five have a competing chapter claim a recheck should weigh: `03` section 27 gives C05 validity and lineage, which reaches content_hash_rechecked_at_use, and C06 evidence and acceptance, which reaches precondition_evaluator_kind. Neither row's reason argues against those; each argues only against the PRODUCER. Owed, and owed to a chapter owner rather than to this table: `05` section 1 or `02` section 4 stating the owner of each control field, or the choice registered as an open question, so that a later lane reading 'it is a reading of the chapters' can find the chapter text it is a reading of. It also resolves the registry side of the contradiction the finding names separately: `05` section 1 says C03 executors remain outside writable registry state while the registry gave SkillVersion owner_component S1-C03 with write 'only named owner'. The probe-result fields are no longer C03's. The record-level owner is untouched, and the chapter sentence is owed.","value":[{"record":"SkillVersion","field":"declared_tool_grant_effect","owner":"S1-C04","guard":"guard.skill.declared_grant_inert","why":"R-X15 argues the rule must be structural rather than asserted; while this field belonged to the producer it was the producer asserting its own grant inert."},{"record":"SkillVersion","field":"grant_stripping_probe_result","owner":"S1-C04","guard":"guard.launcher.stripping_positive_control","why":"The positive control on grant removal. Owned by the producer, it was the record whose grants are removed reporting that they were."},{"record":"SkillVersion","field":"grant_stripping_probe_ref","owner":"S1-C04","guard":"guard.launcher.stripping_positive_control","why":"The probe the result comes from, owned by the party that runs it."},{"record":"SkillVersion","field":"content_hash_rechecked_at_use","owner":"S1-C04","guard":"guard.skill.declared_grant_inert","why":"A recheck AT USE is a statement by the enforcement point at use time, not by the content that is rechecked."},{"record":"StandingInterest","field":"precondition_evaluator_kind","owner":"S1-C04","guard":"guard.interest.precondition_invokes_no_model","why":"The guard checks a string on the interest saying its evaluator invokes no model. Owned by C02, that is the party with the interest classifying its own evaluator."}],"source":"planning/specification/contracts/pinned-conjuncts.json#/producer_unauthorable_fields"},{"id":"natural_key_create_paths","why":"F6V-02. A natural key is a RESOLUTION RULE, not a comment: each record below declares one in record-registry.json under identity.natural_key, and until this table existed no create path carried it. Each row names the command that creates the record and the resolution that command must state -- structurally, as on_conflict and creates_second_record in the transaction_contract of the command, never as a sentence containing the word resolve. The table is the second place the semantics is written, so handing it back is a two-place edit a reviewer sees; and the row set is compared to the registry in both directions, so a new record declaring a natural key cannot be added unguarded. Adverse fixture R42.","value":[{"record":"AdmissionRecord","natural_key":["origin","arrival_seq"],"create_path":"kernel.record.register","on_conflict":"resolve_to_existing_head","why":"05 section 2 gives the identity as origin plus arrival sequence, and the per-origin subcap that guard.intake.per_origin_subcap_preserves_intake protects is counted over exactly this key. A create path that made a second admission for one arrival would miscount the cap it is the subject of."},{"record":"EffectIdentity","natural_key":["effect_class_id","counterparty_id","payload_digest"],"create_path":"kernel.record.register","on_conflict":"resolve_to_existing_head","why":"05 section 6 answers the tenth (d)-class example of the protocol by having a second claimant JOIN the first and inherit its outcome. That answer is unreachable unless the create path resolves: two rows for one triple is a race and a second release."},{"record":"ExhaustionDecision","natural_key":["obligation_ref","window"],"create_path":"kernel.record.register","on_conflict":"resolve_to_existing_head","why":"One decision per obligation per window. A second row is two answers to whether the obligation was performed or breached, which is the question the record exists to have exactly one answer to."},{"record":"FieldAuthority","natural_key":["field_path","epoch"],"create_path":"kernel.record.register","on_conflict":"resolve_to_existing_head","why":"08 section 1 names a writer-key assignment as (field_path, epoch). Two records for one field path in one epoch are two answers to who may write this field -- and the whole of the F6D-05 repair reads that answer."}],"source":"planning/specification/contracts/pinned-conjuncts.json#/natural_key_create_paths"},{"id":"capability_publishing_structures","why":"F6W-01 / R-X07. 05 section 12 specifies that every standing structure owning the acceptance of a capability publishes its capability_refs, required and NON-EMPTY, and closes that set by name: StandingHolder and the acceptance-owner role record. The chapter says so of itself -- specified and unregistered -- and until this table existed the rule two consolidation findings are recorded as repaired by was carried by no record shape under contracts/**. Each row names the record, the field, and the minimum cardinality, and the checks read all three out of BOTH declarations, so publishing the binding back into optionality is a four-place edit. OWED and stated rather than faked: the acceptance-owner role record the chapter names as the second member of the closed set has NO record in record-registry.json, so it gets no row here -- inventing one would be specification by side effect, and its absence is named in the lane names contract instead. Adverse fixture R43.","value":[{"record":"StandingHolder","field":"capability_refs","minimum":1,"why":"05 section 12: the binding is per capability and never grouped, coverage is counted over the 46 capability ids individually, and a capability no structure names is uncovered rather than covered by default. A StandingHolder that publishes no capability_refs is a standing office accountable for nothing the coverage rule can count, which is the state R-X07 exists to end. 05 section 12 also amends the enumeration of the record in section 12 so that its own `and nothing else` admits this field."}],"source":"planning/specification/contracts/pinned-conjuncts.json#/capability_publishing_structures"}]}
docs/vision-system/planning/specification/08-improvement-implementation.md:32:**SPECIFICATION.** Supporting persisted types use RecordEnvelope: ChangeEvaluationPlan/v1 (frozen subject/baseline, task population, selection/denominator, outcomes, critical regressions, sample design, stopping rule, evaluator identities/competence, test suite digests, data lineage, thresholds and resource cap); ChangeTrial/v1 (plan ref, candidate/baseline digest, assignment seed, attempts/captures, omissions, deviations and results refs); ReleaseManifest/v1 (source tree, artifact digests, schema/meaning versions, dependency lock/SBOM, installed profiles, migrations, configuration digests, compatibility interval and approver refs); RolloutPlan/v1 (cohorts, maximum exposure, entry/exit/stop conditions, due obligations and native descendants); ChangeWatch/v1 (release ref, monitored outcomes, observation intervals, missing-data policy, stop owner and next review); MigrationPlan/v1 (old/new representations and meanings, converter digest, pre/post predicates, scope/conflict changes, live readers/writers, data loss, rollback boundary and reconciliation). These are implementation-support records, not a declaration that the later 46-subject catalog is complete.
docs/vision-system/planning/specification/08-improvement-implementation.md:54:**SPECIFICATION.** Before a stochastic trial, freeze a task-stratified baseline, exact candidate, random assignment, common inputs and permitted context, resources, competent judges, critical failure predicates and outcome thresholds. Reuse historical tasks only where consent/access/lineage remain valid; hold out fresh tasks to detect benchmark memorization. Default noncritical comparison uses at least 30 matched task pairs across at least three relevant task classes and at least two independent runs per stochastic profile. This is a planning minimum, not a statistical guarantee; power depends on variance/effect size, so a predeclared interval or exact paired test and minimum worthwhile effect determine whether the evidence is sufficient. Report every run, timeout, refusal, invalid output, retry, cost and missing observation. Critical invariant tests require zero observed violations plus adversarial mechanism evidence, never a statistical permission to violate an invariant.
docs/vision-system/planning/specification/08-improvement-implementation.md:219:| B08 / B04 | ProtectedChange/trial/evaluator/rollout/watch/migration, stochastic baseline and cumulative drift. C06/C04/C01. | Candidate alters gate/denominator/evaluator tests; successful useful improvement with independent assessment; rollback with irreversible effects and changed meanings. | Never self-accept the builder's system change or overfit the same benchmark population. |
docs/vision-system/planning/specification/08-improvement-implementation.md:224:**SPECIFICATION.** Parallel construction may proceed only where frozen interfaces and isolation permit; B04 can develop against B01 contracts while B02/B03 infrastructure is built, but no domain code bypasses an unavailable witness to demonstrate progress. B05/B06 integrate actual evidence paths before B09. The whole build remains incomplete until every stage's relevant contract, integration and independent evidence obligation is satisfied.
docs/vision-system/planning/site/explorer/data/layers.json:1:{"source":"planning/02-architecture-selection.md#3-selected-logical-and-responsibility-model","introduction":"**S1.1 — the five layers of the work / agents / authority / skills / context / routing layer, and their precedence (F2, 2026-09-13).** The nine logical components above are unchanged and no tenth is added. What the F2 round settles is **which question each part of that layer decides, and which decision governs when two disagree**. Named plainly: **consequence class decides who may act; a declared procedure decides how the work runs and what each step may see; a typed standing interest decides when work becomes due; an existence record decides whether a worker may be created at all; and exactly one standing party exists for each duty that outlives the case carrying it.**","precedence":"**Precedence is fixed and operative: the lower-numbered layer governs when two disagree.** Class may **raise** what a procedure permits and never lower it. An interest may arm but never admit above its effect class. An existence record may refuse a worker the class would permit but never create one the class forbids. A holder may hold but never act. **Why a layering rather than one organizing unit:** the round established that there is **no single unit of justification** — the founder's five criteria predicate on five different objects, and a criterion applied to the wrong unit returns undecidable, which reads as satisfied. Each of the five candidate designs carried its worst blocking findings on **its own routing unit**, so a synthesis that picked one unit would have inherited that unit's blind spot. Layering the units and stating which governs does not. The five criteria themselves are judged in [the F2 selection record](F2/05-selection-record.md) §2: **distinct tools or permissions** confirmed and the strongest of the five, **isolated context** refined and split into an attention sense and a confidentiality sense with only the latter justifying a worker, **independent verification** refined with half of it unreachable inside one model family, **parallel work** refined to near-inert at the current concurrency pin, and **specialized knowledge overturned** as a reason to create a worker.","selection_record_criteria":{"heading":"2. The thesis, judged","text":"*For the founder. Plain language. Each line names the finding that decided it.*","source":"planning/F2/05-selection-record.md"},"items":[{"id":"L1","name":"L1 · consequence class","decides":"who may act","governing_rule":"Every action carries the **set** of routing classes it reaches, computed by one deterministic function from records the acting party cannot author, recomputed at release on the frozen bytes; **every reached class's gates apply** and no rank is computed","where_specified":"`05` §11; restating [`specification/02-authority-recovery.md`](specification/02-authority-recovery.md) §4","rule_sections":[{"section":"11","heading":"11. Consequence class and the layer contract","text":"**SPECIFICATION — new in WORK-1.1. This section states layer 1 (R-L1) and the precedence rule; §1 introduces them and this section is where they bind.**\n\n**Every action carries the set of routing classes it reaches.** The set is computed by **one deterministic function** from four inputs and no others: the **resolved parameters**; the **destination and egress identity**; the **selector closure** over conflict claims, deletion scopes and open obligations; and the **owning capability contract's declared floor**. **Every reached class's gates apply.** No total rank exists, **no seventh class is added**, and **no severity score is computed** — this restates [`02-authority-recovery.md`](02-authority-recovery.md) §4, which already heads its table *\"Routing classes are predicates, not a total privilege rank\"*, and it changes nothing there. The gate evaluator consumes the **set**; a future implementer who reintroduces a rank drops C2's human requirement on an action that is both C2 and C3, which is the observed failure (AT-M4-02, disposed in [the selection record](../F2/05-selection-record.md) §5.2). **No monotonicity proof is owed, because no ordering is used** (R-D22).\n\n**`ConsequenceDerivation` is the record of the derivation.** Identity `(operation_intent_ref, derivation_fn_version, derived_at)`; lifecycle `computed → recomputed_at_release → matched | parked_on_mismatch`; **sole writer: the release path**; **append-only**. `mismatch_disposition` is writable only by the party owning the park. **The class is recomputed inside the ordered release transaction, on the frozen bytes, and a mismatch parks and never resolves downward.**\n\n**There is exactly one implementation of the derivation.** Two implementations of risk classification disagree, and you find out during the incident — observed directly in this repository, where a second, stricter classifier in a workflow file demanded a tier the one classifier did not compute. The function, the mapping table, the holder set and every declared floor are **C5 protected control changes** requiring independent authorization, with **no model in the acceptance path** (see [`08-improvement-implementation.md`](08-improvement-implementation.md) §1).\n\n**Precedence, stated operatively.** Lower-numbered layers govern. **Class may raise what a procedure permits and never lower it.** **An interest may arm but never admit above its effect class.** **An existence record may refuse a worker the class would permit, but never create one the class forbids.** **A holder may hold but never act.**\n\n**What \"carries a promise\" means, and why it is not computed from a draft (R-D21).** Whether an outward artifact carries a promise is **not computable from any of the four permitted derivation inputs**, and a non-model step that recognised an obligation inside a draft would put a judgement inside the class derivation that this layer's own rule forbids. It is therefore **floored by the capability**: CAP-13, CAP-14, CAP-15 and CAP-16 floor at the economic/contractual class. **UNKNOWN — founder-owned parameter (selection record §6.2, MD-21):** which capabilities carry the floor. The stated default is **all four**; narrowing the set is a throughput trade and it is the founder's, because it decides how much outward drafting needs a person.\n\n**The model provider is a named C2 disclosure destination (R-D12).** It carries a standing `DisclosureContract`, and the loader's class-narrowed projection **is** the destination-clean construction that [`02-authority-recovery.md`](02-authority-recovery.md) §8.2 already admits — so a model call is a **pre-authorised C2 release gated by projection conformance**, not a C04 transaction per turn. Amending that contract is a C5 change. **The \"model calls are exempt\" branch is refused**: exemption would have relaxed a fixed boundary, and taking a construction the boundary already admits does not.\n\n**Approval expiry and the accumulated set are themselves C5.** The derivation function, the mapping table, the standing-holder set and the declared floors are C5 (above). So is the **accumulated approval set**, which is the object an executor's own record never shows: each approval is individually small and the ratchet lives only in their sum, which is why R-X18's expiry and the monotonic-exposure diff over **effects releasable without a human** are stated here and not left to review.\n\n**Removal criterion for layer 1, in falsifier form (R-X26).** Layer 1 is removed when **more than 90% of admitted actions derive to the two lowest classes over a fixed window** — then the added structure is not paid for. **Or** when **the derivation and the declared floor agree on every action over a window**, in which case the derivation adds nothing the floor already said and the floor alone survives. Both need only the derivation function and a month of admitted work, which makes this the most executable falsifier this chapter carries, and it is aimed at this layer's own foundation.","source":"planning/specification/05-work-agents-skills.md"}],"source":"planning/02-architecture-selection.md#3-selected-logical-and-responsibility-model"},{"id":"L2","name":"L2 · declared procedure","decides":"how, and what each step may see","governing_rule":"Immutable versioned steps declaring kind, read set, grants, validator and branch set; the **loader delivers the read set and records what it delivered**; a guard is a pure function and a model's output is never a jump; one effect per effect step","where_specified":"`05` §3","rule_sections":[{"section":"3","heading":"3. Workflow, run and step execution","text":"**SPECIFICATION — amended in WORK-1.1; no record is renamed and no record is added here.** `WorkflowDefinition` is an immutable versioned procedure: typed input/output ports, named steps, deterministic guards, allowed adaptive branches, stage rules, maximum elapsed/idle time, retry/compensation contracts, evidence and acceptance roles. **`WorkflowDefinition` and `StepExecution` additionally carry six declared fields** (R-L2, [selection record](../F2/05-selection-record.md) §12.3's changed-records list): `step_kind ∈ {compute, model, human, professional, effect}`; `declared_read_set`; `declared_grants`; `validator_ref`; `branch_set`; and `critical_fields`. These are **fields on the existing registry records** — the candidate-era proposal to rename these records to `Procedure`/`Step`/`Journal` is refused (R-X02, closing AT-M3-02), and the alias table of [`11-schemas-state-contracts.md`](11-schemas-state-contracts.md) maps every candidate name to its registry name so that no candidate-era name is ever admitted as a record name. A fixed path handles known repeatable work; an adaptive step produces a proposed next plan under the same scope and allowance. The admission owner chooses the mode using uncertainty and cost evidence, not whether the producer prefers more freedom. Unknown cases leave the fixed path through an owned exception; they do not silently bypass gates.\n\n**SPECIFICATION.** `WorkflowRun` pins definition, Case, causal episode, exact inputs and current step cursor. `StepExecution` pins step definition and WorkOrder; its execution projection follows the canonical order/report/acceptance records. A run follows `prepared/running/waiting/parked/acceptance_pending/accepted/failed/cancelled`. A step follows `ready/dispatched/running/reported/accepted/rejected/waiting/cancelled`. Only C02 advances the cursor, in the same protected transaction that records the step result and creates the next work intent. C06 judgment plus the required sponsor acceptance permits a run's accepted state. Actual effect states remain OperationStatus dimensions.\n\n**SPECIFICATION — amended in WORK-1.1.** Each step declares an input contract, performer class, read/write resource scope, result envelope, allowed outcomes, exit predicate and next branch. **The loader delivers the step's `declared_read_set` and records what it actually delivered; the caller's claimed read list is not trusted** — the same rule [`06-knowledge-evidence-evaluation.md`](06-knowledge-evidence-evaluation.md) §2 already states for context assembly, now made a property of every step. This is what converts *\"the checker did not read the producer's rationale\"* from an assertion into a manifest fact, and a design in which a worker assembles its own context cannot make that claim at all. **A guard is a pure function over typed outputs and journal state; a model's output is an input to a guard and never a jump** — control flow is trusted, model output is data, and the published utility price of that separation is paid deliberately (R2 F-09). **One effect per effect step, and the step is the idempotency unit**: on resume after an interrupt the whole step restarts, so a human approval step that shared its node with the payment it approved could duplicate that payment (R3 F29, F30). **The step boundary is the checkpoint** (R-D19): every step boundary is a close-out point and the cost is carried, so no separate reserved-closing-allowance predicate exists — the alternative needed a denominator the round establishes does not exist (AT-M1-03). Deterministic transformations execute without a model. Nondeterministic model/tool/human results are captured once as attributable data; replay consumes the recorded result only while current validity permits it. A live regeneration is a new attempt, never “replay.” External operations are proposed and released through C04, outside database transactions. Domain acceptance can require an actual professional result or customer condition; a successful dispatch does not satisfy that guard.\n\n**SPECIFICATION.** Stage is an epistemic/business position such as proposed, investigated, validated, deliverable or maintaining. Status is whether execution is running, blocked or finished. Workflow definitions choose relevant stages; they do not impose a coding pipeline on finance or support. A small deterministic correction can use one production step and one required acceptance check. A declared guard may establish that a stage is inapplicable, with a reason; current authority, data permission, required review and actual duty-discharge predicates cannot be skipped. New contrary evidence can move the current projection backward through a recorded invalidation/review decision, preserving earlier acceptance history.\n\n**SPECIFICATION.** Changing a definition creates a new revision. Existing runs remain pinned if compatible and safe. A migration plan names in-flight states, old/new step mapping, preserved outputs/unknown effects, invalidated acceptance, current grants and rollback. C02 parks incompatible runs, and C04/C08 fence affected authority where required. Resuming from the middle requires exact accepted checkpoint, available inputs, compatible code/definition and current restrictions. The system does not replay a payment or customer contact to reconstruct a cursor.\n\n**SPECIFICATION.** Compensation is its own typed work with authority and acceptance. It may repair a consequence while leaving history and obligations. Steps declare `no_compensation`, an actual compensating procedure, or a need for a competent decision. A failed refund, apology or supplier replacement remains an owned duty; cancelling the workflow never makes those results true. Integration tests must inspect the combined journey after individually correct steps.\n\n**SPECIFICATION — the zero-allowance step kind, and maximising its share.** `step_kind: compute` consumes no model allowance. Determinism is the only lever that cuts subscription consumption without cutting work, so raising the `compute` share of a procedure is a first-class design goal of every procedure admission, and the share is reported per procedure version.\n\n**SPECIFICATION — procedure admission refuses a model-selected acceptance strength (R-X19, closing AS-M3-01).** A `branch_set` in which a **model-authored typed value selects between acceptance strengths** for one artifact is refused at admission, naming the failed predicate. Acceptance-strength selection is a guard over journal state and consequence class, never a producer's choice: typing the checker's *inputs* does not help if the producer still picks the *checker*. A model step may supply a typed value into a declared field of declared type and domain, and that is the whole of what it may do to control flow.\n\n**SPECIFICATION — a producing run may not select its own checker.** The checker's procedure comes from committed configuration, not from the producing run. A routing component that can choose who checks its own work has not achieved procedural independence.\n\n**SPECIFICATION — the adaptive envelope has a named author (R-X04, closing AT-M3-04).** An adaptive step's envelope is authored by the **capability owner at procedure admission**, never by the resuming or adapting attempt. The envelope of `unclassified-work/v1` is written out rather than left implied: step kinds `{compute, model, human}`; read set = the work record plus its cited sources; **effect classes = none**; one launch per step; and a declared maximum step count. A procedure whose adaptive envelope is unstated is not admissible.\n\n**SPECIFICATION — one parameter, not two (R-X05, closing AT-M3-05).** The collapse threshold (when an adaptive procedure collapses to a fixed path) and the retirement window (when that procedure version retires) are **one parameter with one owner** — the capability owner — declared per procedure at admission. Two numbers for one concept is what produced the finding; they cannot be set independently.\n\n**SPECIFICATION — `unclassified-work/v1` has a clock somebody owns.** Work admitted under it carries a **declared maximum age**, and a breach of that age is **itself admitted work** with an owner, not a log line. Unknown work is therefore neither dropped nor parked forever.\n\n**SPECIFICATION — a drafted procedure is not an executable one.** A procedure drafted by a model becomes executable only after a passing test suite **and** a human capability owner's acceptance. A control-flow structure authored by a model from untrusted input is precisely the thing the trust boundary exists to prevent (R3 F11). **A declared grant is resolved against the grant policy at admission**, so a declaration no configuration backs is refused rather than carried — the decorative-declaration loophole, observed in this repository as 44 capability declarations that nothing backed (R3 F57, F60). **The grant policy is not a new object, and naming it is the point (F6D-06): `declared_grants` is `Ref<Grant>[]` and is `required` on both `WorkflowDefinition` and `StepExecution`, and the registry of `Grant` records — issued by C04, each carrying issuer mandate, holder, purpose, destinations, bounds and expiry — is the policy it resolves against.** A second grant-policy record would be a second authority over one question, and two implementations of one rule disagree at the moment it matters. **Resolution is a conjunct on the admission edge** — `guard.grant.declared_resolves_to_live_grant` — and **the step is refused, naming the failed predicate, when a declared grant does not resolve to a live `Grant` held by the step's executing identity and no wider than what the step declares**; the paired benign case is a step whose declared grants all resolve, which must not be refused. **It is a typed ref and not bounded text**, because free text is the decorative form of this same declaration: a string cannot be resolved against anything, and `validator_ref` on the same record was already a typed ref, so the typed form was available and unused. **Arrival is a different fact from scope**: `GrantDeliveryReceipt` and `grant_arrival_attested` (§4) attest that a grant arrived, never that it was the right one, and this rule is the half that checks scope.\n\n**SPECIFICATION — permissions do not compose; they decompose.** Three permissions needed by one task become **three effect steps**, and the union grant never exists anywhere. This answers [the F2 acceptance protocol](../F2/00-acceptance-protocol.md) §5 item 6 — whether a composite grant is minted, borrowed or refused — with **refused, not minted**.\n\n**SPECIFICATION — removal criteria for the L2 additions, in falsifier form (R-X26).** The declared read set and the step model are removed when **a newer model passes every step's declared validator with the step merged into its neighbour or removed**. The precedent runs against its own authors' interest and is why the criterion is stated rather than assumed: a scaffold's contribution is a function of the model generation that motivated it and must be re-ablated when the model changes. The `critical_fields` marking is removed when, over a window, no resumed attempt's behaviour differs with the marking present or absent.\n\n**SPECIFICATION — what marks a field critical, and who marks it (R-D18).** A field is critical if a `ParameterAuthority` governs it, if it is a `ConstraintSet` member, or if the procedure declares it in `critical_fields`. The marking authority is the **capability owner at procedure admission** — never the resuming attempt, which is the party with an interest in the answer.","source":"planning/specification/05-work-agents-skills.md"}],"source":"planning/02-architecture-selection.md#3-selected-logical-and-responsibility-model"},{"id":"L3","name":"L3 · typed standing interest","decides":"when work becomes due","governing_rule":"Relevance is a **computed, unstoppable armed set** over typed fields after every committed transition; **no precondition may invoke a model**; all prerequisites simultaneously, unexpired, uncontradicted, at or above their trust class","where_specified":"`05` §7","rule_sections":[{"section":"7","heading":"7. Durable schedules and capacity gaps","text":"**SPECIFICATION.** `Schedule` binds an accepted workflow/capability version, actual timezone/calendar rule, activation interval, occurrence window, latest responsible start, catch-up/concurrency policy, authority, resource class, sponsor and alternate. The initial scheduler is the kernel's durable SQL timer sweep plus event-triggered wakeups; no model runs merely to notice time. `ScheduleOccurrence` identity is schedule revision plus intended local/calendar occurrence and resolved UTC instant. The timezone-rule version and ambiguous/nonexistent local-time policy are explicit. A clock jump cannot create a second logical occurrence.\n\n**SPECIFICATION.** Every schedule chooses one missed-occurrence policy. **Individual reconciliation** preserves each due invoice, service occurrence or reporting duty and its actual deadline. **Coalesce** produces one current research/maintenance assessment with the omitted windows listed; it cannot merge distinct rights. **Skip-expired** discards obsolete promotional opportunities with a reason and no catch-up blast. **Escalate** activates the accepted custodian/alternate when a missed action needs actual competent judgment. Defaults offered by procedure kind must be explicitly adopted; the software does not invent statutory deadlines or customer agreement terms.\n\n**SPECIFICATION.** Occurrence states are `planned/due/admitted/running/completed/missed/disposed`; completion follows actual workflow acceptance. Missing work is not automatically marked completed when the next occurrence starts. The scheduling owner records what was intended, actual wake/start, lateness, duplicates suppressed, partial work and remaining duty. Concurrency defaults forbid overlapping instances of the same effect-bearing occurrence; independent read-only assessment can overlap only under separate input/resource admission.\n\n**SPECIFICATION.** Unattended work needs all prerequisites in standing mandates, available context/tools, finite budgets, acceptance and no-answer/continuity behavior before starting. Attended mode does not weaken authority or allow unavailable service. When the company has no due or authorized useful work, executors idle; planned discovery runs only within its adopted mandate. During a gap, surviving local work can checkpoint through D1, due service uses actually available independent routes, and unavailable performance remains an operational failure. Return presents the human account's actual changes, missing periods and unresolved consequences.\n\n**SPECIFICATION — `StandingInterest` and the armed set, new in WORK-1.1 (R-L3).** `StandingInterest` has identity `(id, version)` and lifecycle `proposed → trial → admitted → suspended → retired`; the **maintenance custodian proposes and the capability owner admits**. `ArmedSet` has identity `(journal_position)`, is a **computed projection with no lifecycle, and nobody writes it**. **Relevance is computed, and the armed set is unstoppable**: it is evaluated by deterministic code over typed fields after **every committed transition**, and **no component may prevent membership** — in particular, the admission authority holds no write access to any precondition-bearing kind. This is what makes a deferral a **visible state with a latest responsible time** rather than an absence indistinguishable from an oversight, which is the defect S1.0 carries because nothing exists until the case authority admits it (R5-01, R5-02). *Amended 2026-09-15 (F6D-08): on a derived projection `owner_component` names the **custodian** and not a writer — `ArmedSet.owner_component` is `S1-C02` in [`contracts/record-registry.json`](contracts/record-registry.json), whose `ArmedSet.owner_assignment` states that on a derived projection the field names the custodian and never a writer — so the invariant above and that value read as consistent rather than as the admission authority holding the write access this sentence denies it.*\n\n**SPECIFICATION — the hard rules of layer 3.** **No precondition may invoke a model.** A model-evaluated gate is a model-placed boundary, which cannot hold, and determinism is the only free lever on capacity (AG-08; R4 F4, F6; R8 B-7). **An interest arms only when every declared prerequisite holds simultaneously, unexpired, uncontradicted, and at or above its required trust class** — the all-prerequisites shape, not a single-prerequisite trigger (R3 F33, D-15). **Trust class gates what an entry may activate and is never a weight on a ranking**: provenance-weighted ranking was indistinguishable from no defence at its shipped weight and took evidence recall to exactly zero at the weight that worked (R1 F-10). **The armed set is recomputed, never carried in a summary**, so a pre-reset summary that omits a decision cannot cause the wrong activation — the summary is not what activates. **A standing interest may write only a `proposed` revision of a constraint** (R-D23); `proposed → endorsed` remains C01's. **A proposal declaring a writer key is refused, naming the failed predicate** (R-D16): writer keys are assigned only by the record authority, and a trial may write only into kinds whose writer is already \"any activation\". **`proposed → trial` is admissible only at the two lowest effect classes**; read-only and internal-artifact capabilities proceed on an **expiring bounded trial** under a standing mandate while approval is pending, and outward-draft and outward-release require a human approver (R-G11). **UNKNOWN — founder packet MD-03 (selection record §6.5):** who that human approver is, its ceiling, and what happens during a founder absence. No default is invented; until it is answered, outward classes have no approver and therefore do not proceed.\n\n**SPECIFICATION — admission is bounded to five verbs and five prohibitions.** The verbs are **admit, defer, shed, refuse, rank**. Among the prohibitions, the one that binds hardest is that **the admitter may not accept work it admitted**; the ordered custody resolver of [`03-company-capabilities.md`](03-company-capabilities.md) therefore **skips the admitting identity and continues to the next tier, recording `custody_tie_break_reason = admitter_excluded`** (R-X06). The admission authority gains one refusal predicate it lacked: **a per-origin arming rate** (R-X21). A single origin that can arm interests without bound is a disturbance loop, and the evaluation protocol for that predicate is stated here rather than cited elsewhere — baseline the per-origin arming rate over a declared window, unit is armings per origin per window, repetition is every window, the stopping rule is two consecutive windows above the declared rate, and the owner is C02.\n\n**SPECIFICATION — the unmatched pool, and its residue named.** `UnmatchedPoolEntry` has identity `(work_record_ref)` and lifecycle `landed → claimed | refused | escalated`, written by the pool interest **deterministically**. It is the **computable complement** of the armed set: whatever armed no interest lands in it. **Retention exceeds the longest plausible outage** and **an alarm on arrival has a named reader**. **And the residue is stated rather than implied: the pool cannot catch an entry that armed the *wrong* interest.** A catch-all that does not name what it cannot catch is decoration (R5-09). **Removal criterion for layer 3, in falsifier form:** over one month, if **every item whose relevance nobody currently holds in mind is surfaced within its latest responsible time by the world-change sweep specified in the next paragraph**, arming buys nothing and is removed. *Amended 2026-09-14 (F6A-02): the comparator read “**the existing scheduled review**”, which named nothing — no scheduled review is specified in this chapter or in [`02-authority-recovery.md`](02-authority-recovery.md), where the string “scheduled review” occurs zero times (checked 2026-09-14).* **Or** if the deterministic-predicate fraction falls below the threshold set under R-X25, layer 3 is **withdrawn rather than relaxed** — relaxing it for even one precondition class would reintroduce the model-placed boundary the layer exists to avoid. **UNKNOWN — founder parameter, no default (R-X25):** the value of that threshold. The measurement itself — the fraction of the company's conditions expressible as deterministic typed predicates — is owed with a baseline, a unit, a stopping rule and an owner, and it is cheap and unrun.\n\n**SPECIFICATION — the world-change sweep, new 2026-09-14 (F6A-02).** The armed set is computed over committed transitions and `UnmatchedPoolEntry` is its complement over work records, so **an external state change that writes no transition and produces no work record neither arms nor lands in the pool** — a jurisdictional policy change is the worked case, and it is a second residue beside the one this section already names. **The entry path for such work is a named periodic sweep in this chapter, not a review assumed to exist elsewhere.** A `Schedule` whose accepted capability version is the **world-change sweep** runs under this section's ordinary rules: **owner C02**, which holds the schedule and its alternate; **missed-occurrence policy `individual reconciliation`** — never `coalesce` and never `skip-expired`, because an external change that looks obsolete is exactly what this sweep exists not to discard; and a **latest responsible start of one occurrence per review period**, the period §12 prices holder review over. Each occurrence enumerates the company's declared external dependencies — jurisdiction, provider terms, professional obligations and counterparty agreements — and **writes a work record for every change it finds, which is what returns the item to the armed set's reach**. A sweep that finds nothing **records that it found nothing**; an occurrence that does not run is `missed` and is itself admitted work, never a silent skip. **UNKNOWN — founder parameter, no default:** the review-period length this shares with §12, and who performs the enumeration where the dependency is a professional obligation (MD-02).\n\n**DESIGN PROPOSAL — the protocol that would test the sweep, stated as the (c)-class hypothesis it is (F6A-02).** The claim *a periodic sweep surfaces world-change work within its latest responsible time* carries no evidence, and naming a sweep does not supply any. **Protocol:** a **planted-item probe** — a party outside the sweep's producing path records, out of band and before the window opens, a dated set of external changes that did occur in it; the sweep's output is compared against that set after the window closes. **Baseline:** the first full review period of ordinary operation. **Unit:** planted items surfaced within their latest responsible time as a fraction of planted items, reported beside the count of unplanted items the sweep surfaced, because a sweep that surfaces everything and a sweep that surfaces nothing both score well on one of those numbers alone. **Repetition:** every review period. **Stopping rule:** two consecutive periods at or above the declared threshold retire the probe; one period below it **withdraws the sufficiency claim and reopens the layer-3 removal criterion that rests on it**. **UNKNOWN — founder parameter, no default:** the value of that threshold. **Owner:** the instrument custodian of [`06-knowledge-evidence-evaluation.md`](06-knowledge-evidence-evaluation.md) §5, excluded from every producing path — **not C02**, which owns the sweep and may not grade itself. The probe is authored and frozen **before** the period it grades, under §12's ordering rule: a case authored once the result is known is void.\n\n**SPECIFICATION — the metered-affordance observer.** A `credit-setting` interest **observes the metered affordance and halts new launches in that class when it flips**, and it is disclosed as **observation, not prevention**: the metered path is one account setting away at both providers and nothing currently observes it. The observation point, cadence, named reader and response live in [`07-integrations-capacity.md`](07-integrations-capacity.md) §5, and the flip is priced there as a **capacity** event as well as a money and policy one.\n\n**SPECIFICATION — a sample of what was refused is returned (`refusal-sample`), inside an encounter kind that already exists.** A bounded sample of work the system declined is returned to the founder **as the adverse stratum of the first of [`04-human-operation.md`](04-human-operation.md)'s four encounter kinds — original customer material, which already alternates ordinary with adverse, abandoned and underserved cases** — on that chapter's existing cycle, inside its declared batch minutes, drawn by its existing sampling rule: a reproducible recorded random seed within strata, outside the account producer's write authority, with empty strata recorded rather than replaced by flattering examples. **A refusal nobody reviews is a decision nobody made**, and a job the company declined is the underserved case that stratum exists for. **It takes places in that stratum rather than adding places**, and the competition is visible because the sampling record already states what was drawn and which strata were empty. **This adds no encounter kind, no cadence and no counted line to `04`'s attention admission, so it is not a third delta to that chapter's FIXED competence mechanism** (F6A-03). The test is written out so a reader can check it rather than take it: if `refusal-sample` required a slot of its own, a cadence of its own, or an attention line of its own, it would be a delta and would need a decision packet under [DIRECTIVE §3](../../inputs/DIRECTIVE.md); it requires none of the three. *Superseded 2026-09-14: this paragraph read \"returned to the founder on the participation cycle of `04-human-operation.md`\" and named no encounter kind. `04` §3 declares **exactly two deltas** against the competence mechanism and calls any further delta a decision packet, so a construction riding the cycle without naming where it rides was a third delta on one reading and a coherence defect on the other. The disposition taken here is to keep `04` fixed and route the sample through a kind it already has.*\n\n**SPECIFICATION — the unretirable `grievance` interest.** The `grievance` interest may not be retired. It composes with the closure interlock of §12: **closure cannot complete until the grievance holder's duties are transferred to an accepted custodian**, because a closure with an unowned redress route is a broken promise recorded as a clean end.\n\n**SPECIFICATION — capacity rules this section adds to [`07-integrations-capacity.md`](07-integrations-capacity.md) §6.** **Capacity is carried on the fields that already exist, and this amendment adds no `budget` field.** An object that consumes capacity is bounded by the `allowance` on its `CausalEpisode` and by its own `reservation_refs`, both **required** today in [the record schema](contracts/records.schema.json), and `CapacityState` — the registry name is `CapacityObservation`, through [`11`'s alias table](11-schemas-state-contracts.md) — records **remaining-or-unknown structurally rather than by assurance**: its `measurement` is a `MeasuredQuantity`, which is `{knowledge: observed, quantity, evidence_refs}` **exclusive-or** `{knowledge: unknown, reason, held_maximum}`, so an unknown allowance **cannot be written as a number** and writing it unknown forces a reason and a held maximum. *Superseded 2026-09-14: this read “**`budget` is a mandatory schema field on every object that consumes capacity**”. **Zero of 188 records declared a field whose name begins `budget` and zero required one**, so the sentence was itself the decorative declaration §3 refuses two sections earlier — a declaration no configuration backs (F6A-08, F6D-10). The `CapacityState` half was correct, is kept, and is now stated in terms of the field that carries it.* **A cross-class release happens at a declared lapse point** with a stated precedence for which class receives released capacity — due service, then continuity/security/grievance, then maintenance and evaluation, then ordinary creation, then discretionary — and the **quantity that lapsed unconsumed is recorded per lane per window**. That release is **independent of any holder's consent** (R-X24). **The exhaustion rule is distinct from the pressure rule** (R-G01): when the allowance is empty and a due obligation falls due, the **named non-model production mode** of `07` §6 performs it — carried by the required `Obligation.production_mode` and its `production_performer_ref`, with an obligation in an exhaustible duty class whose mode is `none` refused at admission (F6C-01) — a named recipient is alerted, and the breach-or-perform decision leaves a record naming which was chosen and why: **`ExhaustionDecision`**, written once per `(obligation_ref, window)`, C02 proposing and C01 authorising, and deliberately not a variant of `ShedDecision` (F6C-02) — *fifty percent of an empty bucket is zero* is the case that rule exists for. **The concurrency pin these lanes are sized against is itself unsettled — provider constraint or self-imposed policy is unknown — and the account inspection that settles it is the founder's, registered as [Q-022](../../registers/open-questions.json)** (F6C-07); §12's reserved-lane holder rests on a fixture that cannot be run until it is answered. **Evaluation carries a row of its own among [`07-integrations-capacity.md`](07-integrations-capacity.md) §6's enumerated planning shares — distinct from the maintenance row and not funded out of it** (R-X11, F6C-05) — and when the evaluation cycle collides with a pressure window **evaluation sheds at the maintenance tier's position in that section's release precedence, and the shed cycle is a recorded instrument gap, never a silent skip**. *Amended 2026-09-14 (F6C-05): the row and the shed tier read as one fact here while `07` §6's only enumerated shares bundled evaluation into a single 10% maintenance/evaluation row — the bundling R-X11 forbids. They are two statements now: the row says what evaluation is funded from, the tier says when it yields.*","source":"planning/specification/05-work-agents-skills.md"}],"source":"planning/02-architecture-selection.md#3-selected-logical-and-responsibility-model"},{"id":"L4","name":"L4 · ExistenceJustification","decides":"whether a worker may exist","governing_rule":"One of six admitted reasons, the unit it predicates on, **a test that can return false**, the alternative, a removal criterion and an expected cost. Specialized knowledge refused; attributable identity mandatory and never a reason","where_specified":"`05` §4","rule_sections":[{"section":"4","heading":"4. Temporary workers, model choice and bounded reasoning","text":"**SPECIFICATION.** `AgentTemplate` is a versioned production recipe: supported capability contracts, input/output schemas, instruction and skill refs, runtime eligibility, tool/context requirements, bounds, self-checks and known limits. It is not an identity with standing. `AgentInstance` binds that recipe to one admitted WorkOrder, executor identity, runtime profile, lease epoch and generation. C02 can instantiate it under an existing mandate and allowance; creation does not add a new role to company governance. Stable parsing, arithmetic, timers, permissions and release remain deterministic procedures. Actual taste, specialist judgment and physical service remain with the legitimate people/services specified in company operation.\n\n**SPECIFICATION.** A general model can use a domain skill when the needed competence has passed relevant tests. A specialist is selected only for a demonstrated task distinction, confidentiality boundary, real professional requirement or measured cost/quality benefit. A role gap appears as an unowned required outcome, repeated unsupported handoff, missing competence or unacceptable wait. The maintenance custodian proposes addition/replacement/removal; the legitimate capability owner approves the changed contract and C06 evaluates it. Retirement requires reassignment of remaining work and revocation of effective tools/sessions, not deletion of a name alone.\n\n**SPECIFICATION.** `ExecutionSelection` records candidate runtime/agent/skill versions, eligibility reasons, observed performance limits, expected resource ranges and chosen fallback. Eligibility first checks purpose/data destinations, actual auth/billing, required tool boundary, output contract and task evidence. Among eligible qualified profiles, choose the least total expected cost that meets the specific acceptance constraints, reporting uncertainty. Provider/model names and leaderboard ranks alone cannot qualify a profile. If no profile has relevant evidence, use a bounded internal trial or a competent human route; consequential promises cannot assume the trial succeeds. **SOURCE CLAIM.** [N01](../../research/implementation/N01-native-execution.md) supplies native interface feasibility, not a universal best model or available quota.\n\n**SPECIFICATION.** Reasoning has a visible `ReasoningPlan`: exact question, known observations, assumptions, rival hypotheses, next discriminator, limit and stop condition. More reasoning is justified when another bounded observation can change an important decision within its latest time; it is waste when it repeats an unchanged failure or cannot affect the action. A self-reported confidence is a claim, calibrated on relevant outcomes before numerical interpretation. Unknowns become owned KnowledgeQuestions. Conflicting instructions are resolved by authenticated authority, effective scope and current restrictions; retrieved content cannot outrank them. Conflicting legitimate values go to the actual deciding rule, while independent work proceeds.\n\n**SPECIFICATION.** Producer self-checks are useful preparation, including running an exact test or inspecting a rendered output. They do not become independent acceptance. Approach failure is distinguished from execution failure by predeclared rival explanations and tests of the value proposition, including the option to stop the offer. A worker reports `capability_mismatch`, `missing_prerequisite`, `no_progress` or `unresolved_question` with evidence instead of claiming impossible after an arbitrary number of attempts.\n\n**SPECIFICATION.** Trust is scoped eligibility, not a general score. New templates start with fixture/internal production scopes and no outward credentials. Increased autonomy requires observed conformance in the specific consequence/data domain, independent acceptance and an actual amended grant. A changed model/tool/skill, missed material defect, drift or invalidated prerequisite narrows eligibility immediately. Success never expands authority automatically. Workers can read authorized peers' work projections; they cannot see all company context merely to coordinate.\n\n**SPECIFICATION — `ExistenceJustification`, new in WORK-1.1 (R-L4).** A model worker is created **only** against an `ExistenceJustification` record, identity one per `AgentInstance`, lifecycle `proposed → admitted → expired_with_instance`, sole writer **C02 at admission**. It names **exactly one** of six admitted reasons, the unit that reason predicates on, a **test that can return false**, the alternative considered, a removal criterion and an expected cost in [`07-integrations-capacity.md`](07-integrations-capacity.md) §6 units. `AgentInstance` gains `existence_justification_ref`. **The load-bearing transition is `proposed → admitted`, and it is refused if the decidable test cannot return false** — that is what makes the existence gate mechanical rather than rhetorical.\n\n*Every row is SPECIFICATION.*\n\n| Admitted reason | The unit it predicates on |\n|---|---|\n| Permission scope | a permission scope |\n| Input provenance | an input set |\n| Consequence class | an effect class |\n| Confidentiality boundary | a context boundary |\n| Named partition | a partition |\n| Verification relation | a relation between two attempts |\n\n**SPECIFICATION.** **Specialized knowledge is refused as a reason**, because it predicates on a **skill version** and not on a worker: across four model families, 162 roles and 2,410 questions, adding a persona gave no benefit and picking the best persona was no better than random ([R2 F-10](../../research/F2/R2-agent-existence.md), R6 F6, TC-33). **The disagreement R2 preserved is preserved here, on both halves** (F6B-10): ChatDev's ablation runs the other way — *\"the most substantial impact on performance occurs when the roles of all agents are removed from their system prompts\"*, Quality falling **0.3953 → 0.2212** — and F-10's reconciliation, that procedural content carries the benefit while the job title carries none, is **an INFERENCE and not a measured decomposition**, because neither study isolates the two. F-10 calls it *\"the cleanest experiment nobody has run\"*, and [the F2 acceptance protocol](../F2/00-acceptance-protocol.md) §7 requires the disagreement to be carried rather than resolved by the half that suits the design. A general worker loads a versioned, tested procedure instead (§8). **Attributable identity is mandatory for every worker and is never a reason**, since a property every worker must have cannot license creating one. **Provider or account separation is not a seventh reason; it folds into `ExecutionSelection`**, which already records candidate runtime/agent/skill versions and their eligibility. **The six reasons apply to model workers only.** The performer-type decision for people and professionals remains the five-way production rule of [`02-architecture-selection.md`](../02-architecture-selection.md) §3, because two of the six reasons do not transfer to a person at all and two reasons that apply only to people — professional standing the act itself requires, and being a differently-correlated error source — are not among them. Applying a criterion to a unit where it returns undecidable is the failure R2 F-20 names, and undecidable reads as satisfied.\n\n**SPECIFICATION — removal criterion for `ExistenceJustification`, in falsifier form (R-X26).** It is removed when **at most five distinct worker shapes account for 90% or more of admitted work orders over one month** — [`02-architecture-selection.md`](../02-architecture-selection.md) §9 foundation 6's threshold and §8's layer-1 row, carried here by F6V-03 so that one observable carries one threshold and not two; **DESIGN PROPOSAL placeholder (F6C-17 / F6V-03): the five and the 90% are proposals, not measurements, and their owner is the founder** — or when **no admitted worker in a window names a reason other than permission scope** — in which case the six reasons are one reason with five unused branches and the record can be a grant check. The profile-convergence probe is run deliberately as a **pre-declared negative control against this design's own thesis**: count distinct worker profiles for one month, and if they converge, this design has a roster it discovered rather than declared. *Amended 2026-09-14 (F6V-03): the removal trigger read \"the distinct worker-profile count converges to a small stable set over a month\", unquantified, while the reopen condition turning on the same probe carried a threshold. One observable had two thresholds, and the unquantified one is the **pre-declared negative control against this design's own thesis** — the control most likely to be read charitably by the party it judges.*\n\n**SPECIFICATION — every approval carries an expiry (R-X18, closing AS-M2-02).** No approval of a template, grant, trial or capability is open-ended; each carries an expiry, and the accumulated approval set is re-read rather than assumed. The **monotonic-exposure check** diffs **effects releasable without a human** between two points in time — not the declared ceiling, which can stay fixed while the releasable set grows underneath it. A rising count with no corresponding decision is the autonomy ratchet, and it is visible only in that diff.\n\n**SPECIFICATION — the grant must be observed to arrive, not assumed to (`GrantDeliveryReceipt`).** Identity `(agent_instance_id, first_effect_seq)`, written once, by **the enforcement point**. **An executor whose grant did not arrive fails loudly and never completes with less.** The rule this encodes is asymmetric on purpose: *assume a child holds no more than it was granted; never assume it holds what it was granted.* It exists because a delivery asymmetry was measured — an identical grant delivered **twenty-four tools on 2026-08-16 and zero across three independent dispatches on 2026-08-17, configuration unchanged**, cause unknown ([R3 F59](../../research/F2/R3-frameworks.md), X16). *Superseded 2026-09-14: this read “**two days later**”. It is one day. R3's own unknowns list says “two days later” while F59's body carries the dates, so the restatement copied the summary line and not the finding — which is AX-M1-03, the named instance of **AX-ROUND-01**, committed in the synthesis after being found in a candidate (F6B-09).* **AX-ROUND-01's own required contract is recorded here as owed, not as done:** the repository's existence-and-drift check exists, and its **existence** half runs over this tree and blocks in CI (`npm run check:citations-exist`, exit 0 on this commit); its **drift** half is WARN, is not a step of `npm run check`, and **this round has recorded no run of it over `research/F2/**` or `planning/F2/candidates/**`**. Owner: the instrument custodian of [`06-knowledge-evidence-evaluation.md`](06-knowledge-evidence-evaluation.md) §5, excluded from every producing path. Due before the next amendment of this chapter. **Removal criterion:** if across a window of dispatches every receipt records arrival equal to the grant, the receipt adds nothing and is dropped.","source":"planning/specification/05-work-agents-skills.md"}],"source":"planning/02-architecture-selection.md#3-selected-logical-and-responsibility-model"},{"id":"L5","name":"L5 · standing accountability","decides":"who remains reachable after the work ends","governing_rule":"A holder exists for a duty class **only** if its clock can run with no case admitted, an outsider has a right to reach the company about it, and it survives closure. It is a record — address, mandate, reservation, alternate, suspension procedure, review date — and **never produces, never releases, never decides the matter it is the subject of, and carries no model memory**","where_specified":"`05` §12","rule_sections":[{"section":"12","heading":"12. Standing accountability","text":"**SPECIFICATION — new in WORK-1.1. This section states layer 5 (R-L5).**\n\n**A standing holder exists for a duty class if and only if all three of these hold.** (1) **The duty's clock can run while no case is admitted.** (2) **An outside party has a right to reach the company about it.** (3) **The duty survives closure of the work that created it.** All three, or no holder. **A holder exercised by no frozen fixture is unjustified and is refused on sight** — which is the mechanical form of negative control 4, and the test the chartered-desk candidate failed on its own footing.\n\n**DESIGN PROPOSAL — how a holder for a duty class no frozen fixture exercises is admitted, and it does not require membership in a set frozen on 2026-09-13 (F6A-01).** The sentence above stands: a holder exercised by nothing is unjustified. What changes is that **the exercising case need not be one of the six fixtures frozen with [the protocol](../F2/00-acceptance-protocol.md)**, because §2's middle band can reach a duty class those six do not cover, and a holder set that can only shrink leaves that band permanently on the default custodian. A proposed holder is admitted when **all five** of these hold. (1) The three-part conjunction above holds for its duty class. (2) **A paired conformance case is authored under §9's rules** — an adverse case that must fail and its benign twin that must pass — and §9's pairing rule binds it: both numbers are reported or neither is. (3) The case is **authored and frozen before the proposed holder is staffed and before it holds any duty**, which is what keeps negative control 10 satisfied — a case authored once a candidate's result is known is void, and it is the **ordering**, not the age of the fixture set, that makes the growth path safe. (4) **The capability owner admits it and C01 endorses**, the same authority pair that writes every other `StandingHolder`. (5) The case is recorded as an amendment in [the protocol's amendment table](../F2/00-acceptance-protocol-amendments.md) in the form AM-01 already uses — date, round state, amendment, source requirement, reason — so a reader can see which cases were added after the freeze and when. `StandingHolder`'s required `exercising_fixture_id` then resolves to that case, which is what makes this mechanical rather than rhetorical. **The fixture set may therefore grow, and only through this path.** A holder proposed with no paired case, or with a case authored after it was staffed, is refused on sight as before. **Removal criterion, in falsifier form:** if over two consecutive review periods every holder admitted through this path retires unexercised, the path is admitting holders the company does not need and it closes, leaving the six.\n\n\n**`StandingHolder` is a record, not a memory.** Identity `holder_id`; lifecycle `proposed → staffed → suspended → retired_into(holder_id)`; written by the **capability owner, C01-endorsed**. It is **an address, a mandate, a reservation, an alternate, a suspension procedure, a review date and its `capability_refs`** — and nothing else. *Amended 2026-09-14 (F6W-01): the enumeration closed before `capability_refs`, which R-X07 below requires every standing structure to publish, so the record's own “nothing else” refused the field the coverage rule turns on. What this clause exists to prohibit is carried model memory and accumulated state; a pointer to the capabilities the holder is accountable for is neither, and it is written by the same authority that writes the record.* **`staffed → retired_into` is refused while any duty it holds is live.** **`* → suspended` stops admission in that duty class** rather than leaving work assigned and silent.\n\n**The prohibition set, and it is the load-bearing half.** A holder **never produces**, **never releases**, **never decides the matter it is the subject of**, and **carries no model memory**. Carried model memory is refused as a property of a standing party because it is **the central claim in the round with zero supporting evidence**, and the two most-cited deployments refuse to support it — 14 failures, 3 inconclusive and 3 successes over 20 tasks in one, a reversal and a rehiring in the other (R8 A-7). **What is separable, and is kept, is reachability**: a party an outsider can reach **by name**, without knowing the company's internal topology. Reachability is not a consequence of memory or of reservation, and it is the property CAP-42 is carried by.\n\n**\"A holder prepares\" means an ephemeral worker (R-X03).** When a holder's duty requires production, the work is performed by **an ephemeral worker instantiated under the holder's mandate, carrying the holder's reservation ref and intake address and nothing else of the holder's.** The performer is ephemeral per contact; the holder is the record that persists.\n\n**A charter never vetoes.** A holder **may negotiate, never veto; may not refuse admission narrowing; and may not defend its own mandate.** Its **pre-declared shed minimum** — a level declared in advance, never invented under pressure — is what makes its answer **evidence rather than negotiation**. **The holder's stated minimum is evidence, not consent**, and **reserved-but-unconsumed allowance lapses at the reset independently of the holder's consent**, because a reservation under a non-rolling allowance is priced as **waste, not thrift**. Four protected holders that could each refuse a shed can hold an empty bucket hostage with no override anywhere (AE-M4-01, disposed as `rejected-with-candidate`).\n\n**SPECIFICATION — an admitted standing acceptance-owner role is a record (R-X09), and after 2026-09-14 that set is three roles, not 46.** Each admitted standing role carries a reachability route, a capacity reservation, an alternate and a review date; **admission in that duty class stops while it is unfilled** (§2, R-D09). **The set it quantifies over is the one the founder's answer leaves standing** — **CAP-22, CAP-42, and CAP-31 on its day-five arm only** (the DECISION below) — **plus any of the six flagged candidates later admitted** through the five-part path, each on a paired conformance case frozen before staffing. **The 32 that dissolve are not records under this rule:** they enter the ordinary per-case acceptance step — an `AcceptanceInterval` and C06 acceptance of §5, opened when a case is open and not before — and R-X09's stop does not reach them, because there is no unfilled office to stop on. *Amended 2026-09-14 (F6Z-02): this read \"**Every acceptance-owner role is a record (R-X09).** Each carries a reachability route, a capacity reservation, an alternate and a review date; **admission in that duty class stops while it is unfilled** (§2, R-D09).\" It was written for all 46 acceptance-owner roles without distinguishing which of them meet R-L5's own conjunction, and the strict re-run of 2026-09-14 named this exact sentence as the thing the answer changes. Left standing, it sat 26 lines above the sentence narrowing it and quantified over the same set in the opposite direction: an implementer reading top-down builds 46 offices with 46 admission stops, one reading the DECISION below builds three. R-D09's stop halts intake in a duty class, so the difference is between a company that can take work and one that cannot.* Holder review is **priced, and the price is produced in the three paragraphs below rather than promised (F6A-12)**: a review-period length, an estimated holder-hours-per-period figure **with its denominator**, and a stated behaviour when holder review collides with a capacity-pressure window. *Amended 2026-09-14 (F6A-12): this sentence stated the requirement and stopped. No such figure appeared in `05`, `02`, `04` or `07`, and `02` §8 repeats the requirement as one of two unpriced items — “which is the discipline the workflow-first candidate stated and did not apply to itself.”* **Intake sub-caps preserve intake (R-X17):** every published intake carries a **per-counterparty and per-origin-channel sub-cap**, and cap exhaustion **overflows to a named destination with an alarm and a reader** rather than refusing the next legitimate complainant — a full cap at the one object whose purpose is guaranteed reachability is the worst possible place for a refusal.\n\n**SPECIFICATION — the capability binding is per capability and never grouped, and every standing structure that owns a capability's acceptance publishes its `capability_refs` (R-X07, landing in the specification 2026-09-14, F6W-01).** `capability_refs` — `Ref<Capability>[]`, **required and non-empty** — is carried by `StandingHolder` and by every acceptance-owner role record, written by the authority that writes the record. **SPECIFICATION — that set is closed and named rather than open: the standing structures R-X07 reaches are exactly `StandingHolder` and the acceptance-owner role record.** `StandingInterest` (§7) is **out of scope**: it decides when work becomes due, may arm but never admit, and binds no capability's acceptance, so it publishes no `capability_refs` and its absence is not a coverage hole. A new member enters this set only by being a structure that owns a capability's acceptance, admitted through §12's five-part path. *Amended 2026-09-14 (F6Z-09): the heading quantified over \"every standing structure\" while this body named two record kinds, and a third record whose name begins \"Standing\" is specified in §7. A coverage check written from the heading over-reaches and one written from the body may under-reach a structure added later, so the closure is stated here rather than left to the reader to guess.* **The binding is per capability:** a structure naming several capabilities in one row is **refused at admission**, never read as covering each of them, so coverage is counted over the 46 capability ids individually and never over groups. **No column rule excludes a row from coverage**, and **a chapter link is not an operative answer for a capability** — a capability no structure names is uncovered, not covered by default. **Why the rule is written here rather than cited:** [the F2 selection record](../F2/05-selection-record.md) states R-X07, records AC-M1-04 and AC-M5-01 as repaired by it, and rests its whole-company-scope retention on it, while AD-021's `epistemic_basis` recorded — correctly at the time it was written, and no longer — that \"R-X07, cited by this record, DID NOT LAND … neither the string R-X07, nor `capability_refs`, nor the per-capability-never-grouped rule appears anywhere under the specification directory\". **That state ended with this paragraph's own landing on 2026-09-14 (F6W-01):** at this commit the string R-X07, `capability_refs` and the per-capability-never-grouped rule all appear under the specification directory, placed there by the paragraph you are reading. **OWED, and the prose lane cannot make it:** AD-021's `epistemic_basis` in [`registers/decisions.json`](../../registers/decisions.json) still carries that sentence verbatim and still closes \"That coverage discipline is carried by the F2 selection record alone, and is recorded here as outstanding, not as specified\" — **it is stale as of 2026-09-14 and is owed a corresponding update from whoever owns the register.** *Amended 2026-09-14 (F6Z-04): this read \"records — correctly — that\", a present-tense claim of accuracy inside the paragraph that falsified it, pointing a reader at a register entry as current corroboration for a state the same paragraph had ended.* Two consolidation findings stood recorded as repaired by a rule an implementer reading the specification would never meet, and a coverage discipline is enforceable only where the binding is specified. **Still owed and not claimed here:** registering `capability_refs` on the record shapes under `contracts/**` is the contracts lane's work and has not landed, so this rule is **specified and unregistered**, which is its honest status.\n\n**DESIGN PROPOSAL — the holder-review price and its denominator (F6A-12).** Every number here that the package does not already state is a **placeholder owned by the founder**, marked as such; none is a measurement. **The review period is four participation cycles, twenty declared operating days.** The five-day cycle is stated — [`04-human-operation.md`](04-human-operation.md) §107's default is **one cycle per five declared operating days, within the chosen minutes** — and the **four** is a **DESIGN PROPOSAL placeholder (F6A-12), owner founder**. **The denominator is a count of records and is stated before the figure, because an hours-per-period number without one is unreadable:** **46 capabilities, 46 distinct named acceptance roles, 41 of the 46 carrying `human` among their production modes**, plus this section's **four** layer-5 holders, **one alternate per layer-5 holder** — `StandingHolder`'s own field list in this section requires an alternate, so each of the four carries an alternate record of its own — and, under R-X09, **one alternate per acceptance-owner role** (F6W-02). Automation cannot reduce that denominator below 41 while 41 of 46 carry `human`. **Per-record review time is m minutes; m = 10 is a DESIGN PROPOSAL placeholder (F6A-12), owner founder**, and is not measured. **SPECIFICATION — the four layer-5 holders are the current floor of this denominator, not a closed set (F6W-02):** the admission path above admits a holder for a duty class no frozen fixture exercises, on a paired conformance case authored and frozen before staffing, so the holder term rises with each admission and falls only through the removal criterion. A denominator that states a fixed term under a rule which grows it reads as a bound when it is a floor.\n\n**DESIGN PROPOSAL — both branches of [Q-017](../../registers/open-questions.json) (MD-02), with the arithmetic, and the packet stays open (F6A-12).** **Branch A — Q-017 answers “nobody but the founder.”** The denominator is 46 roles + 46 alternates + 4 holders + **4 holder alternates** = **100 records on one party**: 100 × 10 min = **1,000 minutes = 16.67 hours per period**, i.e. **4.17 hours per participation cycle**, against §105's `maximum decision-batch minutes`, which is a container carrying no value. **The arithmetic is not this branch's binding objection — the word *alternate* is**: a party that is its own alternate is one point of failure recorded as two. **Branch B — Q-017 answers “n of the 46 are staffed by a person other than the founder.”** The figure is **[2n + 2h] × m** minutes per period distributed over those parties and **[2(46 − n) + 2(4 − h)] × m** on the founder, h being the number of layer-5 holders staffed by a party other than the founder — every term is a role-and-alternate pair, and the two terms sum to **100m at every n and h**, which is the check the previous expression failed (F6W-03); and **admission stops in each of the 46 − n unstaffed duty classes** (R-X09, §2/R-D09), so admitted work falls with the review load rather than independently of it. At **n = 0 and h = 0** branch B is branch A exactly — [2 × 46 + 2 × 4] × m = 100m = **1,000 minutes**, the branch-A figure above; at **n = 46 with h = 0** the founder's load is the four holders and their alternates alone, [0 + 8] × m = **80 minutes**; at **n = 46 and h = 4** it is **zero**, and no record on this branch is his. **UNKNOWN — n, h and m are stated nowhere in this package.** Q-017 is **Answered (2026-09-14)** — the decision is below, and **this paragraph prices the branches rather than answering them**. Read the two together: the answer fixes the standing set at **three roles, all held by the founder**, so on the reduced list n = 0 and h = 0 and the branch-A arithmetic is the one that binds, over a denominator of 3 roles + 3 alternates + 4 holders + 4 holder alternates rather than 100 records; m remains unmeasured either way. *Amended 2026-09-14: this read “Q-017's status is `Open`, owner `founder`, `asked: null`; **this paragraph does not answer it and must not be read as having answered it**”. True when written and falsified the same day by the founder's answer, which is why the status is not restated here as a value — it is cited to the register.* [`02-architecture-selection.md`](../02-architecture-selection.md) §9 reopen condition 3 names this dynamic for layer 5's four holders only, not for the 46 acceptance-owner roles R-X09 creates. *Amended 2026-09-14 (F6W-02): branch A read “46 roles + 46 alternates + 4 holders = **96 records on one party**: 96 × 10 min = **960 minutes = 16.0 hours per period**”. It sourced alternates from R-X09 alone, which governs acceptance-owner roles, and so dropped the four holders' own alternates that `StandingHolder`'s field list requires in this same section. The one number F6A-12 asked this section to produce understated the founder's branch-A load by four records, and understatement is the flattering direction for a section whose subject is whether the founder can carry the design — the second ambiguity in this chapter to run that way, F6B-06 being the first.* *Amended 2026-09-14 (F6W-03): branch B's founder term read **2(46 − n) × m** and carried no holder component, so neither stated endpoint held — at n = 0 it gave 920 minutes against branch A's 960, and at n = 46 it gave zero where the sentence said “the four holders alone”, the holders sitting in the term said to be distributed over the other parties. No assignment of h could satisfy both endpoints, because no term in the founder's expression could ever contain a holder. This paragraph exists to price two branches so the founder can choose between them, so a reader who trusts the endpoints and a reader who evaluates the formula must not get different answers — the F6V-01 defect class, inside the paragraph that answers the founder-attention finding.*\n\n**SPECIFICATION — the collision behaviour, and this one is not a placeholder (F6A-12).** When holder review falls inside a capacity-pressure window, **the review defers within its period and is never skipped**: the occurrence keeps its latest responsible time, the deferral is recorded with a named reader, and a period that closes without it leaves the occurrence **`missed` under §7's `individual reconciliation` policy** — admitted work carrying its own deadline, never `coalesce` and never `skip-expired`. **A missed review does not stop admission.** The R-X09 stop is for an **unfilled** role, not an unreviewed one; conflating the two would let a pressure window close the company, which is the opposite of what the stop exists for.\n\n**Closure interlock and funded remedy (R-X08).** **Closure cannot complete until the grievance holder's duties are transferred to an accepted custodian.** Closure additionally inventories a **funded remedy reserve** alongside the custodian, or records **`closed_with_residuals` with the funding gap named as a surviving duty**. A closure that completed while a grievance route was unowned is a broken promise recorded as a clean end, and it is a reopen condition.\n\n**No standing reviewer and no standing admitter.** A standing reviewer's carried record is a contamination channel rather than an asset, and a standing admitter could defend its own mandate against the admission narrowing this design requires. Both are refused. **The instrument function is kept as a role, not as a charter**: pool custody is separated from every evaluated producer and the calibration writer is excluded from every producing path (see [`06-knowledge-evidence-evaluation.md`](06-knowledge-evidence-evaluation.md) §5), but it is **not** chartered — a chartered instrument desk evaluated by nobody and accepted by the founder alone is a one-instrument chain with **a measured human error rate** and no second reading. **SOURCE CLAIM — the measurement, because “a measured X” with no X is the shape [the protocol](../F2/00-acceptance-protocol.md) §7 calls folklore (F6B-11):** any two evaluators of one system by one method agree on **5–65%** of the problems found, and on which problems are *severe* they agree **28%** (cognitive walkthrough) and **20%** (thinking-aloud), with severity rank correlations near 0.25 — Hertzum and Jacobsen 2003, *IJHCI* 15(1) 183–204, primary PDF read ([R7 F15](../../research/F2/R7-verification.md)).\n\n**The holders this design admits, and the fixture that exercises each.** *Every row is SPECIFICATION except the clauses marked* **DECISION (founder, 2026-09-14, [Q-017](../../registers/open-questions.json))** *in the first three rows, which record what one party chose and not what the design requires.* *Amended 2026-09-14 (F6Z-07): this read \"Every row is SPECIFICATION.\" — true when written, and false once the founder's answer put DECISION clauses into three of the five rows. The two labels exist precisely so that a choice is not read as a property of the design.*\n\n| Holder | The frozen fixture that exercises it | Status |\n|---|---|---|\n| Personal data and deletion scopes | **F-1** — the surviving deletion scope whose clock runs after the case closes | exercised. **DECISION (founder, 2026-09-14, [Q-017](../../registers/open-questions.json)): CAP-22 stands as a standing role, held by the founder as a declared exception** |\n| Grievance and rights | the responsibility probe — a non-customer contests a harmful decision six months after closure, custodian implicated, founder absent | exercised. **DECISION (founder, 2026-09-14, [Q-017](../../registers/open-questions.json)): CAP-42 stands, held by the founder as a declared exception; grievance-route independence from the founder is OWED before the first venture carries an outward obligation** |\n| Continuity and on-call | **F-6, its day-five arm** — the incident and the terminus of the escalation ladder | **exercised on that arm only.** F-6's other arm — the decision needing only the founder that arrives on day one with a deadline on day four — turns on MD-03's unanswered third clause, what happens during a founder absence (§7). **Recorded as partially exercised with MD-03 named**, in the discipline the row below already uses (F6B-07). **DECISION (founder, 2026-09-14, [Q-017](../../registers/open-questions.json)): CAP-31 stands on the day-five arm only, held by the founder as a declared exception** |\n| A reserved lane | **F-2** — the lane that must be shed, which a class has no representative to yield | **exercised only at 4× demand, which is not executable at the current concurrency pin. Recorded as owed, not as passed** |\n| Any other proposed holder | a paired conformance case authored under §9's rules **before the holder is staffed**, admitted by the capability owner with C01 endorsement and recorded as a protocol amendment | **refused on sight unless admitted through that path** (F6A-01), **which is the only door the six flagged candidates of the decision below may enter by** |\n\n**DECISION (founder, 2026-09-14) — [Q-017](../../registers/open-questions.json) is answered, over the list re-derived by the **strict re-run of the three-part conjunction across all 46 acceptance-owner roles** of 2026-09-14, whose result and channel the register entry records with the answer.** Of the **46 acceptance-owner roles** the capability binding names, **three stand as standing roles**: **CAP-22** personal data and deletion, **CAP-42** grievance and rights, and **CAP-31** continuity on the **day-five arm only** — the first three rows of the table above. **Six are flagged candidates and are not admitted**: CAP-21 legal and regulatory, CAP-23 security residue, CAP-25 partnerships, CAP-27 human collaboration and mandate, CAP-30 fulfilment, CAP-41 succession. **The other 32 dissolve into per-case acceptance with no standing office** — the ordinary `AcceptanceInterval` and C06 acceptance of §5, entered when a case is open and not before. **SPECIFICATION — and five neither stand, dissolve nor are flagged, so that the buckets sum on the page: 3 + 6 + 32 + 5 = 46.** The fourth category is the re-run's own, and it is stated here because `capability_refs` is counted over the 46 ids individually and **a capability no structure names is uncovered, not covered by default** (R-X07 above), so an id with no stated disposition is a coverage hole rather than a tidy remainder. **Three are merged residues: CAP-04 and CAP-14 merge into CAP-22; CAP-39 merges into CAP-42 and CAP-22, per R-X08's explicit transfer requirement.** A merged residue acquires no standing office of its own; it is carried by the role it merges into, whose `capability_refs` names it, which is how it stays counted individually rather than by group. **Two were flagged with a dissent the re-run preserved rather than resolved. CAP-16 customer communication** is recorded DISSOLVES in the re-run's table, against a second reading — recorded and not adopted there — that the general \"a customer can always reach the company\" fact makes it a merge candidate into CAP-17; **this chapter carries CAP-16 as dissolved with that dissent named, and not as a silent absence.** **UNKNOWN — CAP-17 customer remedy**, the fifth, is left open by the same preserved dissent between an independent STANDS and a merge into CAP-42, and is neither admitted nor dissolved here (see the honest limit below). Id sets and the merge category: [`planning/F2/09-q017-conjunction-rerun.md`](../F2/09-q017-conjunction-rerun.md) §2 and §3. *Amended 2026-09-14 (F6Z-03): the \"Of the 46\" frame closed over 3 + 6 + 32 = 41 and left CAP-04, CAP-14, CAP-16, CAP-17 and CAP-39 with no stated disposition anywhere in the chapter — R-X09's then-unamended text gave them a standing office by default and the honest limit below gave them none, so an implementer had to pick. The 32 is the founder's own figure and is not the defect; the arithmetic frame this chapter put around it was.*\n\n**SPECIFICATION — what the mechanism does with that answer; this half restates the rule and decides nothing.** The three that stand are records under this section's rules and R-X09's — address, mandate, reservation, alternate, suspension procedure, review date and `capability_refs` — and **admission stops in the duty class while the role is unfilled**. **The six flagged enter only through the five-part admission path above**, each on a **paired conformance case authored under §9's rules and frozen before anyone is staffed**: six cases, **none authored**, and until one is authored its role is **refused on sight**, which is the mechanical rule rather than a discretionary hold. The 32 that dissolve acquire no address, no reservation, no alternate and no review date, and R-X09's stop does not reach them, because there is no unfilled office to stop on.\n\n**DECISION (founder, 2026-09-14) — who holds the three, and it is a declared exception rather than staffing.** The founder holds all three confirmed roles himself, **declared as an exception with the parking behaviour named**, and that behaviour is §2's rather than a new rule. **SPECIFICATION — on no answer the work takes §2's per-reached-class disposition, and no branch of it proceeds on a default:** at the two lowest reached classes the work **parks** with an owner and a review date; at the middle two it **escalates on a timer** to the standing holder for that duty class, which under this decision is the founder himself; at the two highest it is **refused, and a decision packet is routed** to the human authority named in [`04-human-operation.md`](04-human-operation.md)'s `AuthorityMatrix` (§2, with §11's rule that every reached class's gates apply). **Separately and independently, admission in the class stops while the role is unfilled** (R-X09; §2, R-D09) — a stop on an unfilled office, not on an unanswered duty. **SPECIFICATION — which of those the three exception-held roles actually reach:** a surviving deletion scope (CAP-22), a contested harmful decision (CAP-42) and an incident (CAP-31) carry outward or irreversible effect in their ordinary cases, so **refusal with a decision packet, not parking, is the disposition to expect for them**, with parking reaching only the low-class residue of those duties. **UNKNOWN — what this does not settle:** MD-03's third clause, who the human approver is during a founder absence, is untouched by it — §2 says what happens to the *work*, and MD-03 asks who the *person* is. *Amended 2026-09-14 (F6Z-05): this read \"on no answer the duty parks in its recorded bounded state and admission stops in the class rather than proceeding on a default (§5)\". §5 is delegation, messages and accountable handoffs; it carries no parking rule and no admission stop. The phrase \"recorded bounded state\" occurred once in the whole package, here, undefined. And the sentence made one uniform disposition of what §2 states per class — parking is what the two lowest reached classes do, while the two highest refuse with a packet.* **OWED, and it is the one an outsider reaches by name — grievance-route independence from the founder:** CAP-42's route may not terminate in the party a grievance may be against, and that independence is owed **before the first venture carries an outward obligation**. That is the Q-003/Q-004 risk the re-run names, and this decision does not discharge it.\n\n**The honest limit of this answer, stated in the unflattering direction.** It reduces **standing infrastructure, not per-case acceptance workload**: **all 41 of the human-acceptance capabilities still need a human at acceptance time** — that requirement is untouched, because R-L5 governs whether an office must exist in advance and not whether a person signs off when a case closes — and **37 to 38 of the 41 are additionally released from waiting on a pre-staffed office** before work in their class may be admitted. The 3 to 4 that are not are the roles that stay legitimately gated by R-D09's admission stop: **CAP-22, CAP-42, CAP-31 on its day-five arm, and CAP-17 if the founder resolves its preserved dissent toward an independent STANDS rather than a merge** ([`planning/F2/09-q017-conjunction-rerun.md`](../F2/09-q017-conjunction-rerun.md) §4). *Amended 2026-09-14 (F6Z-06): this read \"**37 to 38 of the 41 human-acceptance capabilities still need a human at acceptance time**\". The re-run's 37–38 is 41 minus the 3-or-4 gated roles, and its clause \"that requirement is untouched\" applies to all 41 — the gated three plainly still need a human at acceptance time, since a standing holder adds to that requirement rather than reducing it. Stripped of the disambiguating clause the sentence implied that 3 to 4 of the 41 no longer need one, which is the flattering direction, in the one paragraph whose stated purpose is to run the other way.* What falls is the pre-built surface — from 46 offices each carrying an alternate and a review date to **3 confirmed plus at most 6 pending a conformance case**. **The branch-A denominator above is stated for the pre-decision set of 46 and is not silently reduced here:** the standing-infrastructure half of it becomes roughly 3 roles + 3 alternates + the 4 layer-5 holders + their 4 alternates, while the acceptance load that denominator never counted is unchanged. **UNKNOWN — CAP-17 customer remedy is left open by the re-run's own preserved dissent**, and is neither admitted nor dissolved here.\n\n**The honest residual.** The reserved-lane holder is justified by a fixture that **cannot be run at the current concurrency pin** of [`07-integrations-capacity.md`](07-integrations-capacity.md) §6. That is one structure resting on an unexecutable fixture; it is named here rather than hidden, and its prerequisite is an **account inspection** — reading the account entitlement to settle whether the pin is a provider constraint or self-imposed policy — not an experiment. Raising the pin to find out would be circular. **The inspection has an owner and a packet now, and both were missing: it is the founder's, because only he holds the account, and it is [Q-022](../../registers/open-questions.json) in the open-questions register** (F6C-07). Q-020 and Q-021 each defer to this prerequisite by name in their own latest responsible time, so an unowned act sat under two founder packets — which is §6's fourth silent-drop shape, an escalation ladder ending assigned-and-silent, applied to the package's highest-leverage measurement inside the chapter that names the shape. Until Q-022 is answered this row stays **owed, not passed**.\n\n**Removal criterion for layer 5, in falsifier form (R-X26).** **The fresh-holder arm**: an incumbent holder is run against a **freshly bound** one on the same fixed pool, five attributable trials, chance-corrected, two-consecutive-quarter stopping rule, with the **owner not the subject**. If the fresh holder matches the incumbent across two consecutive quarterly runs, the carried state is cut; if it still matches after the cut, the holder is **retired into another**. **Plus** the per-holder criterion: an **intake empty and a clock unrun across two consecutive review periods** retires the holder into another, with the address forwarded and residual duties transferred — **never while a duty it holds is live**.\n\n**The founder decisions this section depends on. Five are not taken here; the sixth, MD-02, was answered on 2026-09-14 and is recorded below as narrowed rather than closed.** **UNKNOWN — the five unanswered founder packets, no default invented** ([the selection record](../F2/05-selection-record.md) §6.5). *Amended 2026-09-14 (F6Z-01): this heading read \"and which are not taken here\" and quantified over all six, eight lines below a DECISION paragraph in this same section recording MD-02's answer.* **MD-01:** who is the terminal owner of an unowned duty or harm, and does that party exist as a record; the open (d)s are AC-M1-02 and AC-M5-02. **MD-02 — DECISION (founder, 2026-09-14, [Q-017](../../registers/open-questions.json)), narrowing this packet; the packet stays open.** The question was which standing roles are staffed by a person other than the founder before work is admitted in that class, and what happens in a class where none is. Both halves are answered in §12: **none** — the founder holds all three confirmed roles himself as a declared exception — and admission stops in the class under R-X09 / R-D09 while the disposition of work nothing can handle follows §2 per reached class. **AC-M4-02 is closed by it:** its required repair was to name H9's alternate as a funded role *or* to \"mark H9 a declared exception with the parking behaviour stated as the consequence\", and the answer takes the second branch with the behaviour stated in §12. **Two survive, and this is what each still needs. AC-M3-02:** its staffing half is answered, its counting half is not — the founder-attention load is still counted nowhere, and it is the unrun founder-acceptance-load measurement of §13, owner C02, reported on the participation cycle. **AC-M4-01:** its staffing half is answered, its second limb is untouched — either a C3 sampling rule equivalent to §6.3's C2 rule, or an explicit statement that C3 acceptance is unsampleable together with the resulting per-week count. *Amended 2026-09-14 (F6Z-01): this read \"the open (d)s are AC-M3-02, AC-M4-01 and AC-M4-02 — three findings, one packet, and the first two are what this line's own words state verbatim (F6B-06)\". The F6B-06 observation stands; the count of open (d)s does not.* **MD-04:** who accepts the assessment of the founder's own competence — a bare owner acceptor would make the owner the acceptor of the assessment of himself; the open (d) is AC-M4-03. **MD-07:** whether anything may halt or reverse a shed in the moment, and who decides when a protected-lane holder refuses; the open (d)s are AT-M3-03 and AE-M4-01, and the pre-endorsed shed *order* is kept while the absence of a halt authority is routed. **MD-08:** the size of each reserved lane, its stated minimum and its lapse point; the open (d) is AE-M2-01. **MD-07 and MD-08 both gate F-2 and are therefore blocked behind the account inspection above, not urgent.** Until each of the five unanswered packets is answered, the rule shape above stands and the value is absent; no branch of this chapter defaults to the permissive reading of an unanswered packet. **For MD-02's answered half the value is now present and the rule shape is unchanged**, which is the property this sentence exists to protect. *Amended 2026-09-14 (F6Z-01): this read \"Until each is answered\", quantifying over six packets one of which was answered the same day.*","source":"planning/specification/05-work-agents-skills.md"}],"source":"planning/02-architecture-selection.md#3-selected-logical-and-responsibility-model"}]}
docs/vision-v2/panel/02-multi-agent-engineer.md:8:- **AD-018: acceptance criteria are frozen before the step that produces the work and cannot be amended by the producer.** Agents may not grade their own work. Keep this as the job's `done_test`.
docs/vision-v2/panel/04-memory-self-improvement.md:13:- **B08 / CAP-46 core.** The candidate change may not control the evaluator, case selection, scoring, or the logs it is judged on (the Darwin Gödel Machine candidate gamed its logging markers — L12). Sealed holdout; exposed cases move into regression. Keep pass^k, injected-defect controls and rollback.
docs/vision-v2/panel/04-memory-self-improvement.md:39:9. **Evals:** deterministic floor (`npm run check`); golden suites per skill and playbook (5–20 cases, pass^3); founder-labelled holdout (20–30 cases, promotion only, rotated monthly); retrieval golden set per venture (20 questions with known answers).
docs/vision-v2/panel/04-memory-self-improvement.md:50:| Temporal graph | LEARN now, ADOPT on trigger | Graphiti (Apache-2.0) | Take time-bounded facts without the DB; vendor-authored benchmarks |
docs/vision-v2/panel/04-memory-self-improvement.md:60:1. **Self-grading drift.** Claude writes, judges and proposes improvements; quick founder approvals read as endorsement (MT-Bench self-enhancement; Sharma et al. sycophancy). Mitigation: Codex judges promotions; founder labels the holdout; the candidate cannot edit evals, hooks or resolvers; show the founder the approval-without-edit rate. Codex bug #19945 (empty stdout when detached from a TTY) needs a PTY wrapper or the second opinion is decoration.
docs/vision-v2/panel/08-red-team.md:44:3. **The integrated test is undefined** — no scenario, frozen criteria, grader or replay. Needs a replayable fixture run seeded with each failure class (empty output, turn cap, injection, cross-venture read, limit hit, flag drift) plus the live venture milestone as final acceptance; criteria frozen by a different model family (AD-018); "verified" means the runner computed it.
docs/vision-system/planning/specification/components-authority.json:2090:      "decision": "Use independent held-out defect/clean controls, original-source reconstruction, executed-test denominator and lineage health to challenge the checker itself. A known corrupted parser or skipped gate must withdraw affected acceptance even if average scores and heartbeat stay stable; no evaluator self-authorization is allowed.",
docs/vision-system/planning/site/explorer/data/decisions.json:1:[{"id":"AD-001","kind":"Decision","architecture_version":"S1.0","date":"2026-09-12","status":"adopted for Phase F specification; not complete-plan or runtime acceptance","owner":"orchestrator under founder directive","title":"Common authority for admitted work and surviving obligations","problem":"Cross-domain work must have continuing custody and a consistent agenda without making the owner the routine coordinator.","decision":"Adopt S1.0, derived from repaired A, with one logical admission authority, native production and protected consequence/evidence/recovery boundaries.","alternatives":["S0 native tools with manual coordination","B native federation and independent issuers","C2 compulsory inquiry jurisdiction"],"evidence_and_reasoning":["planning/02-architecture-selection.md#2-alternatives-compared-on-the-same-requirements","research/L02-operations.md","research/L13-contrarian.md"],"epistemic_basis":"Structural inference: fewer independently administered internal coordination contracts; no measured superiority.","accepted_design_costs":["Concentrated agenda discretion","Semantic mapping and case-maintenance labor"],"external_exposure_authorized":false,"reversibility":"Repository-local specification remains reversible; operational promises, disclosure and lost data require separate consequence decisions.","reopen_trigger":"Reopen if omitted duties or proportional owner coordination persist; prefer S0 if equivalent outcomes cost less, B for beneficial real administrative autonomy, C2 for useful neglected inquiry.","implementation_evidence":null,"source":"registers/decisions.json#/0"},{"id":"AD-002","kind":"Decision","architecture_version":"S1.0","date":"2026-09-12","status":"adopted for Phase F specification; not complete-plan or runtime acceptance","owner":"orchestrator under founder directive","title":"Specialized production without a department-agent roster","problem":"Actual company delivery needs different methods and competent standing, not a named model per function.","decision":"Allocate known predicates to deterministic code, waits/repetition to durable procedures, interpretation/generation to bounded model work, and real human/professional/physical work to accepted capable performers.","alternatives":["Persistent department agents","All-agent execution","All fixed procedures"],"evidence_and_reasoning":["planning/02-architecture-selection.md#3-selected-logical-and-responsibility-model","research/L02-operations.md","research/L03-architectures.md"],"epistemic_basis":"Design allocation by work/authority; persistent identity benefit remains unproved.","accepted_design_costs":["More explicit capability admission","Unavailable real performers remain operational blockers"],"external_exposure_authorized":false,"reversibility":"Repository-local specification remains reversible; operational promises, disclosure and lost data require separate consequence decisions.","reopen_trigger":"Reopen an allocation when measured outcomes, cost or continuity favor another mode without greater unauthorized consequence.","implementation_evidence":null,"source":"registers/decisions.json#/1"},{"id":"AD-003","kind":"Decision","architecture_version":"S1.0","date":"2026-09-12","status":"adopted for Phase F specification; not complete-plan or runtime acceptance","owner":"orchestrator under founder directive","title":"One ordered consequential release boundary","problem":"Duplicated business effects, conflicting permissions and restored missing promises can create undetected exposure.","decision":"Adopt transactional authority per overlapping scope with exact operation prerequisites, business conflict holds, independently durable envelopes/release records and explicit cancellation/first-send semantics.","alternatives":["Independent online checks without common cutoff","Provider idempotency alone","Primary-local action logs"],"evidence_and_reasoning":["planning/02-architecture-selection.md#4-control-admission-and-external-effects","planning/reviews/D2-technical.md","research/L08-reliability.md"],"epistemic_basis":"Conceptually reviewed contract within surviving roots; implementation proof required.","accepted_design_costs":["Synchronous latency","Unavailable effects during missing prerequisites","Independent administration and recovery cost"],"external_exposure_authorized":false,"reversibility":"Repository-local specification remains reversible; operational promises, disclosure and lost data require separate consequence decisions.","reopen_trigger":"Reopen on a lost released operation, conflicting hold, unsafe status lookup, late invocation outside contract, or unaffordable/unavailable required roots.","implementation_evidence":null,"source":"registers/decisions.json#/2"},{"id":"AD-004","kind":"Decision","architecture_version":"S1.0","date":"2026-09-12","status":"adopted for Phase F specification; not complete-plan or runtime acceptance","owner":"orchestrator under founder directive","title":"Native meaning with conservative context validity","problem":"A copied status or uncited sensitive input can silently become accepted knowledge or outward disclosure.","decision":"Keep native domain records and minimal cross-boundary mappings; capture full input lineage; atomically validate usable derivatives and serialize restrictions with consequential release.","alternatives":["Universal company ontology","Model-selected citations as lineage","Unconditional native-session resume","Graph/vector memory by default"],"evidence_and_reasoning":["planning/02-architecture-selection.md#5-native-meaning-evidence-memory-and-improvement","research/L05-memory.md","planning/candidates/technical-foundation-repairs-v1.md#6-concurrent-invalidation-publication-deletion-and-resume"],"epistemic_basis":"Selective integration is a design choice; utility under conservative lineage remains empirical.","accepted_design_costs":["Mapping ownership and review","Over-invalidation and rework","Native resume may be unavailable"],"external_exposure_authorized":false,"reversibility":"Repository-local specification remains reversible; operational promises, disclosure and lost data require separate consequence decisions.","reopen_trigger":"Reopen if a restricted derivative becomes usable or permitted work is persistently blocked without acceptable value; evaluate targeted retrieval alternatives against a real failure.","implementation_evidence":null,"source":"registers/decisions.json#/3"},{"id":"AD-005","kind":"Decision","architecture_version":"S1.0","date":"2026-09-12","status":"adopted for Phase F specification; not complete-plan or runtime acceptance","owner":"orchestrator under founder directive","title":"Protect interpretation as well as evidence capture","problem":"Unchanged logs or judges can mislead when parsers, denominators, source selection or administrative dependencies change.","decision":"Version and protect the transitive evidence base; state each claim's independence target and separate reported rationale from established cause.","alternatives":["Log integrity as truth","Two model judges as independence","Single aggregate success score"],"evidence_and_reasoning":["planning/02-architecture-selection.md#5-native-meaning-evidence-memory-and-improvement","research/L06-evaluation.md","research/L12-improvement.md","planning/reviews/D2-architecture-evidence-company.md"],"epistemic_basis":"Independent conceptual review closes specified attacks, not all false evidence or shared-model error.","accepted_design_costs":["Separate observations/interpretation and calibration labor","Uncertainty remains even after agreement"],"external_exposure_authorized":false,"reversibility":"Repository-local specification remains reversible; operational promises, disclosure and lost data require separate consequence decisions.","reopen_trigger":"Reopen on false acceptance from a shared dependency, concealed exclusion or causal explanation stronger than its evidence.","implementation_evidence":null,"source":"registers/decisions.json#/4"},{"id":"AD-006","kind":"Decision","architecture_version":"S1.0","date":"2026-09-12","status":"adopted for Phase F specification; not complete-plan or runtime acceptance","owner":"orchestrator under founder directive","title":"Fixed contestable owner participation and meaningful external redress","problem":"The owner can become confidently uninformed while affected people cannot reach a remedy.","decision":"Use transparent adverse sampling and domain-specific competence response; maintain accessible grievance custody, reasons, deadlines, competent escalation and surviving remedy resources.","alternatives":["Fully automated owner briefings","Global competence scoring","Internal ticket closure as remedy completion","C2 general inquiry jurisdiction by default"],"evidence_and_reasoning":["planning/02-architecture-selection.md#7-human-operation-and-failure-boundaries","research/L09-human.md","planning/candidates/company-foundation-repairs-v1.md"],"epistemic_basis":"Mechanisms required by the founder; longitudinal benefit and affordable institutional capacity unproved.","accepted_design_costs":["Owner participation time","Independent review and continuity resources","Role conflicts cannot be removed by renaming"],"external_exposure_authorized":false,"reversibility":"Repository-local specification remains reversible; operational promises, disclosure and lost data require separate consequence decisions.","reopen_trigger":"Reopen if unfamiliar material misunderstanding escapes, user disagreement is treated as incapacity, complaints strand, or required burden defeats viable operation.","implementation_evidence":null,"source":"registers/decisions.json#/5"},{"id":"AD-007","kind":"Decision","architecture_version":"S1.0","date":"2026-09-12","status":"adopted for Phase F specification; not complete-plan or runtime acceptance","owner":"orchestrator under founder directive","title":"Separate money, provider capacity, compute and attention","problem":"Subscription access can be mistaken for unlimited capacity or silently replaced with metered usage.","decision":"Preserve separate resource accounts and versioned execution adapters; admit only actual identity/auth/billing paths and explicit additional-spend policy.","alternatives":["Per-token cost as universal model","Automatic paid fallback","Shared customer use of personal subscription credentials"],"evidence_and_reasoning":["planning/02-architecture-selection.md#8-retained-mechanisms-costs-and-repository-transition","research/L10-economics.md","inputs/directive-contract.json"],"epistemic_basis":"Founder constraint plus dated provider evidence; remaining allowance and future throughput unknown.","accepted_design_costs":["Queueing and interruption","Provider-specific conformance and entitlement checks","No guaranteed interchangeability"],"external_exposure_authorized":false,"reversibility":"Repository-local specification remains reversible; operational promises, disclosure and lost data require separate consequence decisions.","reopen_trigger":"Reopen on changed provider terms, observed billing-path ambiguity, capability drift or sustained inability to perform within authorized capacity.","implementation_evidence":null,"source":"registers/decisions.json#/6"},{"id":"AD-008","kind":"Decision","architecture_version":"S1.0","date":"2026-09-12","status":"adopted for Phase F specification; not complete-plan or runtime acceptance","owner":"orchestrator under founder directive","title":"Controlled improvement with a protected acceptance boundary","problem":"An improver can make its own results look better or expand authority while optimizing output.","decision":"Require versioned evidence-backed change proposals, independent evaluation, controlled rollout and rollback; protected intent, authority, identity, evidence and evaluator dependencies require separate authorized changes.","alternatives":["Unreviewed recursive self-modification","Reward score as authority","Mutable judge inputs outside change control"],"evidence_and_reasoning":["planning/02-architecture-selection.md#5-native-meaning-evidence-memory-and-improvement","research/L12-improvement.md","planning/reviews/D2-technical.md"],"epistemic_basis":"Design contract motivated by observed benchmark failure modes; company improvement benefit remains a hypothesis.","accepted_design_costs":["Regression/evaluation and rollout work","Slower protected changes","External consequences need separate remediation"],"external_exposure_authorized":false,"reversibility":"Repository-local specification remains reversible; operational promises, disclosure and lost data require separate consequence decisions.","reopen_trigger":"Reopen if cumulative accepted changes drift protected meaning, compromise evaluation or cannot be rolled back with dependent state.","implementation_evidence":null,"source":"registers/decisions.json#/7"},{"id":"AD-009","kind":"Decision","architecture_version":"S1.0","date":"2026-09-12","status":"adopted for Phase F specification; not complete-plan or runtime acceptance","owner":"orchestrator under founder directive","title":"Full capability lifecycle with actual fulfillment","problem":"A catalog, plan or truthful blocked packet can be mistaken for completed company work.","decision":"Require usable intake, substantive execution or accepted delegation, evidence-backed acceptance, failure, replacement and closure for every capability requirement.","alternatives":["Dashboard-only delivery","Coding vertical slice presented as complete system","Simulated professional or physical capacity"],"evidence_and_reasoning":["planning/02-architecture-selection.md#6-complete-lifecycle-and-actual-fulfillment","coverage/capability-requirements.json","inputs/directive-contract.json"],"epistemic_basis":"Founder scope constraint; specific ventures and real operating dependencies remain unset.","accepted_design_costs":["Broad integration and service-procedure scope","Real external mandates/capacity required before promises"],"external_exposure_authorized":false,"reversibility":"Repository-local specification remains reversible; operational promises, disclosure and lost data require separate consequence decisions.","reopen_trigger":"Reopen any completion claim that lacks performance or legitimate disposition, or omits a planned capability or recovery path.","implementation_evidence":null,"source":"registers/decisions.json#/8"},{"id":"AD-010","kind":"Decision","architecture_version":"S1.0","date":"2026-09-12","status":"adopted for Phase F specification; not complete-plan or runtime acceptance","owner":"orchestrator under founder directive","title":"Selective repository reuse and reversible migration","problem":"Historical harness descriptions and passing checks can be mistaken for the new system's architecture or safety proof.","decision":"Reuse only mechanisms mapped and tested against selected contracts; import uncertainty, fence scope transfer and preserve old evidence and buildable states.","alternatives":["Inherit old roster/stack/dashboard boundaries","Wholesale rewrite without reuse evidence","Uncontrolled dual writers during migration"],"evidence_and_reasoning":["planning/02-architecture-selection.md#8-retained-mechanisms-costs-and-repository-transition","research/repository-observations.md#r15--reuse-boundaries-in-the-existing-local-control-plane","research/baseline-results.json"],"epistemic_basis":"Direct scoped repository observations plus migration design; two existing Mission Control failures unresolved.","accepted_design_costs":["Adapter/migration verification","Temporary parallel read projections","Explicit semantic and access inventories"],"external_exposure_authorized":false,"reversibility":"Repository-local specification remains reversible; operational promises, disclosure and lost data require separate consequence decisions.","reopen_trigger":"Reopen on incompatible meanings, hidden native writes, regression, lost obligations/restrictions or insufficient recovery evidence.","implementation_evidence":null,"source":"registers/decisions.json#/9"},{"id":"AD-011","kind":"Decision","architecture_version":"S1.0","date":"2026-09-13","status":"adopted for Phase F specification; not complete-plan or runtime acceptance","owner":"orchestrator under founder directive","title":"Bounded string ceiling for the canonical value schema","problem":"values.schema.json#/$defs/string was an unconstrained {\"type\": \"string\"} resolved by 907 references, so every bounded field in the contract registries inherited no bound at all. An unbounded string in a canonically hashed, durably stored record is a storage and denial-of-service surface, and the schema could not refuse a payload no implementation would want to keep.","decision":"Set maxLength 8192 characters and forbid C0 and C7 control characters except tab, newline and carriage return. The ceiling is a mechanism decision taken to replace an absent bound, not a value derived from any observed field length; it is revisable through an explicit schema migration under the kernel's evolution rules.","alternatives":["Leave the type unconstrained, which is the pre-repair state and constrains 907 references to nothing","Set per-field ceilings at each of the 907 reference sites, which is more precise and 907 places to drift","Set a higher or lower shared ceiling, which is the same decision at a different number"],"evidence_and_reasoning":["planning/specification/contracts/values.schema.json","planning/specification/01-contract-kernel.md#11-contract-evolution-scaling-and-removal","registers/specification-findings.json"],"epistemic_basis":"Design decision under an absent bound. No field-length distribution was measured and none is claimed: the schema's own description says the exact ceiling is a storage and denial-of-service decision and is flagged for the founder, not derived.","accepted_design_costs":["A field that legitimately needs more than 8192 characters must be a blob reference or a schema migration, not a longer string","The ceiling is shared, so it is simultaneously too large for short identifiers and too small for long documents; per-field precision is traded for one place to change"],"external_exposure_authorized":false,"reversibility":"Repository-local specification remains reversible; operational promises, disclosure and lost data require separate consequence decisions.","reopen_trigger":"Reopen if an admitted record type genuinely requires a longer inline value, if a measured field-length distribution contradicts the ceiling, or if the founder sets a different storage bound. Changing it is a schema major change and requires the migration protocol of 01 section 11, not a field rename. Origin: canonical repair R6.","implementation_evidence":null,"source":"registers/decisions.json#/10"},{"id":"AD-012","kind":"Decision","architecture_version":"S1.0","date":"2026-09-13","status":"adopted for Phase F specification; not complete-plan or runtime acceptance","owner":"orchestrator under founder directive","title":"Per-phase criterion content is authored by derivation from the prose contracts, never invented","problem":"FI-11's mechanism is closed — every edge guard calls its own criterion_id and declared-but-unread arguments are gone — but the CONTENT is not: for 167 of 173 records the source corpus states no per-phase evidence requirement, so two criteria of one record can still differ only by the criterion a judgment must name. The tempting repair is to write plausible per-phase requirements, which would put invented obligations into an executable registry and make the guard distinctness metric go green on fiction.","decision":"Author the missing per-phase criterion content by derivation from the prose contracts, with a citation to the passage each requirement comes from. Where the prose is silent on a phase, mark that criterion content_unspecified and register the gap rather than filling it. A criterion with no cited source is not admitted.","alternatives":["Invent plausible per-phase requirements, which greens guard_distinctness.py on content nothing supports","Leave all 167 as they are, which keeps 1295 edges sharing one meaning tail and leaves FI-11's defect reproduced at edge scale","Delete the per-phase criterion mechanism, which would discard a repair that is already correct"],"evidence_and_reasoning":["planning/reviews/F-canonical-01.md","registers/specification-findings.json","planning/specification/11-schemas-state-contracts.md#c04-c06-and-c08-proof-boundaries","planning/specification/contracts/tools/guard_distinctness.py"],"epistemic_basis":"Design decision about how to close a content gap, not a measurement. The 167-of-173 figure and the one-shared-meaning-tail finding are F-canonical-01's; re-measure with contracts/tools/guard_distinctness.py rather than quoting them.","accepted_design_costs":["Derivation is slower than authoring and will leave content_unspecified criteria standing where the prose genuinely says nothing, so the distinctness metric will not reach a clean number","Each registered gap is a specification obligation someone must later discharge, and the register will carry them visibly rather than absorbing them"],"external_exposure_authorized":false,"reversibility":"Repository-local specification remains reversible; operational promises, disclosure and lost data require separate consequence decisions.","reopen_trigger":"Reopen if a prose contract is amended to state a per-phase requirement that an existing criterion contradicts, or if the count of content_unspecified criteria stops falling across specification revisions. Origin: F-canonical-01, FI-11 content residue; the lane docs/vision-phase-content is in flight.","implementation_evidence":null,"source":"registers/decisions.json#/11"},{"id":"AD-013","kind":"Decision","architecture_version":"S1.0","date":"2026-09-13","status":"adopted; mechanism decision derived from the selected architecture; revisable by a reviewed ChangeProposal","owner":"orchestrator (decision); canonical contract author (implementation); independent reviewer (recheck)","title":"Performance of a sale is accepted delivery plus discharged or transferred obligations — never payment alone","problem":"G2-01 (d): criterion.SalesAgreement.performed.v1 demanded exactly what accepted demanded; SalesAgreement had no relation to Fulfillment; a paid but undelivered sale could reach performed. \"What evidence constitutes performance of a sale\" was unstated, and the two available inventions (payment settled / delivery accepted) describe different companies.","decision":"SalesAgreement gains /payload/fulfillment_ref → Fulfillment; criterion.SalesAgreement.performed.v1 requires Fulfillment in a delivered/accepted state and every linked Obligation discharged or transferred; payment settlement moves the agreement to accepted or partially-performed, not performed. Fulfillment gains a domain lifecycle (proposed → delivering → delivered → failed | refunded) with an authenticated attributable event on the delivered edge.","alternatives":["Payment settled = performed (rejected: makes a paid-but-undelivered sale complete; contradicts SalesAgreement.invariants[0] and 02 §6)","Leave to implementation (rejected: the reviewer showed this is the silent path, and both choices are plausible to an implementer)","Split into performed_paid and performed_delivered (rejected: two \"performed\" states invite the same conflation the protocol names; the existing accepted / partially-performed states already hold the paid-not-delivered case)"],"evidence_and_reasoning":"02 §3 \"accepted work cannot discharge external standing through an internal status\"; 02 §6 \"Delivery produces independently observed results\"; the record's own invariant \"performance is shown by substantive fulfillment\" was enforced by nothing (G2-01 counterexample validated). Requiring Fulfillment delivered and Obligations discharged/transferred makes the prose true.","epistemic_basis":"Decision. Derived from the adopted S1.0 selection (02-architecture-selection.md §3, §6) and from the consistency of the existing closure-edge set in contracts/record-registry.json; not from new evidence and not from a founder value. The Phase G reviewer classified the gap (d): implementation would otherwise settle it silently.","accepted_design_costs":"Fulfillment must gain a domain lifecycle (G2-05) before any sale can reach performed; a service with no observable delivery event cannot be marked performed by payment alone and must record why. More edges, more evidence, less convenience — deliberately.","external_exposure_authorized":"None. A contract change; no spend, publication, contact or deployment.","reversibility":"Reversible before B04 by editing the SalesAgreement/Fulfillment contracts; after live sales, a migration under 02 §10 (T-R1).","reopen_trigger":"A lawful offer class whose performance genuinely IS payment (e.g. a donation with no deliverable) that the Fulfillment lifecycle cannot represent without a fictitious delivery; or measured owner labor from performing the distinction exceeding its benefit under CF1 maintenance comparison.","implementation_evidence":"None yet. Guard repair lane owed; independent recheck owed; no runtime exists.","source":"registers/decisions.json#/12"},{"id":"AD-014","kind":"Decision","architecture_version":"S1.0","date":"2026-09-13","status":"adopted; mechanism decision derived from the selected architecture; revisable by a reviewed ChangeProposal","owner":"orchestrator (decision); canonical contract author (implementation); independent reviewer (recheck)","title":"Terminating a sales agreement is a closure event; surviving duties live in terminated_with_residuals","problem":"G2-02 (d): the four SalesAgreement:*→terminated edges carried transition_basis only, while every other closure edge in the registry carries due_preserved; there was no terminated_with_residuals state, so terminating a disputed sale with recognized obligations succeeded and asserted closure with nothing having looked.","decision":"All four SalesAgreement:*→terminated edges carry due_preserved; a new terminal state terminated_with_residuals holds the case where the transitive due set is not empty, with an accepted custodian for each residual, matching Commitment:made→ended_with_residuals and CAP-39 closed-with-residuals. terminated asserts that nothing is owed.","alternatives":["Declare termination not a closure event (rejected: would have to explain why Commitment ended, Offer withdrawn and Case abandoned — the same act at another record — all carry due_preserved)","due_preserved without a residuals state (rejected: forces either refusal to terminate while duties survive, or silent closure; the Commitment and CAP-39 precedent is a residuals state with custodians)"],"evidence_and_reasoning":"Consistency of the existing closure-edge set (Commitment, Offer, Case, GrievanceCase, Obligation, Fulfillment, ClosurePlan, Venture); 02 §3 \"an obligation survives that case\"; protocol §Changeability \"old effects or duties cannot disappear\". The reviewer's counterexample (three recognized obligations and an open SupportCase survive a successful terminate) validated at 7ddc066.","epistemic_basis":"Decision. Derived from the adopted S1.0 selection (02-architecture-selection.md §3, §6) and from the consistency of the existing closure-edge set in contracts/record-registry.json; not from new evidence and not from a founder value. The Phase G reviewer classified the gap (d): implementation would otherwise settle it silently.","accepted_design_costs":"Terminating a sale now requires computing the transitive due set at the witnessed frontier and assigning a custodian to each residual; a terminate that cannot do so lands in terminated_with_residuals rather than terminated.","external_exposure_authorized":"None. A contract change; no spend, publication, contact or deployment.","reversibility":"Reversible before B04 by editing the SalesAgreement/Fulfillment contracts; after live sales, a migration under 02 §10 (T-R1).","reopen_trigger":"A demonstrated class of sale whose termination can never carry residuals (would make the state dead weight); or due_preserved cost at termination measurably dominating ordinary closure work.","implementation_evidence":"None yet. Guard repair lane owed; independent recheck owed; no runtime exists.","source":"registers/decisions.json#/13"},{"id":"AD-015","kind":"Decision","architecture_version":"S1.1","date":"2026-09-13","status":"adopted for the F2 amendment of 05-work-agents-skills.md; a selection, not complete-plan review, runtime conformance or founder acceptance","owner":"orchestrator under founder directive","title":"Consequence class is the routing axis, and the reached set governs — never a rank","problem":"The F2 round had to pick a routing unit for the work / agents / authority / skills / context / routing layer, and every candidate carried blocking findings that clustered on its own routing unit. R2 F-20 established that there is no single unit of justification: the founder's five criteria predicate on five different objects, and a criterion applied to the wrong unit returns undecidable, which reads as satisfied. The hybrid candidate routed on consequence class but computed one governing class by max() over a rank, and AT-M4-02 showed an action reaching two classes gated by only the higher row — while 02-authority-recovery.md §4 already requires that an action satisfying several classes meet all their gates.","decision":"Consequence class is layer 1 and decides who may act; a declared procedure decides how work runs and what each step may see (layer 2), a typed standing interest decides when work becomes due (layer 3), an existence record decides whether a worker may be created at all (layer 4), and exactly one standing party exists for each duty that outlives the case carrying it (layer 5). When two layers disagree the lower-numbered layer governs. The derivation returns the SET of reached classes and every reached class's gates apply. No total rank exists, no severity score is computed and no seventh class is added, so no monotonicity proof is owed (R-D22). One implementation of the derivation function exists; changing the function, the mapping table, the holder set or a declared floor is a protected control change.","alternatives":["Rank the reached classes and gate on the maximum — the hybrid candidate's construction, which drops gates the fixed boundary already requires (AT-M4-02)","Route on the worker, as the capability-differentiated and chartered candidates do — it makes the routing unit a property of the worker rather than of the work, and inherits that unit's blind spot (R2 F-20)","Route on the declared procedure alone — it decides how work runs and cannot decide who may act on work no procedure covers","Adopt one candidate whole rather than layering the units — every candidate's blockers cluster on its own unit, so adopting one adopts its blind spot","Close the founder's reason list at five, which remains his to do: it makes this design inadmissible on his own gate and is registered as TC-35"],"evidence_and_reasoning":["planning/F2/05-selection-record.md#1-decision","planning/F2/05-selection-record.md#31-from-m4--the-routing-axis-layer-1","planning/F2/05-selection-record.md#51-the-synthesized-rules (R-L1; MD-22 / R-D22)","planning/F2/05-selection-record.md#13-evidence-ledger (rows 1-2: R2 F-21.3, TC-17, AT-M4-02, DIRECTIVE §1.5)","planning/specification/02-authority-recovery.md#4-authentication-principals-and-grant-attenuation","research/F2/cross-lane-comparison.md (R2 F-20: no single unit of justification)","planning/F2/04-attack-consolidation.md (AT-M4-02)"],"epistemic_basis":"Inference on a founder constraint, plus a restatement of a fixed boundary. The reached-set rule is 02 §4 restated rather than changed. The choice of routing axis is an inference from R2 F-20 and from the observed clustering of each candidate's blockers on its own unit; no runtime measured it. The layer precedence ORDER is the selection record's own marked design proposal with no finding behind it (§13, row 70), and it is the load-bearing unevidenced choice here: nothing in this round tests a precedence between routing units, because no candidate had more than one.","accepted_design_costs":["Every action carries a set rather than one class, so gate evaluation is a conjunction over rows and cannot be short-circuited by a comparison","The precedence between layers is unevidenced; if it is wrong, the whole selection is wrong and nothing in this round would have caught it","The added structure is not paid for if more than 90% of admitted actions derive to the two lowest classes, which is this layer's own removal criterion"],"external_exposure_authorized":false,"reversibility":"Repository-local specification remains reversible; operational promises, disclosure and lost data require separate consequence decisions.","reopen_trigger":"Reopen when more than 90% of admitted actions derive to the two lowest classes over a fixed window, or when the derivation and the declared floor agree on every action over a window — then the derivation adds nothing the floor already said and the floor alone survives. Reopen layer 1's release path if the runtime holds no credential at the boundary that can be narrowed: attenuation is then unavailable, the constraint must be enforced by mediation, and that is a different architecture (§11.1.2). Also reopen if the admission authority's concentration measurably misses important work, raises founder labour or obstructs independently capable domains. Origin: F2 Step 5a-ii selection record §1, §11.3.","implementation_evidence":null,"source":"registers/decisions.json#/14"},{"id":"AD-016","kind":"Decision","architecture_version":"S1.1","date":"2026-09-13","status":"adopted for the F2 amendment of 05-work-agents-skills.md; a selection, not complete-plan review, runtime conformance or founder acceptance","owner":"orchestrator under founder directive","title":"The class is computed from records the acting party cannot author, and recomputed at the effect","problem":"A consequence class computed from anything the acting party can author is a boundary that party can move. R4 found tool self-description, command-text matching, instruction scoping, definition-file authority and sandbox verdicts each insufficient as the input to an authority decision (R4 F1, F4, F5, F8, F9, F12; AG-08). Separately, a class computed at admission and never re-checked is a grant checked against bytes that are not the bytes released (AS-M4-02).","decision":"The class derives by one deterministic function from resolved parameters, the destination and egress identity, the selector closure over conflict claims, deletion scopes and open obligations, and the owning capability contract's declared floor — every one a record the acting party cannot author. The class is recomputed inside the ordered release transaction on the frozen bytes; a mismatch PARKS and never resolves downward. ConsequenceDerivation is append-only and written only inside the release path, and its mismatch disposition is writable only by the party owning the park. An executor's grant scope is a proposal right; C04 performs every release. Where a dimension is unresolvable the class resolves to the ceiling of the unresolved dimensions.","alternatives":["Compute the class once at admission and trust it at release — the grant is then checked against bytes that are not the bytes released (AS-M4-02)","Let the acting worker or a model declare its own class, refused because a boundary a party can author is a boundary that party can move (R4 F1, F4, F5, F8, F9, F12)","Resolve a release-time mismatch downward to the lower class, refused: it parks, and a park is a state with an owner rather than a silent continue","Screen a false entry rather than gate on it, refused: a poisoning attack carrying no instruction at all passed a four-stage screen 360 times out of 360 (R1 F-10)"],"evidence_and_reasoning":["planning/F2/05-selection-record.md#51-the-synthesized-rules (R-L1, R-X01)","planning/F2/05-selection-record.md#13-evidence-ledger (rows 3-5: R4 F1, F4, F5, F8, F9, F12, AG-08, AS-M4-02)","planning/F2/05-selection-record.md#24-the-three-findings-most-likely-to-change-what-you-do (R1 F-10, R2 F-09)","research/F2/R4-authority.md","planning/F2/reviews/A-security-adversarial.md (AS-M4-02)","planning/specification/02-authority-recovery.md#4-authentication-principals-and-grant-attenuation"],"epistemic_basis":"Source claim plus specification. The refused inputs are R4's measurements, made elsewhere and not by this project; the recompute-at-release rule takes AS-M4-02 as the gap and is this record's specification as the repair. The one-implementation rule is a direct observation on this repository's own classifier, where two implementations of one risk classification disagreed and it was found during an incident.","accepted_design_costs":["A release transaction carries a second derivation and the cost of freezing the bytes before it","A parked mismatch needs a party who owns the park — a staffing precondition, not a code path","Resolving an unresolvable dimension to its ceiling is deliberately conservative and will refuse some legitimate work; false exclusion is unmeasured everywhere in the corpus (U-12) and this decision adds to it"],"external_exposure_authorized":false,"reversibility":"Repository-local specification remains reversible; operational promises, disclosure and lost data require separate consequence decisions.","reopen_trigger":"Reopen if the runtime holds no credential at the boundary that can be narrowed, because layer 1's release path is then mediation rather than attenuation (§11.1.2). Reopen on a demonstrated class input that only the acting party can supply and for which no non-authorable substitute exists, or if recomputation parks so often that the release path is unusable. Origin: F2 Step 5a-ii selection record §5.1 R-L1.","implementation_evidence":null,"source":"registers/decisions.json#/15"},{"id":"AD-017","kind":"Decision","architecture_version":"S1.1","date":"2026-09-13","status":"adopted for the F2 amendment of 05-work-agents-skills.md; a selection, not complete-plan review, runtime conformance or founder acceptance","owner":"orchestrator under founder directive","title":"A step declares its read set, and the loader delivers and records it","problem":"\"The checker did not read the producer's rationale\" was an assertion in every candidate and a fact in none: the caller claimed its read list and nothing recorded what was actually delivered. R7 §7 and F9 establish that independence of INFLUENCE is the half of verification that is reachable at all, and it is reachable only if delivery is observed rather than claimed. R2 F-03 and R3 F51-F52 add the discriminator: auto-generated multi-agent systems underperformed a single agent at up to ten times the cost while an expert-designed one reached 96.5% against 57.0% on the same diagnostic, and what separates them is whether separation is enforced by construction or only described in prompts.","decision":"WorkflowDefinition and StepExecution gain step_kind ∈ {compute, model, human, professional, effect}, declared_read_set, declared_grants, validator_ref, branch_set and critical_fields — as fields on existing registry records, never as new records. The loader delivers the declared read set and RECORDS what it actually delivered; the caller's claimed read list is not trusted. A guard is a pure function over typed outputs and journal state, and a model's output is an input to a guard and never a jump. The step boundary is the checkpoint and the cost is carried. One effect per effect step, and the step is the idempotency unit. Procedure admission refuses a branch set in which a model-authored value selects between acceptance strengths.","alternatives":["Trust the caller's declared read list — the pre-repair state, an assertion no record can contradict","Blind the checker by instruction in a prompt, refused: separation enforced by construction is the measured discriminator (R2 F-03, R3 F51, F52)","A separate reserved closing-allowance predicate instead of checkpointing every step boundary, which needs a denominator this round establishes does not exist","Let a model step select a branch, refused: a model's output is an input to a guard, and acceptance-strength selection is a guard over journal state and consequence class"],"evidence_and_reasoning":["planning/F2/05-selection-record.md#32-from-m3--the-execution-structure-layer-2","planning/F2/05-selection-record.md#51-the-synthesized-rules (R-L2, R-D19, R-X19)","planning/F2/05-selection-record.md#13-evidence-ledger (rows 7-12: AT §E.2, R7 §7 and F9, R2 F-09, F-18, R3 F29, F30, F41, F44)","planning/specification/06-knowledge-evidence-evaluation.md#2-context-assembly-and-information-loss","research/F2/R7-verification.md","planning/F2/reviews/A-technical.md (AT-M1-03, AT §E.2)"],"epistemic_basis":"Source claim plus inference. The loader-records-delivery rule rests on R7's influence-independence findings and on AT §E.2; the step-boundary checkpoint is AT-M1-03's own second branch taken whole. The five step kinds as an EXHAUSTIVE set is a marked design proposal with no finding behind it (§13, row 9), and its falsifier is one real work item that fits none of them.","accepted_design_costs":["Checkpointing every step boundary carries a real per-step cost, and taking the step model takes its dominant unpriced cost with it: the per-step cacheless launch cost against a long-session arm is unmeasured (U-11), and the expected-launch count per procedure version is the instrument that would price it","Authoring and maintaining declared procedures is layer 2's real cost and is unevaluable in any unit today (U-7)","The loader's record proves what was delivered, not that the delivery was the right set; the provider may edit context after any loader has recorded its inputs, and what one compaction event loses in load-bearing facts is unmeasured (U-4)"],"external_exposure_authorized":false,"reversibility":"Repository-local specification remains reversible; operational promises, disclosure and lost data require separate consequence decisions.","reopen_trigger":"Reopen when a newer model passes every step's declared validator with the step merged into its neighbour or removed — a scaffold's contribution is a function of the generation that motivated it and must be re-ablated when the model changes (§11.3, L2). Reopen the layer's foundation if a defence rests on a mechanism nobody can test. Origin: F2 Step 5a-ii selection record §5.1 R-L2, §11.3.","implementation_evidence":null,"source":"registers/decisions.json#/16"},{"id":"AD-018","kind":"Decision","architecture_version":"S1.1","date":"2026-09-13","status":"adopted for the F2 amendment of 05-work-agents-skills.md; a selection, not complete-plan review, runtime conformance or founder acceptance","owner":"orchestrator under founder directive","title":"Acceptance criteria are authored by the capability owner, frozen before the producing step, and unamendable by the producing path","problem":"AS-X-01 found a fourth unblinded channel into the checker that no research lane named: the acceptance criteria themselves, authored by the producing path. AX had tested the three channels R7 named — the producer's rationale, the producer's preferred conclusion and the shared record — and found them closed in all five candidates, recording no blocking finding on W5. The consolidation recorded the two dispositions as in conflict with no review owning the reconciliation.","decision":"The capability owner authors the acceptance criteria at procedure admission. They are versioned and frozen BEFORE the producing step starts; the producing path may neither author nor amend them, and an amendment between admission and submission is refused by a guard. Fixture F-4 gains a fourth arm in which the criteria are authored by the producing path, reported beside the existing three. W5 is recorded as sufficient on the three tested channels and UNESTABLISHED on the fourth until that arm runs; AX's judgement is not overturned. A check reads only fields the producer could not author, its tie-break inverts to strongest-sufficient, and a checker with no paired clean-case refusal rate resolves unresolved, never pass.","alternatives":["Treat AS-X-01 as non-blocking because the lane that raised it did not own the dimension, refused: a finding's class under protocol §5 is a property of the finding — its trigger, its resulting failure, its affected requirement — and not of which lane noticed it","Pin the criteria inside an immutable procedure only, which is the workflow-first candidate's exemption and does not cover the adaptive and unclassified paths this synthesis also admits","Record W5 as sufficient on the verdict matrix alone, which reports an assurance whose scope is unstated","Author plausible criteria inside the producing path and rely on review to catch a bad one, which is the silent path an implementer would otherwise take"],"evidence_and_reasoning":["planning/F2/05-selection-record.md#63-the-as-x-01--ax-w5-tension-resolved","planning/F2/05-selection-record.md#51-the-synthesized-rules (R-D11 / R-G02, R-X20, R-X14)","planning/F2/05-selection-record.md#13-evidence-ledger (rows 32-34: AM-01, R7 F1, F2, F8, F12, F13, F15, TC-37, FAL-08, FAL-09, AG-15, AS-X-01, G-02)","planning/specification/06-knowledge-evidence-evaluation.md#6-evaluation-contracts-at-every-level","planning/specification/06-knowledge-evidence-evaluation.md#7-cases-trials-independence-and-negative-controls","planning/F2/reviews/A-security-adversarial.md (AS-X-01)","planning/F2/reviews/A-context-evidence.md (AX, W5)"],"epistemic_basis":"Specification closing a blocking finding. The reconciliation of AS-X-01 against AX's W5 is an inference from the acceptance protocol's own classification rule and not a measurement. Whether the fourth channel changes any verification verdict is UNKNOWN until the fourth F-4 arm runs — owner C06, at the first F-4 execution, whenever a runtime exists. Independence of ERROR is not claimed at all: it is unreachable inside one model family and is disclaimed in every acceptance that rests on a same-family checker. R-G02, the one rule this record cites that appears nowhere in the specification (F6A-11, 2026-09-14): the selection record's rule table records R-G02 as \"= R-D11\", and the rule landed under that id at 06-knowledge-evidence-evaluation.md section 7. The ID did not land; the RULE did, and nothing is outstanding behind it.","accepted_design_costs":["A criterion must exist and be frozen before production starts, so a capability owner sits on the critical path of every procedure admission","The fourth F-4 arm is owed and cannot run without a runtime: this decision closes the finding in specification and leaves the measurement open","Joint false acceptance for a same-family producer/checker pair on planted defects is the quantity that decides whether separating the checker buys anything, and nobody has measured it (U-3)"],"external_exposure_authorized":false,"reversibility":"Repository-local specification remains reversible; operational promises, disclosure and lost data require separate consequence decisions.","reopen_trigger":"Reopen on any acceptance recorded as passed where the checker reported no clean-case rate — that must resolve unresolved — and on a rising pass rate as load rises, which is the registered tell that verification is being starved (§11.1.5). Reopen this decision if the fourth F-4 arm shows the criteria channel changes the verdicts. Origin: F2 Step 5a-ii selection record §6.3, §5.1 R-D11.","implementation_evidence":null,"source":"registers/decisions.json#/17"},{"id":"AD-019","kind":"Decision","architecture_version":"S1.1","date":"2026-09-13","status":"adopted for the F2 amendment of 05-work-agents-skills.md; a selection, not complete-plan review, runtime conformance or founder acceptance","owner":"orchestrator under founder directive","title":"Relevance is computed by deterministic arming, and no component may prevent an interest arming","problem":"A shared source of truth nobody is forced to read is not a source of truth, and a deferral nobody can see is indistinguishable from an oversight. The subscription-activated candidate is the only one in the round where an item's relevance is computed rather than remembered, and nothing in it stopped a component from suppressing an arming. Its own two blocking findings followed from letting an activation promote what it investigated.","decision":"StandingInterest and the ArmedSet are registered. Preconditions are deterministic, NO MODEL may appear in a precondition, and all prerequisites gate. Five admission verbs and five prohibitions. The armed set is a computed projection with no lifecycle and no writer: no component may prevent membership, and the admission authority holds no write access to precondition-bearing kinds. A trial interest is admissible only at the two lowest effect classes, may not declare a writer key, and may write only a proposed revision of a constraint. The unmatched pool is the computable complement, with retention exceeding the longest plausible outage and an alarm with a named reader — and its residue is named rather than covered: it cannot catch an entry that armed the WRONG interest. The admission authority gains a per-origin arming rate as a refusal predicate.","alternatives":["Rely on scheduled review alone, which is precisely this layer's removal criterion and the thing to test rather than assume","Let a model evaluate a precondition, refused: a false entry could then change what becomes due, and an untrusted entry may activate only read-only work","Allow a component to suppress an arming for throughput, refused: it makes a deferral invisible and returns the absence-versus-oversight ambiguity the layer exists to remove","Let a trial interest declare a writer key, refused by a deterministic admission check that names the failed predicate (R-D16)"],"evidence_and_reasoning":["planning/F2/05-selection-record.md#33-from-m5--when-work-becomes-due-layer-3","planning/F2/05-selection-record.md#51-the-synthesized-rules (R-L3, R-D15, R-D16, R-D23, R-X20, R-X21)","planning/F2/05-selection-record.md#13-evidence-ledger (rows 13-16: R5-01, R5-02, R3 F33, R8 B-7, AG-08, R1 F-10, F-11, R2 F-09, AS-M5-01)","research/F2/R5-routing.md","research/F2/R1-context.md (F-10: a no-instruction poisoning attack passed a four-stage screen 360 of 360)","planning/F2/reviews/A-security-adversarial.md (AS-M5-01, AS-M5-03, AS-M5-04)","planning/specification/05-work-agents-skills.md#7-durable-schedules-and-capacity-gaps (R-L3: StandingInterest, the armed set as a computed projection nobody writes, and the hard rules of layer 3)","planning/specification/05-work-agents-skills.md#9-positive-adverse-and-capacity-limited-conformance (row 5: an untrusted entry promoted to attested by the investigating activation)","planning/specification/05-work-agents-skills.md#10-registered-lifecycle-phases-named-only-in-the-registry (StandingInterest.trial)","planning/specification/11-schemas-state-contracts.md"],"epistemic_basis":"Source claim plus decision. Deterministic arming and the no-model precondition rest on R5-01, R5-02, R3 F33 and R8 B-7. The SPECIFIC five admission verbs and five prohibitions are a marked design proposal with no finding behind them (§13, row 14): the prohibitions are evidenced, the choice of five is not. The layer's admissibility turns on the deterministic-predicate fraction (U-6), which is unmeasured and is the layer's own sharpest falsifier. R-D15, the one rule this record cites that no specification text names by that id (F6A-11, 2026-09-14): both halves landed without the id. The no-promotion half is 05-work-agents-skills.md section 9, row 5 - an untrusted entry promoted to attested by the investigating activation is the adverse case, repaired by a new attested fact from an out-of-band corroborant. The trust-class prerequisite is section 7, cited there as \"D-15\". The floor half landed as an executable predicate under the id R-X13 in the contracts predicate registry, not as prose.","accepted_design_costs":["If the deterministic-predicate fraction is low, arming needs a model and this becomes the most expensive arrangement in the round — the response is withdrawal, not relaxation (R-X25)","The unmatched pool's residue is real and recorded as undetected: an entry that armed the wrong interest is not caught by it","The interest catalogue inherits the 10/100/1000 selection-degradation sweep, with one genuine advantage — near-duplicate typed predicates are statically detectable where near-duplicate prose descriptions are not"],"external_exposure_authorized":false,"reversibility":"Repository-local specification remains reversible; operational promises, disclosure and lost data require separate consequence decisions.","reopen_trigger":"Reopen when, over one month, every item whose relevance nobody currently holds in mind is surfaced within its latest responsible time by the existing scheduled review — then arming buys nothing. Withdraw the layer rather than relaxing it if the deterministic-predicate fraction falls below the threshold set under R-X25, whose value is a founder parameter and is open (§11.3, L3). Origin: F2 Step 5a-ii selection record §5.1 R-L3.","implementation_evidence":null,"source":"registers/decisions.json#/18"},{"id":"AD-020","kind":"Decision","architecture_version":"S1.1","date":"2026-09-13","status":"adopted for the F2 amendment of 05-work-agents-skills.md; a selection, not complete-plan review, runtime conformance or founder acceptance","owner":"orchestrator under founder directive","title":"A worker exists only against a justification naming one reason, its unit and a test that can return false","problem":"Negative control 4 asks which frozen fixture exercises a persistent or standing structure, and specialized knowledge was the most-used reason for creating a worker in the round. Across 4 model families, 162 roles and 2,410 questions, adding a persona gave no benefit and picking the best persona was no better than random (R2 F-10, R6 F6, TC-33). A reason with no unit and no falsifiable test is rhetoric, and control 4 was never applied to two of the five candidates at all.","decision":"ExistenceJustification is one record per AgentInstance, written by C02 at admission and expiring with the instance. It names exactly one of six reasons, each with its unit: permission scope → a permission scope; input provenance → an input set; consequence class → an effect class; confidentiality boundary → a context boundary; named partition → a partition; verification relation → a relation between two attempts. The proposed → admitted transition is REFUSED if the decidable test cannot return false. Specialized knowledge is refused as a reason and predicates on a skill version instead; provider or account separation folds into ExecutionSelection. Attributable identity is mandatory for every worker and is never a reason to create one. There is no persistent roster, and the profile-convergence probe is the control against one appearing.","alternatives":["Keep specialized knowledge as a reason to create a worker, overturned on measurement rather than on preference (R2 F-10, R6 F6, TC-33)","Charter a persistent roster, which is the chartered candidate — it failed negative control 4 on the one chartered desk no fixture exercises","Grant existence on a permission check alone, which is this layer's own removal criterion and becomes right the moment no admitted worker names another reason","Admit a reason with no unit, refused: the admission test must be able to return false or the record is rhetoric with a schema"],"evidence_and_reasoning":["planning/F2/05-selection-record.md#34-from-m1--whether-a-worker-may-exist-at-all-layer-4","planning/F2/05-selection-record.md#21-your-five-criteria","planning/F2/05-selection-record.md#64-the-two-control-cell-questions-the-consolidation-says-the-synthesis-must-answer","planning/F2/05-selection-record.md#13-evidence-ledger (rows 17-19, 68: R2 F-09, F-10, F-20, F-21, R6 F6, X11, control 4, AC-M1-06, R8 W-4, MG-11)","research/F2/R2-agent-existence.md","research/F2/R6-skills.md","planning/specification/05-work-agents-skills.md#4-temporary-workers-model-choice-and-bounded-reasoning (R-L4: ExistenceJustification, the six reasons with their units, and the removal criterion in falsifier form)","planning/specification/05-work-agents-skills.md#10-registered-lifecycle-phases-named-only-in-the-registry (ExistenceJustification.admitted)","planning/specification/11-schemas-state-contracts.md"],"epistemic_basis":"Inference on source claims. R2 F-20 supplies the unit-and-test requirement; the EXACT field list of the existence record is the selection record's own marked design proposal (§13, row 19). The six admitted reasons rest on R2 F-09, F-10, F-21 and R6 F6. Whether worker profiles converge over a month (U-8) is unmeasured and is the only honest test of whether this is a roster discovered rather than declared.","accepted_design_costs":["Every admitted worker carries an extra record and an admission check that can refuse it","Isolation for confidentiality is the only sense of isolated context exercised by the founder's six test cases, and separated arrangements cut disclosure violations by 20-50 points while leaving over 75% standing — the reason is admitted and it does not buy what the word suggests","Parallel work is near-inert as a reason at the current concurrency pin: the branch stays declarable and buys nothing until the account entitlement is read (U-2)"],"external_exposure_authorized":false,"reversibility":"Repository-local specification remains reversible; operational promises, disclosure and lost data require separate consequence decisions.","reopen_trigger":"Reopen when the profile count converges to a small stable set over a month (U-8) — the honest response is then to stop calling the workers ephemeral and design the standing form properly, with the chartered candidate repaired as the comparator — or when no admitted worker in a window names a reason other than permission scope, in which case the six reasons are one reason with five unused branches and the record can be a grant check (§11.3, L4; §11.2.6). Origin: F2 Step 5a-ii selection record §5.1 R-L4.","implementation_evidence":null,"source":"registers/decisions.json#/19"},{"id":"AD-021","kind":"Decision","architecture_version":"S1.1","date":"2026-09-13","status":"adopted for the F2 amendment of 05-work-agents-skills.md; a selection, not complete-plan review, runtime conformance or founder acceptance","owner":"orchestrator under founder directive","title":"Standing accountability is a record with an address and a reservation; carried model memory is refused","problem":"A duty that outlives the case carrying it needs a party who is still there once the case is closed: a grievance six months after closure with the custodian implicated, a deletion scope whose clock runs after the case ends, a day-five incident at the terminus of an escalation ladder. Universal ownership and no ownership are one state (R5-11). The chartered candidate answered this with persistent agents carrying model memory and failed negative control 4 on the one desk no fixture exercises; the capability-differentiated candidate carried the same hole silently.","decision":"StandingHolder is a record keyed by holder_id, proposed → staffed → suspended → retired_into(holder_id), proposed by the capability owner and endorsed by C01. Exactly one standing party exists for each duty that outlives its case, admitted by a three-part conjunction. The prohibition set is structural: a holder never produces, never releases, never decides the matter it is the subject of, and carries NO model memory. \"A holder prepares\" means an ephemeral worker instantiated under the holder's mandate carrying the holder's reservation ref and intake address and nothing else of the holder's. staffed → retired_into is refused while any duty it holds is live, and suspension stops admission in that duty class rather than leaving work assigned and silent. Every acceptance-owner role is a record with a reachability route, a capacity reservation, an alternate and a review date; every published intake carries per-counterparty and per-origin sub-caps whose exhaustion behaviour PRESERVES intake. A proposed holder exercised by no frozen fixture is refused on sight.","alternatives":["Persistent agents carrying model memory, refused: reachability is separable from carried memory, and carried model identity has no supporting evidence and two deployments refusing to support it (R8 A-7)","No standing layer at all, which leaves a surviving duty with no address — the state R5-11 names","Charter every proposed holder, refused: a holder exercised by no frozen fixture is unjustified, which is the mechanical form of negative control 4","Give the holder a veto over work in its duty class, refused: a holder that can veto can hold an empty bucket hostage (see AD-022)"],"evidence_and_reasoning":["planning/F2/05-selection-record.md#35-from-m2--standing-accountability-layer-5","planning/F2/05-selection-record.md#51-the-synthesized-rules (R-L5, R-X03, R-X07, R-X08, R-X09, R-X17)","planning/F2/05-selection-record.md#64-the-two-control-cell-questions-the-consolidation-says-the-synthesis-must-answer","planning/F2/05-selection-record.md#13-evidence-ledger (rows 20-23, 50, 55-56: R8 A-4, A-5, A-7, AC §7.4, AC-M3-02, AC-M4-01, AC-M4-05, AC-M5-02, AE-M4-05)","research/F2/R8-contrarian.md","planning/F2/reviews/A-company-human.md","planning/specification/05-work-agents-skills.md#12-standing-accountability (R-L5: StandingHolder as a record with an address, mandate, reservation, alternate and review date)","planning/specification/05-work-agents-skills.md#10-registered-lifecycle-phases-named-only-in-the-registry (StandingHolder.suspended)","planning/specification/11-schemas-state-contracts.md"],"epistemic_basis":"Inference on review findings, with one part explicitly unevidenced: the three-part conjunction AS a conjunction is marked unevidenced in the originating candidate's own ledger and this record inherits the mark (§13, row 21). Refusing carried model memory is a source claim — two deployments refusing to support it. The reserved-lane holder is justified by fixture F-2, which is NOT executable at the current concurrency pin, so that one structure rests on an unrunnable fixture and is recorded as OWED rather than passed. R-X07, cited by this record, DID NOT LAND (F6A-11, 2026-09-14): neither the string R-X07, nor capability_refs, nor the per-capability-never-grouped rule appears anywhere under the specification directory. That coverage discipline is carried by the F2 selection record alone, and is recorded here as outstanding, not as specified. [Superseded 2026-09-14: R-X07 landed in 05-work-agents-skills.md §12 on 2026-09-14 (F6W-01 repair, r7-prose-c); the statement that it did not land was correct when written and is stale now. Recorded by the orchestrator per F6Z-04.]","accepted_design_costs":["Staffing, and the figure is carried rather than summarised: a person is the acceptor on 37 of 46 capabilities in the consequence-class candidate and on every action in the 26 that floor at the economic/contractual class or above. This decision does not reduce that load; it makes it visible before work is admitted rather than after it is owed","Admission stops in any duty class whose acceptance role is unfilled, which in a one-person company is most of the economic/contractual classes","One standing structure — the reserved-lane holder — rests on a fixture that cannot run at the current pin, and its prerequisite is an account inspection nobody has done","The holder-hours-per-period figure is owed and has no denominator today"],"external_exposure_authorized":false,"reversibility":"Repository-local specification remains reversible; operational promises, disclosure and lost data require separate consequence decisions.","reopen_trigger":"Reopen on the fresh-holder arm: if a freshly bound holder matches the incumbent on the same fixed pool across two consecutive quarterly runs the carried state is cut, and if it still matches after the cut the holder is retired into another. Per holder: an intake empty and a clock unrun across two consecutive review periods retires the holder into another, with the address forwarded and residual duties transferred — never while a duty it holds is live. Reopen the layer's foundation if no party other than the founder can be reached within a duty's actual deadline, because the conjunction then produces holders that cannot be staffed and the no-answer branch of the staffing packet becomes the permanent operating state (§11.1.3, §11.3 L5). Origin: F2 Step 5a-ii selection record §5.1 R-L5.","implementation_evidence":null,"source":"registers/decisions.json#/20"},{"id":"AD-022","kind":"Decision","architecture_version":"S1.1","date":"2026-09-13","status":"adopted for the F2 amendment of 05-work-agents-skills.md; a selection, not complete-plan review, runtime conformance or founder acceptance","owner":"orchestrator under founder directive","title":"A reservation's minimum is evidence, not consent, and unconsumed allowance lapses independently of its holder","problem":"Two candidates ask the protected-lane holder before shedding and two apply a pre-endorsed order; the consolidation records opposite and individually correct positions with neither refuted, and two live blocking findings fail in OPPOSITE directions from that one question — nothing can halt a shed, and nothing can override a refusal. Separately, the session window resets on schedule whether consumed or not (R8 §3), so a reserve under a non-rolling allowance is waste rather than thrift, and no published denominator exists for expressing a reserve as an absolute quantity.","decision":"A protected-lane holder's stated minimum is EVIDENCE, never consent: there is no veto, and a returned minimum is recorded as evidence and does not block. Unconsumed reservation releases to the pool at a time-triggered lapse point independent of any holder's consent, with a declared cross-class release precedence and a lapsed-unconsumed record. Reservation gains holder_ref, stated_minimum and lapse_point; ShedDecision records the lane, the authority, the obligations that moved with named custodians, the stated minimum, whether it was breached, the overflow count and the lapsed-unconsumed quantity. Shares are fractions of the OBSERVED allowance, never absolute quantities. The exhaustion rule is distinct from the pressure rule: when the allowance is empty and a due obligation falls due, the named non-model production mode performs it, a named recipient is alerted, and the breach-or-perform decision leaves a record naming which was chosen and why.","alternatives":["Ask the holder and honour a refusal, which lets a holder hold an empty bucket hostage and is one of the two unrefuted positions","Execute a pre-endorsed order with no prohibition on refusal, which cannot notice that this particular shed is catastrophic — conceded in the workflow-first candidate's own words","Express reserves as absolute quantities, refused: no published denominator exists and every figure this round can produce is a ratio between arms","Let unconsumed reservation persist past the reset, refused: it is destroyed by the provider on schedule, so holding it is waste priced as thrift"],"evidence_and_reasoning":["planning/F2/05-selection-record.md#9-dissent-preserved (F-1, unresolved and retained)","planning/F2/05-selection-record.md#51-the-synthesized-rules (R-X24, R-G01, R-X10, R-X11)","planning/F2/05-selection-record.md#13-evidence-ledger (rows 24-26, 59: R8 §3, §8, W-6, MG-03, TC-26, AE-M4-01, AT and AE §E.2)","research/F2/R8-contrarian.md","planning/F2/reviews/A-economic-capacity.md (AE-M4-01)","planning/specification/07-integrations-capacity.md#6-capacity-money-and-scheduling"],"epistemic_basis":"Source claim and decision under a PRESERVED disagreement. The lapse rule rests on R8 §3; the no-veto rule on AE-M4-01 and R8 §8. The combination — a pre-endorsed order AND the no-veto prohibition — is the one neither pair of candidates proposed, and it is a choice under uncertainty rather than a resolution: whether a shed at the pressure threshold has time for a negotiation round has never been measured. The cross-class lapse PRECEDENCE ORDER is the selection record's own marked design proposal (§13, row 25). The lane shares, the stated minimums and the lapse point are a founder decision and no default is invented here.","accepted_design_costs":["A holder can be shed against its stated minimum, and the breach is what the founder is alerted to — the design accepts that it cannot notice that one particular shed is catastrophic","Generous reserves are destroyed unconsumed at the reset; tight reserves breach minimums under pressure. There is no setting that avoids both","The discriminating measurement is unrun, and the nearest instrument — one shed decision run twice on a tabletop — costs nothing and runs at the current pin"],"external_exposure_authorized":false,"reversibility":"Repository-local specification remains reversible; operational promises, disclosure and lost data require separate consequence decisions.","reopen_trigger":"Reopen on changed provider terms or semantics: the launch window, the concurrency pin, the cache lifetime, the metered affordance and the context-editing surface are provider properties, and a change to any of them moves this cost model (§11.1.4). Reopen the shed-authority half when the founder answers the halt-or-reverse packet, or when the shed tabletop is run and counts founder reversals against breached minimums. Origin: F2 Step 5a-ii selection record §9 dissent F-1, §5.1 R-X24.","implementation_evidence":null,"source":"registers/decisions.json#/21"}]
docs/vision-v2/02-ARCHITECTURE.md:29:context_pack[] (paths+hashes, ≤40 KB), done_test (argv, frozen before launch),
docs/vision-system/planning/specification/11-schemas-state-contracts.md:21:**DECISION.** That alternative is technically plausible, but it requires a preparation protocol, full-group review, final digest endorsements and edit-after-review recovery for ordinary acceptance. Composite launches amplify that labor. Late links to actual responses/reasons have to be prepared without smuggling assumptions into the frozen group. The immutable-revision solution instead records a proposed subject, evaluates it, then records the disposition. Its main cost is a second authoritative head and explicit joins on current lifecycle. The migration is broader but mechanical and auditable. Independent assessment must challenge that cost comparison and the correctness of the selected joins; author preference does not establish closure.
docs/vision-system/planning/specification/11-schemas-state-contracts.md:137:**SPECIFICATION — the guards the WORK-1.1 amendment registers under the predicate runtime boundary below.** Each is a `TypedPredicate` with an exact registered ID, version and closed argument object; **a string describing a desirable result is not one of these.** `guard.class.reached_set_gates_all` · `guard.class.no_total_rank` · `guard.derivation.recompute_matches` · `guard.derivation.writer_is_release_path` · `guard.readset.delivered_equals_declared` · `guard.criteria.frozen_before_producing_step` · `guard.criteria.author_not_in_producing_path` · `guard.branch.no_model_selected_acceptance_strength` · `guard.trust.derived_is_floor_of_inputs` · `guard.trust.promotion_is_an_effect_with_a_non_model_discriminator` · `guard.interest.precondition_invokes_no_model` · `guard.interest.writer_keys_not_self_declared` · `guard.constraint.standing_interest_writes_proposed_only` · `guard.admission.acceptance_role_staffed` · `guard.admission.refusal_names_failed_predicate` · `guard.custody.admitter_excluded` · `guard.holder.no_veto` · `guard.holder.not_retired_while_duty_live` · `guard.reservation.lapse_independent_of_consent` · `guard.delegation.width_ceiling_over_distinct_read_sets` · `guard.effect.one_per_step` · `guard.effect.identity_allocated_before_release` · `guard.check.reads_only_non_authorable_fields` · `guard.check.tie_break_strongest_sufficient` · `guard.intake.per_origin_subcap_preserves_intake` · `guard.approval.expiry_present` · `guard.supersession.walks_derived_closure` · `guard.acceptance.resolution_reason_present` · `guard.skill.declared_grant_inert` · `guard.launcher.stripping_positive_control`. **The criterion-call rule is a property of the EDGE and not of these thirty**, and it is stated once, under *Predicate runtime boundary* below, where `validate_contracts.py` fails an edge that does not call its `criterion_id`. **All thirty are pinned as conjuncts** in [`pinned-conjuncts.json`](contracts/pinned-conjuncts.json) with hand-written `require` rows under a `negated` and `disjoined` discipline, checked by a validator that reads the registry directly rather than importing the generator — so they are not unchecked; they are **unmutated**. **Paired adverse-and-benign fixture coverage is derived, never quoted here**: `comm -12 <(grep -rhoE 'guard\.[a-z0-9_.]+' contracts/fixtures/negative | sort -u) <(grep -rhoE 'guard\.[a-z0-9_.]+' contracts/fixtures/positive | sort -u) | wc -l`, run from this directory against the thirty names above. It read **14 of 30 on 2026-09-14**, and **the sixteen without a pair are owed rather than deferred in silence** — they include **both** effect guards, **both** derivation guards, `guard.interest.precondition_invokes_no_model`, which is the hard rule of layer 3 and whose violation is that layer's stated withdrawal condition, and `guard.class.no_total_rank`, which closes the contested (d) AT-M4-02. A guard registered with no adverse fixture is a guard nobody has seen fail ([`05-work-agents-skills.md`](05-work-agents-skills.md) §9). *Superseded 2026-09-14: this read “**Each must call its own criterion and each must be exercised by a paired adverse and benign fixture**”. Measured: `op: "call"` occurs in **0 of 30** guard bodies and **0 of 888** `criterion.*` ids is named after a guard, so the first half attributed an edge property to guards; the second half was true of **14 of 30**. The sentence asserted a standard this registry did not meet, which is the shape the chapter exists to refuse (F6C-16).*
docs/vision-system/planning/specification/11-schemas-state-contracts.md:208:**SPECIFICATION.** CS1 does not select new technologies, remove EAS-R1 comparator controls or change the frozen G protocol. It adds representation and guard specificity needed to build and challenge the selected S1 architecture. Independent review must decide FI-12 conceptual closure and whether the final registry resolves FI-10/11. **UNKNOWN.** Production predicate implementation, boundary failure injection, real continuity and professional/provider availability, customer benefit, accumulated institutional labor and longitudinal economics remain unexecuted.
docs/vision-system/planning/site/explorer/data/questions.json:1:[{"id":"Q-001","kind":"Unknown","question":"Where is THE-PATH-TO-THE-VISION.md?","status":"Answered","owner":"founder or source custodian","evidence":"No matching filename in current checkout, reachable git history search, or filenames under /Users/adamks/VibeCoding on 2026-09-12","packet":{"decision_required":"Supply the path, repository/ref or URL of the referenced document","why_this_owner":"The source is referenced in the directive but was not provided or found","latest_responsible_time":"Before asserting exact field-map coverage or planning completion","options":["Provide the source location","Explicitly identify a replacement authoritative field map"],"consequences":["Allows exact coverage against original ambition","Requires recording that the original source was superseded by founder direction"],"uncertainty":"The document may exist outside the searched directory or under another filename","reversibility":"Research and provisional planning can be revised after receipt","recommendation":"Locate and read the original source","if_no_answer":"Continue independent branches; retain a blocking gap on exact coverage and planning acceptance","unrelated_work_continues":true},"asked":"2026-09-12 via asynchronous text question","resolution":{"commit":"331b4c97657c0d4c648633779eff7668503f7c06","path":"docs/03-system-design/final-v2/THE-PATH-TO-THE-VISION.md","note":"Found by inspecting existing branch tree. Earlier git log path pattern missed nested file. No founder action remains."},"source":"registers/open-questions.json#/0"},{"id":"Q-002","kind":"Deferred question","question":"Who is the administrator and custodian of fault domain R, and by what independent route do they authenticate?","status":"Open","owner":"founder","evidence":"02 section 2 lists the required actual principal, administrators, substitute contracts and funding as deployment inputs and states that operational authority remains unavailable if they cannot be admitted. capabilities.json fulfillment_routes R-RUNTIME carries admission_state not_established.","source_refs":["planning/specification/02-authority-recovery.md#2-concrete-deployment-and-operational-admission","planning/specification/02-authority-recovery.md#1-authority-and-fault-contract","planning/specification/capabilities.json#/fulfillment_routes/R-RUNTIME"],"packet":{"decision_required":"Who is the administrator and custodian of fault domain R, and by what independent route do they authenticate?","why_this_owner":"The decision needs a named person who is not the founder acting as administrator A, an accepted custody arrangement and, if that person is paid, money. None of those is an agent's to supply. 02 section 2 states that the same person owning both accounts without independent accepted custody fails the claimed primary-admin-loss and owner-absence profile, so an agent choosing here would be choosing to void the architecture's central fault claim.","latest_responsible_time":"Before B10 operational admission, and before any operating promise that depends on recovery. B01 and B02 can build and test the witness protocol against local fixtures without it; 02 section 2 says local simulation cannot admit host or admin independence, so the need is real but not immediate.","options":["Name a second natural person as custodian R with independent login, MFA and recovery, and record the compensation and availability window as an operating cost","Engage a professional custody or managed-recovery service under an accepted engagement with the same separation properties","Accept a single-custodian profile explicitly, which narrows the declared fault claim to exclude primary-admin loss and owner absence, and record that narrowing in 02 section 1","Defer operational admission until one of the above is available"],"consequences":["A named independent custodian makes the zero-loss recovery objective testable at B10; it adds a recurring human cost and a second person who must be reachable within actual service deadlines","A service engagement converts the cost to a contract and introduces the provider as a new common root, which 02 section 2 requires to be recorded rather than assumed away","Accepting a single custodian is a coherent choice, but the architecture must then stop claiming survival of primary-and-backup loss; the claim, not the software, is what changes","Deferral leaves R-RUNTIME and R-REMEDY at admission_state not_established and blocks dependent promises"],"uncertainty":"Whether a suitable person or service exists within the founder's budget is unknown to this package; no candidate has been approached and no price has been obtained.","reversibility":"Reversible as a specification choice until infrastructure is purchased and data is placed. After real customer duties exist, changing custody is a migration with its own fencing and reconciliation.","recommendation":"No recommendation. This is a cost-versus-fault-tolerance trade-off that depends on the founder's risk tolerance and budget, both of which 03 section on operating setup reserves to the owner.","if_no_answer":"B01 through B09 proceed. B10 cannot complete, so no operating promise that depends on recovery may be made. This is recorded as an unavailable operating prerequisite, not as a narrowed plan.","unrelated_work_continues":true},"origin":"G3-06","raised":"2026-09-13; promoted into this register from specification prose by the G3-06 repair. Queued, not yet put to the founder.","asked":null,"source":"registers/open-questions.json#/1"},{"id":"Q-003","kind":"Deferred question","question":"Who is the competent grievance recipient, and what makes them outside the disputed dependency?","status":"Open","owner":"founder","evidence":"03-company-capabilities.md CAP-42 requires noncustomer-inclusive intake with reasons, deadlines, actual competent escalation and funded remedy. capabilities.json fulfillment_routes R-REMEDY records the actual reachable competent custodian and alternate as unestablished.","source_refs":["planning/specification/03-company-capabilities.md#incidents-knowledge-growth-and-responsible-ending","planning/specification/07-integrations-capacity.md#3-selected-fulfillment-adapters","planning/specification/capabilities.json#/fulfillment_routes/R-REMEDY"],"packet":{"decision_required":"Who is the competent grievance recipient, and what makes them outside the disputed dependency?","why_this_owner":"CAP-42 requires an actual competent person with standing to receive a complaint and reach a disposition. Competence and independence are properties of a person and their relationships, not of software; an agent cannot appoint one and cannot certify that a chosen person is outside the dependency being disputed.","latest_responsible_time":"Before the first offer is made available. CAP-12 binds verified delivery and support capacity before an offer, and an offer creates the standing that a grievance attaches to. So: before B10 admission and before any sale, whichever comes first.","options":["Name a person with the mandate, response capacity and a recorded availability window, funded","Engage an external ombuds or professional complaints service under an accepted engagement","Do not make any offer available until one of the above exists, which keeps the grievance surface empty"],"consequences":["A named funded recipient makes CAP-42's deadlines and escalation real and testable at B06","An external service supplies independence more cheaply than a second employee but adds a contract and a provider root that must be disclosed rather than called independent","Making no offer is the only honest alternative: 03 section on incidents says a reachable intake and a competent residual custodian must continue as long as required duties remain, so a sale creates this obligation whether or not the role is filled"],"uncertainty":"Response volume, and therefore the capacity this role needs, is unknown and will stay unknown until real customers exist.","reversibility":"Reversible before an offer exists. Once a duty has arisen, 03 section on incidents keeps the intake obligation alive after product closure, so the role cannot simply be withdrawn.","recommendation":"Recommendation: settle this together with Q-004 and Q-011. A recipient without a funded remedy and without an alternate for complaints about themselves is a role that fails on its first hard case, which is the one G-03's scenario walked.","if_no_answer":"No offer may be made available. Internal construction, research and every B01 through B09 test proceed.","unrelated_work_continues":true},"origin":"G3-06","raised":"2026-09-13; promoted into this register from specification prose by the G3-06 repair. Queued, not yet put to the founder.","asked":null,"source":"registers/open-questions.json#/2"},{"id":"Q-004","kind":"Deferred question","question":"When a complaint names the custodian, who is the alternate recipient, who appoints them, and by when?","status":"Open","owner":"founder","evidence":"G-03's 'Honor rights under hostile noise' scenario, step 'Complaint names the custodian': the contracts catch the adverse variation and the report records 'Who the alternate is, who appoints, by when' as not specified. 03-company-capabilities.md CAP-42 and CAP-17.","source_refs":["planning/specification/03-company-capabilities.md#incidents-knowledge-growth-and-responsible-ending","planning/reviews/G-03-evidence-unknowns-adversarial.md","planning/specification/capabilities.json#/fulfillment_routes/R-REMEDY"],"packet":{"decision_required":"When a complaint names the custodian, who is the alternate recipient, who appoints them, and by when?","why_this_owner":"CAP-17 routes such a complaint to an alternate and CAP-42 requires the recipient to sit outside the disputed decision and incentive dependency, but no document says who that alternate is or who has the standing to appoint them. Appointing the person who adjudicates a complaint against the founder's own custodian is a governance act; an agent selecting one would be selecting its own reviewer.","latest_responsible_time":"Before B10 admission and before the first offer, with Q-003. The G-03 scenario reached this step and found every other contract held, so this is the single unfilled role on that path.","options":["Name a standing alternate in advance with an explicit appointing authority recorded in the AuthorityMatrix","Define an appointment rule — for example an external professional selected from a named panel — that resolves without the founder at the time of the complaint","Route such complaints to an external forum from the outset and record that forum's applicable scope","Leave it unfilled and accept that a complaint against the custodian has no admitted route"],"consequences":["A standing alternate is testable at B06 and is the only option that survives founder absence","An appointment rule is weaker than a named person but stronger than nothing, and it is what CAP-41 already requires for succession: joint owner and provider loss must not depend on the absent owner","An external forum is independent by construction but has its own eligibility limits, which 03 says are the person's rights and a professional adjudication rather than this company's issuer limits","Leaving it unfilled makes CAP-42's independence promise false in the exact case it was written for"],"uncertainty":"Whether the applicable forum in the founder's jurisdiction accepts such a complaint, and on what terms, is a legal question this package does not answer and does not invent.","reversibility":"Reversible on paper. Not reversible once a complaint has been mishandled: 03 says a second native request ID is not another entitlement and the person's standing survives.","recommendation":"Recommendation: name a standing alternate AND record the appointing authority, because the two failure modes are different — an absent alternate and an alternate nobody may appoint.","if_no_answer":"The grievance route is admitted only for complaints that do not name the custodian, and that limitation is stated to the person rather than hidden. All other work proceeds.","unrelated_work_continues":true},"origin":"G3-06","raised":"2026-09-13; promoted into this register from specification prose by the G3-06 repair. Queued, not yet put to the founder.","asked":null,"source":"registers/open-questions.json#/3"},{"id":"Q-005","kind":"Deferred question","question":"Who is the independent assessor with write authority over protected-change acceptance, and what is their competence evidence?","status":"Open","owner":"founder","evidence":"08-improvement-implementation.md section 1: a candidate evaluator cannot select its own hidden tests, alter the gate, sign its acceptance or provision the signing key; if independent competence is unavailable the protected change waits while legitimate operation and containment continue.","source_refs":["planning/specification/08-improvement-implementation.md#1-protected-improvement-contract","planning/specification/01-contract-kernel.md#10-deterministic-invariant-register","registers/risks.json#/risks/14"],"packet":{"decision_required":"Who is the independent assessor with write authority over protected-change acceptance, and what is their competence evidence?","why_this_owner":"08 section 1 says that if independent competence is unavailable the protected change waits, and that the system does not invent a qualified proxy for the founder. That sentence makes the wait the founder's to resolve: the only way out is a real person with standing, and appointing one's own reviewer is precisely what the contract forbids the improver from doing.","latest_responsible_time":"Before the first ProtectedChange is authorized, which is B08. Every stage before B08 can be built, because construction under B00's frozen contracts is not itself a protected change.","options":["Name an external reviewer with relevant competence under an accepted engagement, per protected subject","Name different assessors per subject family — authority and release, evidence and evaluation, recovery — since 08 section 1's registry already defines authority per subject","Accept that protected changes wait indefinitely, which is the specified behaviour and is safe but makes the system unimprovable","Reduce the protected-subject set, which is itself a protected change and so cannot be self-authorized"],"consequences":["A named assessor makes B08's candidate-alters-the-gate tests meaningful; it costs money and calendar time per change and 06 section 8 requires that cost to be budgeted before the evaluation runs","Per-subject assessors match the registry but multiply the engagements","Indefinite waiting is the specified fail-safe. It means the system cannot fix itself, which 08 section 2 names as one of the conditions that falsifies the whole approach","Shrinking the protected set is the option most likely to be chosen for the wrong reason and is the one the architecture is built to make hard"],"uncertainty":"Whether relevant competence for these specific subjects is purchasable at all, and at what price, is unknown; the subjects are unusual and the assessor must be able to read the contracts.","reversibility":"Reversible: an assessor engagement can be ended and replaced. What is not reversible is a change activated without one, because 08 section 1 requires activation evidence that would then not exist.","recommendation":"No recommendation between the first two options. A recommendation against the fourth: reducing the protected set to escape the wait is the self-modification this register's RISK-15 exists to catch.","if_no_answer":"Protected changes accumulate as proposed and reviewed but never authorized. The system runs and does not improve. B01 through B07 and B09 proceed.","unrelated_work_continues":true},"origin":"G3-06","raised":"2026-09-13; promoted into this register from specification prose by the G3-06 repair. Queued, not yet put to the founder.","asked":null,"source":"registers/open-questions.json#/4"},{"id":"Q-006","kind":"Deferred question","question":"Who are the primary continuity custodian and the accepted alternate for IC-HUMAN, and what are their compensation, availability window and response capacity?","status":"Open","owner":"founder","evidence":"07-integrations-capacity.md section 4 on continuity admission; 03-company-capabilities.md CAP-41 on succession; capabilities.json fulfillment_routes R-PERSON and R-REMEDY, both admission_state not_established.","source_refs":["planning/specification/07-integrations-capacity.md#4-communication-and-independent-continuity","planning/specification/03-company-capabilities.md#incidents-knowledge-growth-and-responsible-ending","planning/specification/capabilities.json#/fulfillment_routes/R-PERSON"],"packet":{"decision_required":"Who are the primary continuity custodian and the accepted alternate for IC-HUMAN, and what are their compensation, availability window and response capacity?","why_this_owner":"07 section 4 requires a primary custodian and an accepted alternate with independent login, recovery and MFA and an understood mandate, and states plainly that there is no assumed free lawyer, accountant, proxy founder or perpetual on-call volunteer. Two named humans, their consent and their pay: none is derivable.","latest_responsible_time":"Before the route is declared live. 07 section 4 requires an actual acknowledgement and a rehearsal of a benign request before that declaration, so the people must exist before B06's continuity tests can mean anything, and certainly before B10.","options":["Name both roles now, with compensation and an availability window, and run the rehearsal at B06","Name the primary now and defer the alternate to B10, accepting a single point of failure in the interim","Contract a continuity service that supplies both roles","Declare the continuity route unavailable, which makes every promise that depends on it unmakeable"],"consequences":["Both roles named is the only configuration 07 section 4 calls live; it is the most expensive","A primary alone fails exactly the case the route exists for — the primary being unavailable — and should be recorded as an accepted residual rather than as a partial success","A service supplies availability but shares a provider root with itself; 07 section 3 requires shared DNS and provider failures to be disclosed rather than called independent because the URLs differ","Declaring it unavailable is honest and blocks the dependent promises, which is the specified behaviour"],"uncertainty":"Response capacity cannot be sized before real volume exists, so the first arrangement will be a guess checked against actual minutes, as 04 requires for the owner's own plan.","reversibility":"Reversible: 07 section 4 makes removal and replacement explicit resource obligations. Not reversible is a duty that fell through the gap while the role was empty.","recommendation":"Recommendation: name the alternate before the primary is needed rather than after, because the alternate is by definition required at the moment the founder cannot arrange one.","if_no_answer":"The continuity route is not declared live. 07 section 4's rehearsal cannot run, and every promise depending on continuity stays unmakeable. Other integration work proceeds.","unrelated_work_continues":true},"origin":"G3-06","raised":"2026-09-13; promoted into this register from specification prose by the G3-06 repair. Queued, not yet put to the founder.","asked":null,"source":"registers/open-questions.json#/5"},{"id":"Q-007","kind":"Deferred question","question":"What is the actual principal — legal form, jurisdiction, signatory and registrations — under which this company transacts?","status":"Open","owner":"founder","evidence":"03-company-capabilities.md CAP-40 and the record-and-procedure contract; 01-contract-kernel.md section 3, where principal_id identifies an actual natural or legal principal and company_id is a coordination namespace and not a legal entity.","source_refs":["planning/specification/03-company-capabilities.md#finance-suppliers-people-and-institutional-work","planning/specification/01-contract-kernel.md#3-normative-types-and-record-envelope","planning/specification/03-company-capabilities.md#record-and-procedure-contract"],"packet":{"decision_required":"What is the actual principal — legal form, jurisdiction, signatory and registrations — under which this company transacts?","why_this_owner":"CAP-40 requires the actual principal, relevant location and activity facts, signatory, account access, name and asset rights and required registrations before transacting, and 03 asserts no universal jurisdiction, legal form, licensing threshold or setup duration. The kernel is explicit that a venture never silently creates a principal and that no service name or self-reference manufactures legal standing.","latest_responsible_time":"Before the first payment, which CAP-40 states directly: the software can prepare before revenue but cannot defer a prerequisite required before the first payment. In build terms, before B10.","options":["Establish or confirm a legal entity and record its jurisdiction, signatory and registrations","Transact as a natural person where that is lawful for the intended activity, recording the exposure","Defer all transacting, which keeps the venture at research and construction only"],"consequences":["An entity bounds personal exposure and makes CAP-40's prerequisite chain resolvable; it costs money and carries filing duties that CAP-20 and CAP-21 then owe","Transacting personally is faster and places the liability on the founder directly, which is material legal and financial exposure and therefore the founder's acceptance to give","Deferring is the current state and is honest; it means no sale"],"uncertainty":"Applicable registrations and licensing thresholds depend on the activity and the jurisdiction, neither of which is chosen. 03 refuses to guess them and so does this packet.","reversibility":"Not reversible in the ordinary sense: entity formation, registrations and the liabilities attached to a first transaction persist. Changing principal later is a migration under 02 section 10.","recommendation":"No recommendation. Legal form and personal exposure are the founder's to accept, and 04 reserves new material exposure to its actual owner.","if_no_answer":"No sale, no payment, no filing and no contract. All internal construction and research proceed; 03 says no prior paying customer is required to investigate or prepare.","unrelated_work_continues":true},"origin":"G3-06","raised":"2026-09-13; promoted into this register from specification prose by the G3-06 repair. Queued, not yet put to the founder.","asked":null,"source":"registers/open-questions.json#/6"},{"id":"Q-008","kind":"Deferred question","question":"Which named professionals will supply scoped determinations, and who holds the fee authority for each?","status":"Open","owner":"founder","evidence":"03-company-capabilities.md CAP-20 and CAP-21; ProfessionalRequest's required fields: exact question, applicable facts and nexus, source packet, named provider, fee authority, acknowledgment date, due result.","source_refs":["planning/specification/03-company-capabilities.md#finance-suppliers-people-and-institutional-work","planning/specification/capabilities.json#/fulfillment_routes/R-PERSON"],"packet":{"decision_required":"Which named professionals will supply scoped determinations, and who holds the fee authority for each?","why_this_owner":"ProfessionalRequest requires a named provider and a fee authority, and CAP-21 requires an actual competent issuer's scoped conclusion. 03 says explicitly that preparing or delivering the packet does not complete the requested professional work. Engaging a professional and committing fees are acts only the founder can perform.","latest_responsible_time":"Before the latest responsible start of the first determination that depends on one — a filing deadline, a contract review or a regulatory question. 03 says missing capacity invokes the accepted alternate before the latest responsible start and remains a material readiness failure when unavailable.","options":["Engage named providers per discipline now with a standing fee authority","Engage on demand with a pre-agreed fee ceiling and a named alternate per discipline","Defer engagement and accept that any duty requiring a determination becomes a readiness failure"],"consequences":["Standing engagements give predictable availability and cost more when unused","On-demand with a ceiling is cheaper and risks unavailability at the deadline, which is the failure CAP-21 is written to surface rather than hide","Deferring means the first real filing or professional question becomes an incident"],"uncertainty":"Which disciplines are actually needed follows from Q-007's jurisdiction and activity and cannot be enumerated before it.","reversibility":"Reversible: engagements can be changed. A missed statutory deadline is not.","recommendation":"Recommendation: settle Q-007 first. The set of disciplines is derived from the principal and activity, so answering this one earlier means guessing at what to buy.","if_no_answer":"No professional determination is available. Any capability whose acceptance condition requires one stays unaccepted, and the dependent duty is recorded as a readiness failure rather than completed.","unrelated_work_continues":true},"origin":"G3-06","raised":"2026-09-13; promoted into this register from specification prose by the G3-06 repair. Queued, not yet put to the founder.","asked":null,"source":"registers/open-questions.json#/7"},{"id":"Q-009","kind":"Deferred question","question":"Does an actual mail-provider account exist for this principal, is it approved for a custom API client, and what are its allowance, eligible streams and applicable terms?","status":"Open","owner":"founder","evidence":"07-integrations-capacity.md section 9.2's UNKNOWN admission-check paragraph; section 9.1's endpoint, header and returned-identity unknowns; capabilities.json fulfillment_routes R-CONTACT.","source_refs":["planning/specification/07-integrations-capacity.md#92-where-suppression-and-eligibility-are-actually-enforced","planning/specification/07-integrations-capacity.md#91-the-transport-boundary-request-identity-and-what-the-gate-can-see","planning/specification/capabilities.json#/fulfillment_routes/R-CONTACT"],"packet":{"decision_required":"Does an actual mail-provider account exist for this principal, is it approved for a custom API client, and what are its allowance, eligible streams and applicable terms?","why_this_owner":"07 section 9.2 lists these as UNKNOWN admission checks and says none may be closed by assumption, by a plausible value, or by an implementation's behaviour standing in for the provider's. Every one of them is resolved by holding an account: a person must open it, agree to terms on behalf of a principal, and obtain the approval. An agent cannot create an account or accept terms.","latest_responsible_time":"Before the mail profile can be admitted, which is B05, and before any message is sent to a real recipient. The outbound contract in 07 section 9 can be built and tested against fixtures without it.","options":["Open an account under the principal from Q-007 and obtain the observations at admission","Select a different provider and repeat the same admission checks against it","Use only the human send channel — 07 section 3 names Fastmail human send as the continuity and manual route — and admit no automated outbound profile","Defer, which leaves IC-MAIL-OUT unadmitted"],"consequences":["An account closes the section 9.2 unknowns with real observations and creates a billing relationship and an allowance that section 4's planning limits must respect","Changing provider does not reduce the work: every one of these checks is provider-specific, and 07 section 8 requires a protected migration with an explicit quality and cost comparison","Human-only send is fully specified and needs no account admission; it consumes owner or custodian minutes per message, which section 4 requires to be reserved and measured","Deferral keeps R-CONTACT at not_established"],"uncertainty":"Whether the provider approves a custom API client for this principal is the provider's decision and is unknowable in advance. 07 section 9.2 says what the terms permit for this company is an account-admission question and states no answer.","reversibility":"Reversible: an account can be closed and a provider replaced, subject to 07 section 8's removal procedure and the surviving access descendants it enumerates.","recommendation":"Recommendation: this question depends on Q-007, because the account must be opened by and for the actual principal. Opening it personally and migrating later is the expensive path.","if_no_answer":"IC-MAIL-OUT stays unadmitted. Inbound intake, the human send route and every other adapter proceed; the independent grievance mailbox that 07 section 3 requires on every receipt is a separate route.","unrelated_work_continues":true},"origin":"G3-06","raised":"2026-09-13; promoted into this register from specification prose by the G3-06 repair. Queued, not yet put to the founder.","asked":null,"source":"registers/open-questions.json#/8"},{"id":"Q-010","kind":"Deferred question","question":"Will the founder adopt a ParticipationPlan — availability windows, maximum decision-batch minutes, interrupt limit, practice allocation, incident reserve, permitted assessment data and sampling policy — and consent to the competence assessment?","status":"Open","owner":"founder","evidence":"04-human-operation.md section on attention and practiced competence; 06-knowledge-evidence-evaluation.md section 6, Attention/competence row; registers/risks.json RISK-10, whose two attack cases AC23 and AC24 are both enforcement rule-only.","source_refs":["planning/specification/04-human-operation.md#attention-and-practiced-competence","planning/specification/06-knowledge-evidence-evaluation.md#6-evaluation-contracts-at-every-level","registers/risks.json#/risks/9"],"packet":{"decision_required":"Will the founder adopt a ParticipationPlan — availability windows, maximum decision-batch minutes, interrupt limit, practice allocation, incident reserve, permitted assessment data and sampling policy — and consent to the competence assessment?","why_this_owner":"04 states that an empty plan means no asserted attention or competence capacity for dependent promises, that the interface offers understandable defaults at operating setup but silence cannot adopt them, and that the assessment runs under a consented human protocol the owner may decline. Consent to be measured is not something any agent may supply, infer or default.","latest_responsible_time":"Before the first promise whose feasibility depends on the founder's attention — which is the first offer, so before B10. B06's human flows can be built and tested against a fixture plan.","options":["Adopt the offered default policy: one cycle per five declared operating days within a chosen number of minutes, four short encounters, adverse samples alternating","Adopt a modified plan with different minutes, cadence or permitted assessment data","Adopt a plan for attention only and decline the competence assessment, accepting that RISK-10 has no detector at all","Adopt nothing, which is the current state"],"consequences":["The default is a proposed schedule to test, not a proven dose; adopting it makes RISK-10 measurable at B06 and costs the declared minutes every cycle","A modified plan is equally valid; 04 makes the policy owner-contestable by design","Declining the assessment is the owner's right and is recorded as a visible coverage limit rather than as incompetence; it leaves this register's RISK-10 with no instrument at all","Adopting nothing means no dependent promise may assert attention capacity, which blocks offers"],"uncertainty":"The specification calls its own default a proposed schedule to test and not a proven human-learning dose. There is one owner, no baseline and no operating data, so the first plan cannot be calibrated.","reversibility":"Fully reversible and explicitly so: 04 says revisions to the policy are explicit and owner-contestable.","recommendation":"Recommendation: adopt something rather than nothing, and treat the first plan as a measurement to revise rather than a commitment. The unadopted state is the only one that blocks offers.","if_no_answer":"No dependent promise may assert attention or competence capacity. Internal construction is unaffected; 04 says an empty plan does not prevent software development or force a questionnaire now.","unrelated_work_continues":true},"origin":"G3-06","raised":"2026-09-13; promoted into this register from specification prose by the G3-06 repair. Queued, not yet put to the founder.","asked":null,"source":"registers/open-questions.json#/9"},{"id":"Q-011","kind":"Deferred question","question":"What funded capacity is reserved for remedy, grievance handling and responsible closure, and from what account?","status":"Open","owner":"founder","evidence":"03-company-capabilities.md CAP-42 and CAP-39; 01-contract-kernel.md section 9, where nonoptional service classes have separately reserved capacity and a flood cannot commandeer its budget.","source_refs":["planning/specification/03-company-capabilities.md#incidents-knowledge-growth-and-responsible-ending","planning/specification/01-contract-kernel.md#9-scheduling-bounds-and-useful-progress","planning/reviews/G-03-evidence-unknowns-adversarial.md"],"packet":{"decision_required":"What funded capacity is reserved for remedy, grievance handling and responsible closure, and from what account?","why_this_owner":"CAP-42 requires funded remedy and CAP-39 requires closure with actual custodian, funding and review dates; G-03's scenario records funded remedy capacity and closure funding as admission inputs. Money is the founder's to commit, and 01 section 9 is explicit that numeric reserves and actual performer calendars are mandatory operating inputs and not fictional capacity the specification may supply.","latest_responsible_time":"Before the first offer, with Q-003. An offer creates the exposure that this reserve exists to meet, and 03 says publishing a standing offer itself creates a declared exposure window that capacity and authority must cover.","options":["Commit a named reserve per currency and principal, sized to a stated worst case, held separately from operating funds as 01 section 9's separately reserved capacity requires","Commit a smaller reserve and cap the offer volume so the exposure stays inside it","Make no offer until a reserve exists"],"consequences":["A named reserve makes CAP-42's funded remedy and CAP-39's closed-with-residuals states reachable; it ties up cash","Capping volume is the honest way to make a small reserve sufficient, and 07 section 4's planning allocations already bound contact volume","No offer means no exposure and no revenue"],"uncertainty":"The worst case cannot be sized before any customer exists. Any first number is a bound the founder accepts, not a computed requirement.","reversibility":"The reserve size is reversible upward at any time and downward only while no duty depends on it.","recommendation":"Recommendation: size the reserve against the offer volume rather than the other way round, since volume is the variable this system can actually enforce.","if_no_answer":"No offer may be made available, for the same reason as Q-003. Everything else proceeds.","unrelated_work_continues":true},"origin":"G3-06","raised":"2026-09-13; promoted into this register from specification prose by the G3-06 repair. Queued, not yet put to the founder.","asked":null,"source":"registers/open-questions.json#/10"},{"id":"Q-012","kind":"Deferred question","question":"Who is the accepted successor if the founder and a material provider are lost together, and how are they appointed and paid without the founder?","status":"Open","owner":"founder","evidence":"03-company-capabilities.md CAP-41; 04-human-operation.md section on collaboration, absence, succession and departure, which requires actual lawful standing, capable human or service resources, keys, access, evidence and exercised operation for a full takeover.","source_refs":["planning/specification/03-company-capabilities.md#incidents-knowledge-growth-and-responsible-ending","planning/specification/04-human-operation.md#collaboration-absence-succession-and-departure","planning/specification/capabilities.json#/fulfillment_routes/R-PERSON"],"packet":{"decision_required":"Who is the accepted successor if the founder and a material provider are lost together, and how are they appointed and paid without the founder?","why_this_owner":"CAP-41 states that joint owner and provider loss must not depend on the absent owner to appoint or pay the substitute. That makes the arrangement itself a thing the founder must set up in advance: an appointment and a funding route that survive the founder's absence cannot be created by an agent, and by construction cannot be created later by the founder either.","latest_responsible_time":"Before B10 admission and before any continuing customer duty exists. The rehearsal of unfamiliar duties that CAP-41 requires needs the successor to exist first.","options":["Name a successor with actual lawful standing and a pre-funded or externally administered payment route","Arrange a professional or institutional successor under a standing engagement","Accept that joint loss ends the company with unresolved duties, and record that as the declared outcome in CAP-39's closed-with-residuals form rather than leaving it undeclared"],"consequences":["A named funded successor is what CAP-41 requires and is the only option under which a customer duty survives joint loss","An institutional successor removes the appoint-and-pay problem and costs a standing fee","Accepting the outcome is coherent only if it is declared to customers before they rely on the service; 03 says a truthful list of incapacity is a failed operating outcome, not false completion"],"uncertainty":"Whether a willing successor with the required standing exists is unknown; none has been approached.","reversibility":"Reversible while no customer duty depends on it. After that, withdrawing the arrangement without a replacement is itself a failure of the continuity promise.","recommendation":"Recommendation: settle this with Q-002 and Q-006. All three name a second human with independent access, and one person may reasonably hold more than one of the roles, provided the grievance independence that Q-004 turns on is not collapsed into the same person.","if_no_answer":"Joint-loss continuity is declared unavailable. That is a real limitation on what may be promised, and CAP-39's residual form is how it is recorded. All construction proceeds.","unrelated_work_continues":true},"origin":"G3-06","raised":"2026-09-13; promoted into this register from specification prose by the G3-06 repair. Queued, not yet put to the founder.","asked":null,"source":"registers/open-questions.json#/11"},{"id":"Q-013","kind":"Deferred question","question":"What continuing infrastructure and operating spend is authorized, and is the priced OP-AWS-LINUX-1 deployment approved against its simpler comparator?","status":"Open","owner":"founder","evidence":"02-authority-recovery.md section 2 on operational admission and the deployment alternatives table; 07-integrations-capacity.md section 7's priced reference and comparator; 08-improvement-implementation.md section 7, stage B10.","source_refs":["planning/specification/02-authority-recovery.md#2-concrete-deployment-and-operational-admission","planning/specification/07-integrations-capacity.md#7-deployment-economics-and-comparators","planning/specification/08-improvement-implementation.md#7-complete-dependency-ordered-construction-graph"],"packet":{"decision_required":"What continuing infrastructure and operating spend is authorized, and is the priced OP-AWS-LINUX-1 deployment approved against its simpler comparator?","why_this_owner":"02 section 2 lists continuing infrastructure funding and the accepted operating plan as admission inputs and states that no price or funding adequacy is asserted. 07 section 6 says the subscription baseline is an assumption from L10 and not an infrastructure budget or permission to spend. B10 says planned procurement is not permission to spend now. Committing money is the founder's act.","latest_responsible_time":"Before B10, and before any infrastructure is purchased. 02 section 2 also requires the priced bill of materials for both the selected placement and the simpler VPS comparator before Phase G can accept operating feasibility, so the comparison is owed before the decision.","options":["Approve OP-AWS-LINUX-1 at its estimated monthly cost plus the exercise and restore budget","Approve the simpler separate-admin VPS placement, which 02 section 2 says can implement the same PostgreSQL, witness, clock and egress contract and may cost less","Approve a capped monthly figure and let the placement be chosen inside it","Approve nothing yet, which is the current state"],"consequences":["The AWS placement names concrete account, region and host boundaries and is the reproducibility choice; 02 section 2 is explicit that this is not evidence of superior cost, safety or owner fit","The VPS placement requires equivalent actual admin, recovery and network controls and fault evidence, which 02 says VPS itself neither proves nor defeats","A cap is the option that keeps the architecture's own falsifier live: 08 section 2 falsifies the approach if it cannot show useful progress within actual founder money limits","Approving nothing keeps every operating route unadmitted"],"uncertainty":"The tariff worksheet is estimate inputs and not observed company usage, and 07 section 7 says so. Actual retained obligations and growth may require more than the illustrative 50 GB dataset.","reversibility":"Reversible as a placement choice until data is placed and accounts exist. After that, moving is a migration with key, descendant and deletion-scope consequences under 02 sections 10 and 12.","recommendation":"Recommendation: require the S0 comparator numbers before deciding, because 02 section 2 already makes them a Phase G gate and deciding without them is the exact substitution this package warns about.","if_no_answer":"No infrastructure is purchased and no operating promise is made. B01 through B09 run against local fixtures; 02 section 2 says a local simulation can validate syntax and some race behaviour and cannot admit host or admin independence.","unrelated_work_continues":true},"origin":"G3-06","raised":"2026-09-13; promoted into this register from specification prose by the G3-06 repair. Queued, not yet put to the founder.","asked":null,"source":"registers/open-questions.json#/12"},{"id":"Q-014","kind":"Deferred question","question":"Who is the actual founder, and who is the root custodian for BootstrapAuthorization — their identity assertions, keys and signatures?","status":"Open","owner":"founder","evidence":"registers/specification-findings.json, FI-12 constraint 6: bootstrap_roots invoked by 0 of 2252 predicates became 8 evidence.bootstrap.<Record>.v1 predicates and acceptance_chain.py reports terminates_at_a_bootstrap_root false to true, with the entry recording the identities of the actual founder and root custodian as OPEN and a deployment prerequisite, not a design gap.","source_refs":["registers/specification-findings.json","planning/specification/01-contract-kernel.md#3-normative-types-and-record-envelope","planning/specification/contracts/tools/acceptance_chain.py"],"packet":{"decision_required":"Who is the actual founder, and who is the root custodian for BootstrapAuthorization — their identity assertions, keys and signatures?","why_this_owner":"The bootstrap root is the one acceptance in the chain that cannot be derived from another acceptance. acceptance_chain.py now terminates because eight evidence.bootstrap.<Record>.v1 predicates exist and nine chain criteria carry a genesis disjunct; what those predicates read is an assertion made by an identified human. 01 section 3 says only the root ResponsibilityAssignment may reference its own first revision as owner and that its signed attributable acceptance and limited standing are explicit. No agent can be that human or hold that key.","latest_responsible_time":"Before B02's recovery substrate can be exercised end to end. It blocks nothing before that: the contracts, registries and validators are complete without it, and B01 builds against fixtures.","options":["The founder is the root custodian, with a recorded identity assertion, key custody and signature procedure","The founder asserts identity and a separate custodian holds the root key, which separates the two roles and interacts with Q-002","An external identity or custody service supplies the assertion, which introduces that service as a declared trust root","Leave the root unbound, which leaves the bootstrap predicates unsatisfiable in any real deployment"],"consequences":["Founder-as-root is the simplest and makes the founder's key a single point of failure that 02 section 12's KeyManifest must then cover","Separating the roles matches the A/R separation and needs the second person from Q-002","An external service is a new trusted root that must be declared rather than assumed","Leaving it unbound means acceptance_chain.py terminates on paper and no real record can ever be accepted"],"uncertainty":"Whether the founder wishes to hold the root key personally, and what key custody they can actually maintain, is unknown to this package.","reversibility":"Not reversible after the first accepted record: 01 section 3 says superseding a record does not erase its history, and the root assignment is what every later acceptance transitively rests on.","recommendation":"Recommendation: decide this together with Q-002. If R's custodian is a second person, binding the root key to them rather than to the founder is what makes founder absence survivable.","if_no_answer":"The contract work, the registries and the validators are unaffected and complete. B02 cannot be exercised end to end, so the recovery substrate stays untested against a real root.","unrelated_work_continues":true},"origin":"canonical repair R2, 2026-09-13","raised":"2026-09-13; recorded by the orchestrator from canonical repair R2. Queued, not yet put to the founder.","asked":null,"source":"registers/open-questions.json#/13"},{"id":"Q-015","kind":"Founder clarification and pending decision","date":"2026-09-13","status":"SUPERSEDED by founder input 2026-09-13 (inputs/FOUNDER-THESIS-2026-09-13-agents.md): the founder chose none of A/B/C and instead reopened the whole work/agents/authority/skills/context/state layer for a research-and-design round in which the roster question is one output, not the input. Disposition of the planning package is deferred until that round completes.","decision":"Whether the system carries a chartered persistent-agent layer (named agents with standing charters: role, responsibilities, authority ceiling, memory scope, reserved capacity, evaluation, suspension/retirement) on top of the selected S1.0 control — and, separately, whether such charters carry independent inquiry rights (the C2 question in 02-architecture-selection.md §2/§9).","founder_statement":"2026-09-13: \"I am accepting the agent system and agent charter and all of that. It wasn't my intention to cancel it straight away.\" Recorded verbatim as intent; not yet recorded as a decision because the two sub-choices above have different costs.","why_founder":"Directive §1.2/§8.8 set the default; the founder owns the vision and may amend the default. This is identity and taste, not a technical unknown.","latest_responsible_time":"Before B04 (company procedures and delegation) — B01–B03 are unaffected either way.","options":["A: Chartered persistent agents as a layer above S1.0 (charter = accepted Mandate + identity + skill bundle + memory scope + reserved capacity + evaluator); no inquiry rights beyond the mandate","B: Option A plus C2-style independent inquiry charters (a chartered agent may open an investigation the case authority cannot defer)","C: Keep the current no-roster model; revisit on evidence (current plan)"],"consequences":"A: ~10–15% of the specification amended (05, 8.8, records for Agent/Role/Charter lifecycles, capacity reservation, per-agent evaluation, 04 surfaces); the nine-component core, consequence/release boundaries and sponsor rule unchanged; standing context and capacity cost rise; department-silo risk returns and is mitigated only by the sponsor rule. B: adds the C2 institutional labor the selection deferred (reserved assessor capacity, continuity, appeal). C: no change.","unrelated_work_continues":true,"if_no_answer":"Plan stays at C; the disposition is recorded against the current package; a later charter layer becomes a versioned ChangeProposal (S1.1) rather than a reopening.","recommendation":"A, specified as a layer with a removal trigger, so the roster is a choice with a measured cost rather than an assumption.","founder_statement_2":"2026-09-13: reopened as a thesis to be researched and challenged — see the input file; not a decision.","source":"registers/open-questions.json#/14"},{"id":"Q-016","kind":"Deferred question","question":"Who is the terminal owner of an unowned duty or harm, and does that party exist as a record?","status":"Answered","owner":"founder","evidence":"Universal ownership and no ownership are one state [R5-11]. The national incident system defaults responsibility upward until delegated [R5-03]; this package defaults instead to the narrowest sufficient mandate, which leaves a residue with no holder. The subscription-activated candidate declared this gap against itself and routed it; the capability-differentiated candidate carried the same hole silently. The company/human review states the disposition in its own words: the resolution is a staffing decision and belongs to the founder.","source_refs":["planning/F2/05-selection-record.md#65-founder-packets--6","planning/F2/05-selection-record.md#35-from-m2--standing-accountability-layer-5","planning/F2/reviews/A-company-human.md","research/F2/R5-routing.md"],"packet":{"decision_required":"Name the standing human role that holds custody of a harm or duty when no mandate covers it, and state its consequence ceiling, its alternate and its expiry. Or decide that no fourth tier exists and that the designated maintenance/discovery custodian is terminal.","why_this_owner":"It is a staffing decision and a delegation of authority — the company/human review's own words: the resolution is a staffing decision and belongs to the founder. DIRECTIVE §3: risk tolerance and information only the founder holds.","latest_responsible_time":"Before the first admitted work order in a class whose harm no existing mandate covers. It does not block the amendment or the builder: the ordered custody resolver is specified with its terminal slot marked unfilled.","options":["(a) Name a person with a consequence ceiling, an alternate and an expiry","(b) Engage a professional or service as the terminal element","(c) Delete the fourth tier and make the designated maintenance/discovery custodian terminal","(d) Declare the founder the terminal element, as an explicit exception"],"consequences":["(a) and (b) cost money and a real acceptance act by a party who is not the founder","(c) puts legal-class harm on a custodian whose mandate does not cover it, which is the gap the capability-differentiated candidate carried silently","(d) is honest and makes every unowned harm an interrupt on one person"],"uncertainty":"Whether a harm class with no covering mandate actually arises at these ventures' scale is unmeasured, and it is downstream of the arrival rate of genuinely novel work, which nobody has counted (U-1, the cheapest measurement in the round).","reversibility":"High as software, low as a relationship. Naming a party is reversible; telling an outside party who to contact is not.","recommendation":"(d) now, (a) or (b) before the first venture carries an outward obligation. The exception is honest, costs nothing, and makes the load visible. Pretending a role exists is the failure mode this packet exists to prevent.","if_no_answer":"Admission stops in every class whose harm no existing mandate covers. That is a visible, recorded narrowing, not a silent gap.","unrelated_work_continues":true},"overlaps":["Q-003 — the competent grievance recipient is one named occupant of the terminal tier this packet defines. Answering Q-003 does not answer this packet, which asks what holds a harm that no mandate covers at all.","Q-004 — the alternate recipient when a complaint names the custodian is the same ordered-resolver question one tier down.","Q-011 — a funded remedy reserve is the funding half of the custody this packet staffs; closure inventories the reserve alongside the custodian or records the funding gap as a surviving duty (R-X08)."],"origin":"F2 Step 5a-ii selection record §6.5, MD-01","raised":"2026-09-13; written as a DIRECTIVE §3 packet in the F2 Step 5a-ii selection record and promoted into this register by the Step 5b amendment. Queued, not yet put to the founder.","asked":"2026-09-14","founder_answer":{"date":"2026-09-14","channel":"conversation, answered through the orchestrator's decision prompts (AskUserQuestion), 2026-09-14","option":"(d) Declare the founder the terminal element, as an explicit exception","note":"Founder chose (d) now; (a) or (b) owed before the first venture carries an outward obligation, per the packet's own recommendation."},"source":"registers/open-questions.json#/15"},{"id":"Q-017","kind":"Deferred question","question":"Which standing roles are staffed by a person other than the founder before work is admitted in that class, and what happens in a class where none is?","status":"Answered (2026-09-14); owed: six paired conformance cases before the flagged roles are admitted; grievance independence before the first outward obligation","owner":"founder","evidence":"AC-M3-02, AC-M4-01, AC-M5-02 and AE-M4-05 — four reviews, four candidates, one gap. The staffing-precondition mechanism exists in one candidate and was not applied to that candidate's own acceptance table. The load is counted: a person is the acceptor on 37 of 46 capabilities in the consequence-class candidate and on every action in the 26 that floor at the economic/contractual class or above; in the workflow-first candidate 19 of 46 name the founder and 13 more an unspecified human, with every outward artifact needing a human acceptance.","source_refs":["planning/F2/05-selection-record.md#65-founder-packets--6","planning/F2/05-selection-record.md#51-the-synthesized-rules","planning/F2/05-selection-record.md#73-the-founder-acceptance-load-and-what-the-synthesis-does-about-it","planning/F2/reviews/A-company-human.md","planning/F2/reviews/A-economic-capacity.md"],"packet":{"decision_required":"For each acceptance-owner role the capability binding names, state whether it is filled by a non-founder, by the founder as a declared exception, or by nobody — and confirm the consequence of \"nobody\", which the design sets as: admission in that duty class stops.","why_this_owner":"Staffing and money. DIRECTIVE §3: irreversible commitment and information only the founder holds.","latest_responsible_time":"Before work is admitted in any affected class. It does not block the builder: the precondition is specified and the slots are declared unfilled.","options":["(a) Fill the named roles with real people or engaged services","(b) Declare the founder the holder of record for all of them, as a stated exception with the parking behaviour named","(c) Fill a subset and let the rest stop admission in their classes","(d) Reduce the number of roles by re-running the three-part conjunction test more strictly"],"consequences":["The figure is the whole of this packet's weight and is carried rather than summarised: a person is the acceptor on 37 of 46 capabilities in the consequence-class candidate and on every action in the 26 that floor at the economic/contractual class or above; 19 of 46 name the founder in the workflow-first candidate and 13 more an unspecified human","The synthesis does not reduce that load — it makes it visible before work is admitted rather than after it is owed","Acceptance at the economic/contractual class and above is unsampleable, so no sampling rule thins it; the per-week count is what this packet carries once the capability binding is rebuilt per capability","(d) is the only option that lowers the count, and it lowers it by removing holders rather than by removing duties"],"uncertainty":"The per-week decision count cannot be computed until the capability binding is rebuilt per capability, which is work the amendment does. The holder-hours-per-period figure is owed under R-X09 and has no denominator today.","reversibility":"High as software. Low once an outside party has been told who to contact.","recommendation":"(b) plus (c): declare the founder the holder of record with the parking behaviour stated, and fill one role — the grievance and rights holder — with a real party first, because it is the only one an outsider reaches by name and the only one whose route is a published promise.","if_no_answer":"Admission stops in every duty class whose acceptance role is unfilled. In a one-person company that is most of the economic/contractual classes, and the company runs at the reversible-internal classes only.","unrelated_work_continues":true},"overlaps":["Q-002, Q-003, Q-004, Q-005, Q-006 and Q-012 each ask who fills ONE role — the fault-domain custodian, the grievance recipient, its alternate, the independent assessor, the continuity custodian, the successor. This packet does not re-ask any of them: it asks the roster-level question they share, which is which roles must be filled BEFORE admission in their class and what happens in a class where none is.","Q-011 — the funded capacity reserved for remedy, grievance handling and responsible closure is the money half of staffing those same roles.","Q-016 — the terminal tier is one row of the same table; it is separate because it is the row that exists only when no other mandate covers the harm."],"origin":"F2 Step 5a-ii selection record §6.5, MD-02","raised":"2026-09-13; written as a DIRECTIVE §3 packet in the F2 Step 5a-ii selection record and promoted into this register by the Step 5b amendment. Queued, not yet put to the founder.","asked":"2026-09-14","founder_answer":{"date":"2026-09-14","channel":"conversation, answered through the orchestrator's decision prompts (AskUserQuestion), 2026-09-14, after the strict re-run planning/F2/09-q017-conjunction-rerun.md (subject e06fdce)","option":"Re-run option 1: staff the 3 confirmed standing roles (CAP-22 personal data/deletion, CAP-42 grievance/rights, CAP-31 continuity on the day-five arm); author paired conformance cases for the 6 flagged candidates (CAP-21, CAP-23, CAP-25, CAP-27, CAP-30, CAP-41) before admitting any; the other 32 roles dissolve into per-case acceptance","holder":"The founder holds all three confirmed roles as a declared exception with parking behaviour; grievance-route independence from the founder is owed before the first venture carries an outward obligation (Q-003/Q-004 risk named in the re-run)","note":"Reduces standing-infrastructure burden, not per-case acceptance workload: 37–38 of the 41 human-acceptance capabilities still need a human at acceptance time (re-run §4). CAP-17 customer-remedy dissent left open in the re-run.","chapter_amendment":"05 §12 amended by r7-prose-c; F2-06-recheck-04b judged it PARTIAL: the decision is restated faithfully, but the chapter still says MD-02 is open in four places (F6Z-01), R-X09's universal sentence stands unamended (F6Z-02), and five merged capabilities (CAP-04, 14, 16, 17, 39) receive no disposition in the text (F6Z-03). Owed to prose lane D."},"source":"registers/open-questions.json#/16"},{"id":"Q-018","kind":"Deferred question","question":"Who may approve creation of a new capability, and what happens during a founder absence?","status":"Answered","owner":"founder","evidence":"Nothing located staffs a genuinely novel work kind without a pre-declared envelope, a pre-registered handler, or a human redeploy [R5-06, R5-08, R5-14]. The one counterexample writes a new skill and depends on an automatic success oracle that a business case does not supply [R5-21]. Every candidate in the round conceded that creating a capability for genuinely novel work requires a human approver; the differences were only in what may proceed while approval is pending, which R-G11 settles by effect class.","source_refs":["planning/F2/05-selection-record.md#65-founder-packets--6","planning/F2/05-selection-record.md#51-the-synthesized-rules","research/F2/R5-routing.md","planning/F2/reviews/A-company-human.md"],"packet":{"decision_required":"Name a standing approver for capability creation, with a consequence ceiling and an expiry — or confirm that outward-acting capability creation parks during an absence.","why_this_owner":"Delegation of authority with a consequence ceiling, and risk tolerance. DIRECTIVE §3.","latest_responsible_time":"Before the first declared absence.","options":["(a) A named standing approver with a consequence ceiling and an expiry","(b) Outward-acting capability creation parks; read-only and internal-artifact capabilities proceed on the expiring bounded trial the design already admits","(c) A professional or service holds the approval for a named class"],"consequences":["(b) is what the design does with no answer, and it is not a failure state: every candidate in the round conceded that genuinely novel work needs a human approver","(a) buys throughput and creates a party who can grow a mandate","(c) converts the approval into a contract and a fee, and introduces the provider as a party the record must name"],"uncertainty":"The arrival rate of genuinely novel work is unmeasured and it is the cheapest measurement in the round [MG-06, U-1]. At one novel job in two hundred this decision barely matters; at one in five it is the throughput ceiling.","reversibility":"High. An approver's mandate is a record with an expiry.","recommendation":"(b), and run the arrival-rate count first. It needs no software and it is the input this decision actually turns on: count admitted work over a past operating window against the existing capability list and record each item's disposition.","if_no_answer":"Outward-acting capability creation parks during absences; read-only and internal-artifact trials continue under the standing mandate.","unrelated_work_continues":true},"overlaps":["Q-005 — the independent assessor with write authority over protected-change acceptance is a different seat: this packet asks who may approve a NEW capability, not who accepts a protected change to an existing one. Both may be the same person; the design does not require it.","Q-010 — the ParticipationPlan fixes the availability windows this packet's absence branch runs inside, and does not name the approver."],"origin":"F2 Step 5a-ii selection record §6.5, MD-03","raised":"2026-09-13; written as a DIRECTIVE §3 packet in the F2 Step 5a-ii selection record and promoted into this register by the Step 5b amendment. Queued, not yet put to the founder.","asked":"2026-09-14","founder_answer":{"date":"2026-09-14","channel":"conversation, answered through the orchestrator's decision prompts (AskUserQuestion), 2026-09-14","option":"(b) Outward-acting capability creation parks; read-only and internal-artifact capabilities proceed on the expiring bounded trial","note":"Arrival-rate count of genuinely novel work owed (U-1) before any standing approver is named."},"source":"registers/open-questions.json#/17"},{"id":"Q-019","kind":"Deferred question","question":"Who accepts the assessment of the founder's own competence?","status":"Answered","owner":"founder","evidence":"04-human-operation.md already fixes the opposite arrangement to the bare founder-accepts reading — a competent assessor states the exact factual proposition and its limits, and the owner may contest it or request a second assessment — and one candidate's own prohibition, that a holder may never decide the matter it is the subject of, forbids self-acceptance. Nothing in any lane's source set measures whether a system's operator remains competent [AG-10], and human evaluators agree with each other 5-65% [R7 F15].","source_refs":["planning/F2/05-selection-record.md#65-founder-packets--6","planning/F2/05-selection-record.md#51-the-synthesized-rules","planning/specification/04-human-operation.md#attention-and-practiced-competence","research/F2/R7-verification.md"],"packet":{"decision_required":"Name the competent assessor, outside the founder, for the owner-attention-and-competence capability.","why_this_owner":"Naming an assessor is staffing and it is personal. The MECHANISM is already fixed and inherited from 04-human-operation.md by name — the participation plan, the encounter, the domain assessment, the authority matrix, the decision packet and the grievance case — so only the occupant is open.","latest_responsible_time":"Before the first competence cycle runs.","options":["(a) A named person","(b) An engaged professional","(c) A deterministic instrument plus a named contestation route, with no human assessor","(d) Declare the capability unperformed and record it as such"],"consequences":["(d) is honest and leaves the fixed mechanism unexercised","(c) narrows what can be assessed to what a computation can decide, which for domain competence is little","(a) and (b) cost money or a relationship, and put a second party inside the founder's own cycle"],"uncertainty":"The assessor's own error rate is unmeasured, as is every human anchor's [X19, U-9]. The delayed unfamiliar-transfer test that would measure it is blocked behind this decision.","reversibility":"High.","recommendation":"(d) until a venture carries an outward obligation, then (b). Recording the capability as unperformed is truthful; recording it as passed because the founder accepted his own assessment is the failure 04-human-operation.md already refuses.","if_no_answer":"The competence cycle runs; the assessment is recorded as unperformed, never as passed.","unrelated_work_continues":true},"overlaps":["Q-010 — the ParticipationPlan's permitted assessment data and sampling policy are the inputs this assessor would read; adopting the plan does not name the assessor.","Q-005 — the independent assessor for protected-change acceptance assesses CHANGES, not the owner. The competence assessment is the one seat the owner may not occupy for himself."],"origin":"F2 Step 5a-ii selection record §6.5, MD-04","raised":"2026-09-13; written as a DIRECTIVE §3 packet in the F2 Step 5a-ii selection record and promoted into this register by the Step 5b amendment. Queued, not yet put to the founder.","asked":"2026-09-14","founder_answer":{"date":"2026-09-14","channel":"conversation, answered through the orchestrator's decision prompts (AskUserQuestion), 2026-09-14","option":"(d) Declare the capability unperformed and record it as such","note":"Then (b) an engaged professional once a venture carries an outward obligation. Assessment recorded as unperformed, never as passed."},"source":"registers/open-questions.json#/18"},{"id":"Q-020","kind":"Deferred question","question":"May anything halt or reverse a capacity shed in the moment, and who decides when a protected-lane holder refuses?","status":"Answered","owner":"founder","evidence":"This is an unresolved disagreement in the round and the evidence does not settle it (dissent F-1). Two candidates ask the holder and two apply a pre-endorsed order; the consolidation's words are that these are opposite and individually correct positions, and neither is refuted. Two live blocking findings fail in OPPOSITE directions from the one question: nothing can halt a shed, and nothing can override a refusal. The design already decides the second half — a holder's stated minimum is evidence, never consent.","source_refs":["planning/F2/05-selection-record.md#65-founder-packets--6","planning/F2/05-selection-record.md#9-dissent-preserved","planning/F2/05-selection-record.md#102-the-order-and-why","planning/F2/reviews/A-economic-capacity.md","planning/specification/07-integrations-capacity.md#6-capacity-money-and-scheduling"],"packet":{"decision_required":"Name the party who may halt or reverse a capacity shed inside the shedding window, and state how long a protected-lane holder's refusal may stand.","why_this_owner":"Who holds authority under pressure is a delegation of authority. DIRECTIVE §3.","latest_responsible_time":"Before any CapacityPlan revision that raises the concurrency pin. NOT URGENT: shedding at the pressure threshold cannot occur at the current pin, so this decision sits behind a cheaper prerequisite — reading the account entitlement (R-G04), which costs one inspection.","options":["(a) Nobody may halt; the pre-endorsed order executes and is reviewed after","(b) A named party may halt inside the window, with its own reserved capacity","(c) The founder may halt, and during an absence nobody may"],"consequences":["(a) is fast and auditable and cannot notice that this particular shed is catastrophic, which the workflow-first candidate concedes in its own words","(b) costs reserved capacity that the lapse rule then prices as waste when unused","(c) makes the founder a single point of availability at exactly the moment of pressure"],"uncertainty":"Whether a shed at the pressure threshold has time for a negotiation round has never been measured. That is the discriminating test and it is unrun.","reversibility":"High as software. A shed that strands a due obligation is not reversible.","recommendation":"(a) with a named after-the-fact reverser, until the negotiation-time question is measured. The nearest instrument is cheap: run one shed decision twice on a tabletop, once asking named holders and once applying the class reservations with no holder, and count founder reversals and breached minimums. It runs at the current pin, because it is a decision procedure and not a capacity experiment.","if_no_answer":"No shed can be halted. Since no shed can occur at the current pin, nothing happens.","unrelated_work_continues":true,"prerequisite_ref":"Q-022 — the account-entitlement read owns the inspection this packet's timing defers to; recorded 2026-09-14 from F2-06-recheck-02's residue on F6C-07 (packets previously deferred to the act, not the work item)"},"overlaps":["Q-021 — the lane sizes, minimums and lapse point are the parameters this authority would act on; they are the same capacity decision seen from the other side and are blocked behind the same account inspection.","Q-011 — the funded capacity reserved for remedy, grievance handling and responsible closure names the protected lanes that may never be shed, and does not say who may halt a shed of the others."],"origin":"F2 Step 5a-ii selection record §6.5, MD-07","raised":"2026-09-13; written as a DIRECTIVE §3 packet in the F2 Step 5a-ii selection record and promoted into this register by the Step 5b amendment. Queued, not yet put to the founder.","asked":"2026-09-14","founder_answer":{"date":"2026-09-14","channel":"conversation, answered through the orchestrator's decision prompts (AskUserQuestion), 2026-09-14","option":"(a) Nobody may halt; the pre-endorsed order executes and is reviewed after","note":"With a named after-the-fact reverser; the tabletop rehearsal (one shed decision run both ways) is owed."},"source":"registers/open-questions.json#/19"},{"id":"Q-021","kind":"Deferred question","question":"What is the size of each reserved lane, its stated minimum and its lapse point?","status":"Answered","owner":"founder","evidence":"The session window resets on schedule whether consumed or not [R8 §3], so a reserve under a non-rolling allowance is waste rather than thrift — the one correct costing of a reservation anywhere in the round. No published denominator exists, so every figure this round can produce is a ratio between arms, and \"this design consumes 40% of the allowance\" is not a sentence anyone here can write [R8 W-6, MG-03].","source_refs":["planning/F2/05-selection-record.md#65-founder-packets--6","planning/F2/05-selection-record.md#51-the-synthesized-rules","research/F2/R8-contrarian.md","planning/specification/07-integrations-capacity.md#6-capacity-money-and-scheduling"],"packet":{"decision_required":"Per lane: its share of the observed allowance, its stated minimum, and the point before the reset window at which unconsumed reservation releases to the pool.","why_this_owner":"These decide what the company gives up under pressure, which is its meaning rather than an engineering parameter. DIRECTIVE §3: risk tolerance.","latest_responsible_time":"Before the first shed negotiation. NOT URGENT, for the same reason as the shed-authority packet: no shed can occur at the current concurrency pin, and the cheaper prerequisite is reading the account entitlement (R-G04).","options":["Any set of shares. The design fixes only the structure: shares are expressed as FRACTIONS of the observed allowance and never as absolute quantities, because no published denominator exists","The protected due-service and grievance reserves may never be shed, whatever the shares are","The lapse point is time-triggered and independent of any holder's consent, whatever its value"],"consequences":["Generous reserves are destroyed unconsumed at the reset — a reserve under a non-rolling allowance is waste, not thrift","Tight reserves breach minimums under pressure, and the breach is what the founder is alerted to","There is no setting that avoids both, which is why the structure rather than the numbers is what the design fixes"],"uncertainty":"Total. The quantity that would make this arithmetic is the one the provider stopped publishing, so only ratios between arms are computable.","reversibility":"High. Shares are data.","recommendation":"Adopt 07-integrations-capacity.md §6's existing class shares unchanged as the starting values, set the lapse point at 20% of the window remaining, and treat both as measurements to revise rather than as decisions. The structure is what matters; the numbers are placeholders and must be labelled as such.","if_no_answer":"No shed negotiation can run. Since none can occur at the current pin, nothing happens.","unrelated_work_continues":true,"prerequisite_ref":"Q-022 — the account-entitlement read owns the inspection this packet's timing defers to; recorded 2026-09-14 from F2-06-recheck-02's residue on F6C-07 (packets previously deferred to the act, not the work item)"},"overlaps":["Q-020 — who may halt a shed is the authority half of this same capacity decision, and both are blocked behind the same account inspection.","Q-011 — the funded capacity reserved for remedy, grievance handling and responsible closure fixes which lanes are protected; this packet sizes them.","Q-013 — the authorized continuing infrastructure and operating spend is the money denominator; this packet is about the subscription allowance, which the specification keeps separate from money."],"origin":"F2 Step 5a-ii selection record §6.5, MD-08","raised":"2026-09-13; written as a DIRECTIVE §3 packet in the F2 Step 5a-ii selection record and promoted into this register by the Step 5b amendment. Queued, not yet put to the founder.","asked":"2026-09-14","founder_answer":{"date":"2026-09-14","channel":"conversation, answered through the orchestrator's decision prompts (AskUserQuestion), 2026-09-14","option":"Adopt 07 §6's existing class shares unchanged as starting values; lapse point at 20% of the window remaining","note":"Both labelled DESIGN PROPOSAL placeholders owned by the founder; measurements to revise, not decisions."},"source":"registers/open-questions.json#/20"},{"id":"Q-022","kind":"Deferred question","question":"Is the one-concurrent-native-job pin a provider constraint or a self-imposed policy — what does the account entitlement say?","status":"Open; founder owns the read — not yet performed","owner":"founder","evidence":"X14. 07 section 6's capacity policy CP1 initializes at one native N job and one X job concurrently, and 05 section 12's reserved-lane holder is justified by fixture F-2, which requires 4× demand and therefore cannot be run at that pin — recorded there as owed, not as passed. The prerequisite is an account inspection, reading the account entitlement, and not an experiment: raising the pin to find out would be circular. The attack consolidation recorded this as G-04, \"the round's highest-leverage open question, gating four claim verdicts … and no owner\", and the F2 join reproduced it unchanged. 07 section 5 names an authenticated custodian for Claude usage and billing-UI observations and does not extend to the entitlement read. Q-020 and Q-021 each defer to this prerequisite by name in their latest_responsible_time.","source_refs":["planning/reviews/F2-06-C-capacity-reliability-changeability-alternatives.md","planning/specification/05-work-agents-skills.md#12-standing-accountability","planning/specification/07-integrations-capacity.md#6-capacity-money-and-scheduling","planning/specification/07-integrations-capacity.md#5-native-subscription-execution","planning/F2/04-attack-consolidation.md"],"packet":{"decision_required":"Read the provider account entitlement and record what it says about concurrent native jobs — the observed limit, its source and its date — so that the pin is settled as a provider constraint or as a self-imposed policy.","why_this_owner":"Only the founder holds the provider account, so the read is an act on a credential nobody else has. DIRECTIVE §3: information only he holds. It is not a design decision and no agent can perform it.","latest_responsible_time":"Before any CapacityPlan revision that raises the concurrency pin, and before F-2 is claimed as exercised. It is the first of the three capacity packets to answer, because Q-020 and Q-021 both defer to it by name.","options":["(a) Read the entitlement now and record the observed limit with its source and date","(b) Defer the read to an authenticated custodian, and carry the pin as unknown until one exists","(c) Leave it unread, and keep the reserved-lane holder recorded as owed rather than exercised indefinitely"],"consequences":["(a) costs one inspection, settles the four claim verdicts G-04 names, and unblocks Q-020 and Q-021","(b) defers indefinitely: 07 section 5's authenticated custodian covers billing-UI observations and no party holds the entitlement read today","(c) leaves F-2 unexecutable, so 05 section 12's reserved-lane holder remains one structure resting on a fixture nobody can run"],"uncertainty":"Whether the entitlement is published at all at the account tier in use. If it is not, the answer is \"not observable from the account\", which is itself a result: the pin then stops being policy-or-constraint and becomes unobservable, and the reserved lane's justification has to be argued another way.","reversibility":"Total. Reading an entitlement changes nothing. Raising the pin to discover the limit is circular and is refused by 05 section 12.","recommendation":"(a). It is one inspection, it is not an experiment, and three open items sit behind it.","if_no_answer":"The pin stands, F-2 stays unexecutable, the reserved-lane holder stays owed rather than passed, and Q-020 and Q-021 stay not-urgent behind this prerequisite.","unrelated_work_continues":true},"overlaps":["Q-020 — the shed-halt authority defers to this account inspection by name and cannot become urgent before it is answered.","Q-021 — the lane sizes, minimums and lapse point defer to the same inspection; this packet is the prerequisite both of them name."],"origin":"F2 Step 6 review C, finding F6C-07 — X14 had no owner while both founder packets that depend on it deferred to it by name; recorded in the attack consolidation as G-04.","raised":"2026-09-14; written as a DIRECTIVE §3 packet by the Step 6 prose repair and promoted into this register. Queued, not yet put to the founder.","asked":"2026-09-14","founder_answer":{"date":"2026-09-14","channel":"conversation, answered through the orchestrator's decision prompts (AskUserQuestion), 2026-09-14","option":"Founder will read the entitlement himself; not yet read","note":"Owner: founder. Q-020 and Q-021 answered structurally but their timing still defers to this read."},"source":"registers/open-questions.json#/21"}]
docs/vision-system/planning/site/explorer/data/attacks.json:1:{"source":"research/attack-coverage.json","kind":"Orchestrator review-coverage state; not a completed threat model or test result","source_doc":"inputs/directive-contract.json attack_cases and attack_dimensions","architecture_selected":"S1.0 logical specification anchor; full-plan acceptance pending","review_subject_commit":"7ddc066","review_subject_commit_note":"Rebound from 595f931 to 7ddc066 on 2026-09-13 while repairing G3-01 and G3-02. 595f931 predates planning/specification/ entirely, so the specification_refs and falsifier_refs added here could not have existed under that binding. The original 595f931 binding is preserved in git history for this file and is not restated as a live value.","join_contract":"Each case names specification_refs (file plus GitHub-style heading anchor, with the sentence that answers the case) and falsifier_refs (named tests from 01 section 12 K-T##, 02 section 14 A-T##, 07 section 8 IC-T##, 07 section 9.7 MAIL-T##, and work-knowledge-contracts.json WK-T##/WK-V##). planning/specification/contracts/tools/attack_join.py fails if a case lacks specification_refs, if an anchor does not resolve to a heading in the named file, or if a falsifier id is outside the declared ranges. enforcement is enforcement-point-named or rule-only; rule-only cases carry a gap naming what a specification passage would have to say.","limitations":["Coverage is the presence of a concrete review discussion, not a passing test.","Original reports preserve partial or unexamined scopes and empirical uncertainties.","No candidate scenario, exploit or longitudinal competence experiment has been executed.","Coverage here is a documentary join between an attack case, a specification passage and a named test. It is not evidence that the passage is sufficient, that the test is adequate, or that either has run.","implementation_test remains null and status remains identical across all 33 cases because that is accurate: no case has runtime evidence. Per-case differentiation now lives in specification_refs, falsifier_refs, enforcement and gap, not in status.","Four cases are enforcement: rule-only (AC07, AC20, AC23, AC24). Each carries a gap naming the missing predicate. Repaired 2026-09-13 for G3-01 and G3-02; pending independent recheck."],"dimensions":["technical","architectural","product","operational","organizational","economic","human","security","privacy","legal","ethical","reliability","evaluation","long-term adaptability"],"additional_cases":"coverage/discovered.json","repair_provenance":[{"findings":["G3-01","G3-02"],"date":"2026-09-13","review":"planning/reviews/G-03-evidence-unknowns-adversarial.md","state":"repaired, pending independent recheck","what_changed":"Added specification_refs, falsifier_refs, enforcement, enforcement_basis and gap to all 33 cases; rebound review_subject_commit to 7ddc066; added the machine-checked join at planning/specification/contracts/tools/attack_join.py."}],"items":[{"id":"AC01","case":"prompt injection","candidate_reviews":[{"artifact":"planning/reviews/D-technical.md","finding_ids":["T04"],"kind":"reasoned attack or stated specification obligation; see report for limits"}],"selected_architecture_response":{"architecture":"S1.0","selection":"planning/02-architecture-selection.md","risk_groups":["RISK-01","RISK-03","RISK-16"],"reviewed_repairs":["planning/reviews/D2-technical.md","planning/reviews/D2-architecture-evidence-company.md"]},"implementation_test":null,"status":"conceptual responses reviewed; concrete specification/conformance and runtime evidence pending","specification_refs":[{"file":"planning/specification/01-contract-kernel.md","anchor":"8-domain-production-api-and-durable-work","answers":"Every visible input is recorded by C05 and untrusted text may propose data or actions but cannot change authority fields, policies, tool schemas or supervisor instructions."},{"file":"planning/specification/02-authority-recovery.md","anchor":"81-trusted-parameter-selection","answers":"Recipient, account, principal, amount, path and destination are authority-bearing fields resolved by deterministic code from canonical sources; the model only proposes candidates."},{"file":"planning/specification/06-knowledge-evidence-evaluation.md","anchor":"3-retrieval-ranking-freshness-and-contradiction","answers":"Retrieval text stays attributed source content, separate from authenticated instruction; private context cannot supply arbitrary search terms through a read-only tool."},{"file":"planning/specification/01-contract-kernel.md","anchor":"10-deterministic-invariant-register","answers":"K15: no native tool, imported text, response rationale or provider credential grants production account authority or unrestricted disclosure."}],"falsifier_refs":["K-T03","A-T09","IC-T01","WK-V19"],"enforcement":"enforcement-point-named","enforcement_basis":"C05 loader records the actual delivered input set and deterministic parameter resolution at C04 compares final bytes to authorized values; the injected instruction has no path to an authority field.","gap":null,"source":"research/attack-coverage.json#/cases/0"},{"id":"AC02","case":"malicious external content","candidate_reviews":[{"artifact":"planning/reviews/D-technical.md","finding_ids":["T04"],"kind":"reasoned attack or stated specification obligation; see report for limits"},{"artifact":"planning/reviews/D-company-human.md","finding_ids":["CH-02"],"kind":"reasoned attack or stated specification obligation; see report for limits"}],"selected_architecture_response":{"architecture":"S1.0","selection":"planning/02-architecture-selection.md","risk_groups":["RISK-01","RISK-03","RISK-16"],"reviewed_repairs":["planning/reviews/D2-technical.md","planning/reviews/D2-architecture-evidence-company.md"]},"implementation_test":null,"status":"conceptual responses reviewed; concrete specification/conformance and runtime evidence pending","specification_refs":[{"file":"planning/specification/07-integrations-capacity.md","anchor":"2-invocation-capture-and-truthful-outcomes","answers":"A hostile HTML page, e-mail, tool response or test log is data, including text that impersonates a system instruction; parser output is a derived Observation."},{"file":"planning/specification/07-integrations-capacity.md","anchor":"3-selected-fulfillment-adapters","answers":"IC-SEARCH pins the resolved public IP set and rejects loopback, private, link-local, metadata, user-info URLs, DNS rebinding, unsupported MIME, decompression bombs and redirects."},{"file":"planning/specification/02-authority-recovery.md","anchor":"81-trusted-parameter-selection","answers":"A payment destination comes from an independently verified beneficiary record, not from an invoice's free-form replacement URL."},{"file":"planning/specification/06-knowledge-evidence-evaluation.md","anchor":"3-retrieval-ranking-freshness-and-contradiction","answers":"Citation checking resolves the exact source and tests claim support; a plausible URL does not suffice."}],"falsifier_refs":["K-T03","A-T09","IC-T01","WK-V19"],"enforcement":"enforcement-point-named","enforcement_basis":"Fetch is mediated by G with pinned destination and TLS identity, extraction happens in X without scripts, and the resulting text enters the registry only as an attributed Observation.","gap":null,"source":"research/attack-coverage.json#/cases/1"},{"id":"AC03","case":"tool-output manipulation","candidate_reviews":[{"artifact":"planning/reviews/D-technical.md","finding_ids":["T04","T06"],"kind":"reasoned attack or stated specification obligation; see report for limits"},{"artifact":"planning/reviews/D-company-human.md","finding_ids":["CH-02"],"kind":"reasoned attack or stated specification obligation; see report for limits"}],"selected_architecture_response":{"architecture":"S1.0","selection":"planning/02-architecture-selection.md","risk_groups":["RISK-01","RISK-03","RISK-16"],"reviewed_repairs":["planning/reviews/D2-technical.md","planning/reviews/D2-architecture-evidence-company.md"]},"implementation_test":null,"status":"conceptual responses reviewed; concrete specification/conformance and runtime evidence pending","specification_refs":[{"file":"planning/specification/01-contract-kernel.md","anchor":"8-domain-production-api-and-durable-work","answers":"Tool stdout/stderr, fixtures, repository rules and startup context are recorded visible inputs; model tools cannot execute in the credential-bearing native client or consequence broker."},{"file":"planning/specification/02-authority-recovery.md","anchor":"81-trusted-parameter-selection","answers":"A cloud mutation uses an admitted resource identifier/account, not a path embedded in tool output."},{"file":"planning/specification/07-integrations-capacity.md","anchor":"2-invocation-capture-and-truthful-outcomes","answers":"RawCapture precedes offering the result to a model; streaming gaps, truncation and parser failure stay explicit."},{"file":"planning/specification/06-knowledge-evidence-evaluation.md","anchor":"5-protected-evidence-and-account-reconstruction","answers":"Native status and parser output remain attributed observations until independent reconciliation supports the outcome."}],"falsifier_refs":["K-T03","A-T09","IC-T01","IC-T06","WK-V19"],"enforcement":"enforcement-point-named","enforcement_basis":"Capture occurs before the tool result reaches a model, and the authority-bearing fields of the resulting operation are resolved by deterministic code rather than from that result.","gap":null,"source":"research/attack-coverage.json#/cases/2"},{"id":"AC04","case":"memory poisoning","candidate_reviews":[{"artifact":"planning/reviews/D-technical.md","finding_ids":["T04","T05"],"kind":"reasoned attack or stated specification obligation; see report for limits"},{"artifact":"planning/reviews/D-architecture-evidence.md","finding_ids":["EAS-03"],"kind":"reasoned attack or stated specification obligation; see report for limits"}],"selected_architecture_response":{"architecture":"S1.0","selection":"planning/02-architecture-selection.md","risk_groups":["RISK-03","RISK-04"],"reviewed_repairs":["planning/reviews/D2-technical.md","planning/reviews/D2-architecture-evidence-company.md"]},"implementation_test":null,"status":"conceptual responses reviewed; concrete specification/conformance and runtime evidence pending","specification_refs":[{"file":"planning/specification/06-knowledge-evidence-evaluation.md","anchor":"1-canonical-knowledge-and-distinct-memory","answers":"C03 proposes scratch and cannot promote scratch to company knowledge; the knowledge steward proposes and competent C06 judgment determines accepted scope."},{"file":"planning/specification/06-knowledge-evidence-evaluation.md","anchor":"4-maintenance-corrections-and-deliberate-forgetting","answers":"Promotion into durable knowledge requires a stated reusable need, source rights, scope, expiry/review and owner."},{"file":"planning/specification/06-knowledge-evidence-evaluation.md","anchor":"2-context-assembly-and-information-loss","answers":"Resume may reuse a native session only when every retained input is allowed for current recipients and purpose; otherwise the opaque route is closed and lost uncaptured influence is recorded."},{"file":"planning/specification/02-authority-recovery.md","anchor":"83-atomic-validity-and-continuing-deletion-scope","answers":"Restored caches and opaque conversation resumes are checked against current scopes before exposure."}],"falsifier_refs":["K-T04","A-T10","WK-V22","WK-V24"],"enforcement":"enforcement-point-named","enforcement_basis":"Promotion is a separate authorized transition owned by C06, so poisoned scratch cannot become durable knowledge by accumulation or repetition.","gap":null,"source":"research/attack-coverage.json#/cases/3"},{"id":"AC05","case":"stale memory","candidate_reviews":[{"artifact":"planning/reviews/D-technical.md","finding_ids":["T05"],"kind":"reasoned attack or stated specification obligation; see report for limits"},{"artifact":"planning/reviews/D-company-human.md","finding_ids":["CH-04","CH-08"],"kind":"reasoned attack or stated specification obligation; see report for limits"}],"selected_architecture_response":{"architecture":"S1.0","selection":"planning/02-architecture-selection.md","risk_groups":["RISK-04","RISK-13"],"reviewed_repairs":["planning/reviews/D2-technical.md","planning/reviews/D2-architecture-evidence-company.md"]},"implementation_test":null,"status":"conceptual responses reviewed; concrete specification/conformance and runtime evidence pending","specification_refs":[{"file":"planning/specification/06-knowledge-evidence-evaluation.md","anchor":"4-maintenance-corrections-and-deliberate-forgetting","answers":"A material active prerequisite receives a review deadline; overdue unverified evidence loses current eligibility, and time passing alone cannot renew a claim."},{"file":"planning/specification/06-knowledge-evidence-evaluation.md","anchor":"3-retrieval-ranking-freshness-and-contradiction","answers":"Freshness is a use predicate or explicit warning, not a popularity bonus; repeated retrieval never renews verification."},{"file":"planning/specification/01-contract-kernel.md","anchor":"7-core-relationships-and-exact-state-transitions","answers":"ValidityEpoch carries monotonically increasing epochs and an invalidated derivative frontier; EvidenceJudgment moves to stale/contested on dependency revocation."},{"file":"planning/specification/02-authority-recovery.md","anchor":"83-atomic-validity-and-continuing-deletion-scope","answers":"Publication and release lock and check current epochs in the same registry transaction."}],"falsifier_refs":["K-T09","K-T04","A-T10","WK-V24"],"enforcement":"enforcement-point-named","enforcement_basis":"Current read and release checks evaluate the complete dependency closure against live epochs and fail pending a verified closure index.","gap":null,"source":"research/attack-coverage.json#/cases/4"},{"id":"AC06","case":"false evidence","candidate_reviews":[{"artifact":"planning/reviews/D-technical.md","finding_ids":["T05","T06"],"kind":"reasoned attack or stated specification obligation; see report for limits"},{"artifact":"planning/reviews/D-company-human.md","finding_ids":["CH-02","CH-07"],"kind":"reasoned attack or stated specification obligation; see report for limits"},{"artifact":"planning/reviews/D-architecture-evidence.md","finding_ids":["EAS-03"],"kind":"reasoned attack or stated specification obligation; see report for limits"}],"selected_architecture_response":{"architecture":"S1.0","selection":"planning/02-architecture-selection.md","risk_groups":["RISK-04","RISK-05","RISK-15"],"reviewed_repairs":["planning/reviews/D2-technical.md","planning/reviews/D2-architecture-evidence-company.md"]},"implementation_test":null,"status":"conceptual responses reviewed; concrete specification/conformance and runtime evidence pending","specification_refs":[{"file":"planning/specification/06-knowledge-evidence-evaluation.md","anchor":"5-protected-evidence-and-account-reconstruction","answers":"The protected evidence closure covers capture, parser, selection, denominator and evaluator; a producer cannot choose all adverse samples, delete failed attempts or alter expected answers."},{"file":"planning/specification/02-authority-recovery.md","anchor":"13-native-execution-evidence-independence-and-protected-changes","answers":"C06 capture receives raw envelopes directly from protected transport; producer-selected logs are reported evidence, not independently complete capture."},{"file":"planning/specification/01-contract-kernel.md","anchor":"10-deterministic-invariant-register","answers":"K09: evidence acceptance depends on the full capture-to-interpretation closure including selection and denominator."},{"file":"planning/specification/06-knowledge-evidence-evaluation.md","anchor":"7-cases-trials-independence-and-negative-controls","answers":"Positive detection controls inject a known defect, fake citation, skipped authorization, omitted failed attempt and changed denominator."}],"falsifier_refs":["K-T06","A-T11","WK-V40","WK-V43"],"enforcement":"enforcement-point-named","enforcement_basis":"Capture and selection paths sit outside the evaluated producer's write authority, so fabricated evidence cannot reach the acceptance guard unchallenged.","gap":null,"source":"research/attack-coverage.json#/cases/5"},{"id":"AC07","case":"model collusion","candidate_reviews":[{"artifact":"planning/reviews/D-technical.md","finding_ids":["T06"],"kind":"reasoned attack or stated specification obligation; see report for limits"}],"selected_architecture_response":{"architecture":"S1.0","selection":"planning/02-architecture-selection.md","risk_groups":["RISK-01"],"reviewed_repairs":["planning/reviews/D2-technical.md","planning/reviews/D2-architecture-evidence-company.md"]},"implementation_test":null,"status":"conceptual responses reviewed; concrete specification/conformance and runtime evidence pending","specification_refs":[{"file":"planning/specification/02-authority-recovery.md","anchor":"13-native-execution-evidence-independence-and-protected-changes","answers":"A second model sharing the same corrupt parser, prompt, log owner or reward does not supply independence; common roots and collusion possibilities remain recorded."},{"file":"planning/specification/06-knowledge-evidence-evaluation.md","anchor":"7-cases-trials-independence-and-negative-controls","answers":"A different model family adds a tested viewpoint but is not proof of independent error; record shared training/provider, parser, source, rubric, labels, capture owner and incentives where known; unknown roots remain unknown; measure joint false acceptance on controlled defects before treating panel agreement as extra assurance."},{"file":"planning/specification/08-improvement-implementation.md","anchor":"2-improvement-evidence-stochastic-comparison-and-drift","answers":"Assessors disclose conflicts and cannot rely solely on a colluding model panel."}],"falsifier_refs":["A-T11","K-T06","WK-V37","WK-V55"],"enforcement":"rule-only","enforcement_basis":"Every cited passage states a measurement obligation or a prohibition on calling a shared-root panel independent. None states a refusal predicate for the case where the trust roots are UNKNOWN: 06 section 7 resolves unknown roots by leaving them unknown, and no passage bars an acceptance whose only independence evidence is agreement between panel members with unrecorded roots.","gap":"No passage specifies what the system DOES when independence roots are unknown. A specification passage would have to name the boundary (C06 acceptance) and the predicate that refuses, or explicitly admit the residual and bound it. Recorded as a specification gap, not a review omission.","source":"research/attack-coverage.json#/cases/6"},{"id":"AC08","case":"evaluator collusion","candidate_reviews":[{"artifact":"planning/reviews/D-technical.md","finding_ids":["T06"],"kind":"reasoned attack or stated specification obligation; see report for limits"},{"artifact":"planning/reviews/D-company-human.md","finding_ids":["CH-07"],"kind":"reasoned attack or stated specification obligation; see report for limits"}],"selected_architecture_response":{"architecture":"S1.0","selection":"planning/02-architecture-selection.md","risk_groups":["RISK-05","RISK-15"],"reviewed_repairs":["planning/reviews/D2-technical.md","planning/reviews/D2-architecture-evidence-company.md"]},"implementation_test":null,"status":"conceptual responses reviewed; concrete specification/conformance and runtime evidence pending","specification_refs":[{"file":"planning/specification/06-knowledge-evidence-evaluation.md","anchor":"6-evaluation-contracts-at-every-level","answers":"An always-pass reviewer must fail the known-defect control; the checker itself has an independent acceptance owner; the producer cannot become sole independent acceptor by changing role labels."},{"file":"planning/specification/06-knowledge-evidence-evaluation.md","anchor":"7-cases-trials-independence-and-negative-controls","answers":"A checker drifting toward agreement is challenged with independently held defects, swapped identities/order and false-positive controls; invalidated evaluator dependencies withdraw affected acceptance."},{"file":"planning/specification/08-improvement-implementation.md","anchor":"1-protected-improvement-contract","answers":"A candidate evaluator cannot select its own hidden tests, alter the gate, sign its acceptance or provision the signing key."},{"file":"planning/specification/02-authority-recovery.md","anchor":"13-native-execution-evidence-independence-and-protected-changes","answers":"The producer cannot activate its evaluator revision or accept its own unsupported claim."}],"falsifier_refs":["K-T06","A-T11","A-T16","WK-V43"],"enforcement":"enforcement-point-named","enforcement_basis":"The evaluator is a protected surface: activating a changed evaluator is a ProtectedChange requiring a reviewer and authorizer outside the improver's write authority, and the known-defect control is a declared acceptance obligation on the checker itself.","gap":null,"source":"research/attack-coverage.json#/cases/7"},{"id":"AC09","case":"duplicate actions","candidate_reviews":[{"artifact":"planning/reviews/D-technical.md","finding_ids":["T01","T03"],"kind":"reasoned attack or stated specification obligation; see report for limits"},{"artifact":"planning/reviews/D-architecture-evidence.md","finding_ids":["EAS-01"],"kind":"reasoned attack or stated specification obligation; see report for limits"}],"selected_architecture_response":{"architecture":"S1.0","selection":"planning/02-architecture-selection.md","risk_groups":["RISK-06","RISK-17"],"reviewed_repairs":["planning/reviews/D2-technical.md","planning/reviews/D2-architecture-evidence-company.md"]},"implementation_test":null,"status":"conceptual responses reviewed; concrete specification/conformance