docs/vision-system/planning/specification/10-components-authority-traceability.md:370:**SPECIFICATION.** Component evaluation entries CA-C01 through CA-C09 require useful valid progress alongside adverse cases. They feed the [complete construction graph](08-improvement-implementation.md#7-complete-dependency-ordered-construction-graph) and [G acceptance protocol](../reviews/G-acceptance-protocol.md). Test ownership must preserve the declared independent capture, expected-answer and evaluator boundaries. The author cannot select its own favorable independent verdict; source inspection, document checks, simulation, local process testing, independent host/admin rehearsal and actual human/provider performance remain separately labelled evidence.
docs/vision-system/planning/specification/05-work-agents-skills.md:7:**SPECIFICATION.** The [kernel](01-contract-kernel.md), [authority/recovery](02-authority-recovery.md), [company procedures](03-company-capabilities.md), [human operation](04-human-operation.md), [capability catalog](capabilities.json), and [knowledge/evaluation contract](06-knowledge-evidence-evaluation.md) form one specification. The [frozen G protocol](../reviews/G-acceptance-protocol.md) remains unchanged. **SOURCE CLAIM.** [L04](../../research/L04-engineering.md) and [L08](../../research/L08-reliability.md) support separating durable work from replaceable executors; **UNKNOWN:** their reported demonstrations do not establish our throughput or business value.
docs/vision-system/planning/specification/05-work-agents-skills.md:49:**DESIGN PROPOSAL — the middle band's terminus when no holder exists, and its deadline behaviour (F6A-01).** The two lowest classes park with an owner and the two highest refuse with a packet to a named human authority; only the middle band routed to a §12 holder, and §12 refuses to admit a holder for a duty class no frozen fixture exercises — so the ladder could name a recipient that does not exist. **Supplier insolvency during a paid pre-order is the case: it reaches the external-contact and economic classes, no admitted holder covers it, and the escalation had nowhere to land.** It lands here. **Where the duty class has no admitted standing holder, the escalation is routed to [`03-company-capabilities.md`](03-company-capabilities.md)'s ordered custody resolver** — promise sponsor, otherwise the service mandate, otherwise the designated maintenance/discovery custodian — and the resulting `ResponsibilityAssignment` records `custody_basis = maintenance_custodian` when it reaches that last tier. The terminus exists unconditionally because that tier has no further branch. **Custody is ownership, not authority.** `03`'s resolver *"assigns ownership, not new grants"*, so a custodian holding work that needs authority it does not have routes a decision packet to [`04-human-operation.md`](04-human-operation.md)'s `AuthorityMatrix`, exactly as the two highest classes do, and never acts above its class. **The deadline behaviour is `03`'s existing one and no new timer is created**: the escalation carries a latest responsible time; expiry activates the accepted alternate through the existing `alternate_assignment_ref`, `deadlines` and `expires_at` fields; a contested assignment is still custody and does not suspend it; and if custody is still unaccepted after the alternate's expiry, **admission in that duty class stops** by the computed predicate of R-D09 above and the unaccepted escalation is refused with a named failed predicate rather than left assigned and silent. That is the explicit awaiting-principal state with a deadline and a standing owner that §6's fourth silent-drop counter promises.
docs/vision-system/planning/specification/05-work-agents-skills.md:146:**SPECIFICATION — the closed `boundary_kind` set and the contested-refs field, new 2026-09-14 (F6X-02, closing the two clauses of F6B-02 the contracts lane could not derive).** `ConstraintSet.payload.boundary_kind` is a **closed set of exactly eight members**, one for each transfer the six frozen fixtures and this section name; **a transfer whose boundary kind is not a member is refused at the boundary, never defaulted**, which is what makes the field an assertion rather than a free string. **Fixture F-4's delivery to the checker is `acceptance_submission`, and F-4 introduces no ninth kind (F6W-08):** the artifact and its capability-owner-authored, version-frozen criteria crossing to the checker **is** the `declared_done → in_acceptance` crossing, and what F-4's blinding withholds — the producer's rationale, its preferred conclusion, the shared record and, under R-D11, criteria authored by the producing path — is withheld as **members the constraint set may not carry**, not as a different boundary. *Amended 2026-09-14 (F6W-08): the completeness claim — one member for each transfer the six frozen fixtures name — was demonstrated by rows citing fixtures 1, 2, 3, 5 and 6, and **fixture 4 appeared in no row and nowhere else in §5**. Because a transfer whose boundary kind is not a member is refused at the boundary rather than degrading quietly, the unnamed branch was a refusal waiting at the boundary of the fixture the round's verification dimension rests on, not a documentation gap. **No ninth member is added**: the eight are registered in the contracts, and the repair names which existing member covers F-4.* The members, each with what names it:
docs/vision-system/planning/specification/05-work-agents-skills.md:154:| `acceptance_submission` | `AcceptanceInterval` `declared_done → in_acceptance`, producing structure's sponsor to acceptance owner (§5); fixtures 1, 2 and 6, and **fixture 4** — the artifact and its owner-authored frozen criteria reaching the blinded checker (F6W-08) |
